Formulir Nomor I.WPB.1.A surat pernyataa:
Form No. I.WPB.1.A statement letter from the prospective WPB declaring that the prospective WPB:
a. is legally competent to perform legal acts;
b. has never committed a disgraceful act and/or been convicted of a proven criminal offense in the field of finance and/or Commodity Futures Trading;
c. is not included in the List of Suspected Terrorists and Terrorist Organizations;
d. is not included in the List of Weapons of Mass Destruction Proliferation Financing;
e. is of good character and morals;
f. is not currently under examination by Bappebti, under police investigation, or still a party against whom a Customer has filed a complaint.

Form No. I.WPB.1.A statement letter from the prospective WPB declaring that the prospective WPB:
a. is legally competent to perform legal acts;
b. has never committed a disgraceful act and/or been convicted of a proven criminal offense in the field of finance and/or Commodity Futures Trading;
c. is not included in the List of Suspected Terrorists and Terrorist Organizations;
d. is not included in the List of Weapons of Mass Destruction Proliferation Financing;
e. is of good character and morals;
f. is not currently under examination by Bappebti, under police investigation, or still a party against whom a Customer has filed a complaint.

Kegiatan ini mencakup jasa intermediasi:
This activity covers other intermediation services related to the transport of goods without operating transport vehicles of one's own, and not classified elsewhere.
This group also covers:
- booking of cargo space;
- handling of goods-shipment documents;
- issuance and procurement of transport documents and cargo charges;
- representation on behalf of the consignor, consignee, or logistics operator;
- freight-forwarding activities by sea and air cargo agents;
- operation of intermediary platforms for goods-transport services;
- activities of customs agents representing clients in customs procedures.
This group does not cover:
- arrangement and handling of goods shipment, see group 52311;
- brokerage of sea-going vessels and spacecraft, see group 46100;
- intermediation in booking passenger seats on ships or aircraft, see subclass 5232;
- underwriting of insurance for motor, marine, aviation, and transport risks, see 6512;
- the carriage of goods itself, see Divisions 49, 50, and 51.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- administrasi da:
This group covers:
- the administration and operation of government institutions dealing with foreign affairs and of diplomatic and consular missions stationed abroad or at the offices of international organizations;
- the administration, operation, and supporting activities for information and cultural services intended for dissemination beyond national borders;
- the provision of foreign aid, whether through international organizations or not;
- the provision of military aid to foreign countries;
- the management of foreign trade, international finance, and foreign technical relations.
This group does not cover:
- refugee services arising from international disasters or conflicts, see subclass 8890;
- activities of extraterritorial organizations and bodies, see subclass 9900.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- administrasi pu:
This group covers:
- public administration relating to environmental services programs;
- the administration of public policy relating to research and development and associated funds for the environment.
This group also covers:
- the administration of drinking-water supply programs;
- the administration of waste collection and disposal;
- the administration of environmental protection programs.
This group does not cover:
- waste disposal, refuse disposal, and remediation activities, see Divisions 37, 38, 39;
- the operation of nature reserves, see subclass 9142.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- aktivitas broke:
This group covers
- the activities of patent brokerage and marketing services, which among others arrange the purchase and sale of patent rights.
This group also covers
- administration/management services for copyrights and the revenue generated therefrom;
- administration/management services for industrial property rights (patent rights, licences, trademarks, franchises, and the like);
- the activities of collective rights administration/management institutions/organisations.
This subclass does not cover
- the leasing of intellectual property and similar products, see subclass 7740;
- the buying and selling of patents and similar intellectual property rights on own account, see subclass 7740.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- aktivitas konsu:
This group covers
- engineering consulting and design activities, which apply the laws of physics and engineering principles in the design of machines, materials, instruments, structures, processes, and systems, such as:
* machinery, and industrial processes;
* projects involving civil engineering, hydraulic engineering, traffic engineering;
* engineering advisory and consulting services;
* engineering services for the construction of residential and non-residential buildings;
* engineering services for civil-engineering water-resources works;
* engineering services for mechanical works in buildings, engineering services for sports-facility buildings;
* environmental engineering consulting services;
* construction-related consulting services for traffic-control system works;
* engineering services for the construction of transmission-network power plants, substations, and electric-power distribution;
* engineering services for industrial processes, production and production facilities, and other industrial-process engineering services;
* the extension and realization of projects related to electrical and electronic engineering, mining engineering, chemical engineering, mechanical engineering, industrial engineering, systems engineering, and safety engineering;
* water-resources management projects;
* project-management activities and field-investigation services related to construction;
- the activities of developing projects that use air conditioners (AC), refrigeration, sanitation, and pollution-control engineering, acoustic engineering, and others;
- geophysical, geological, geochemical survey activities, and seismic or earthquake surveys, including prospectus-preparation services and geological and geophysical interpretation services for the construction sector;
* geodetic survey activities covering boundary and land surveys, hydrological surveys;
- surveys of conditions above and below the ground surface;
- spatial-information and cartography activities;
- mapping activities and map-making services.
This group also covers
- engineering services for transportation civil-engineering works;
- technical facilitation services for public infrastructure and facilities in the construction sector.
This group does not cover
- architectural activities, see group 71101;
- design and consulting related to the planning, construction, demolition, and relocation of plants, see group 71102;
- technical testing, inspection, certification, verification, and validation, see subclass 7120;
- industrial design, see subclass 7411.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- aktivitas memua:
This group covers:
- loading and unloading of goods and luggage regardless of the mode of transport used;
- ship loading and unloading;
- loading and unloading of freight railway cars.
This group also covers:
- the provision of lifting and cargo-handling equipment with operators, such as cargo hoists and cranes;
- the movement of cargo at industrial sites, typically with transport equipment unsuitable for use on public roads.
This group does not cover:
- the transport or movement of objects within a factory under contract or by tariff, where public roads are used, see subclass 4923;
- the operation of cargo terminals and their supporting facilities, see subclasses 5221, 5222, and 5223.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- aktivitas organ:
This group covers:
- the activities of organizations whose members' interests center on the development and welfare of enterprises in a particular business or trade, including agriculture, or on the economic growth and climate of a specific geographic area or political subdivision regardless of line of business;
- the activities of federations of several associations;
- the activities of chambers of commerce and similar organizations;
- the dissemination of information, representation before government bodies, public relations, and labor negotiations on behalf of business and employers' organizations.
This group does not cover:
- the activities of trade unions, see subclass 9420;
- the activities of professional membership organizations, see subclass 9412;
- the activities of non-governmental organizations, see subclass 9499;
- the activities of international organizations of an administrative nature, see subclass 9900.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- aktivitas pemut:
This group covers
- the screening of films or other audiovisual works in cinemas, open-air venues, or other film-screening locations;
- the screening of films at film festival events, whether managed by the government or by private parties.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- aktivitas penci:
This group covers:
- the creation of conceptual artworks;
- choreography activities;
- the activities of fashion stylists and the creation of other artworks not yet covered in subclasses 9011-9012.
This group does not cover:
- furniture restoration (except museum-type restoration), see subclass 9524;
- restoration of stained glass, see group 913;
- renovation and restoration of historic buildings and sites, see Section F;
- the operation of various types of museums, see group 912;
- restoration of artworks, such as paintings, see subclass 9130;
- restoration of fabrics/textiles and embroidery, see subclass 9130;
- restoration of polychrome interiors, furnace-tile restoration, and decorative painting, see subclass 9130.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- aktivitas pener:
This group covers:
- the publishing of journals and other periodicals;
- the publishing of radio and television programming schedules.
All feasible forms of publishing journals and periodicals (whether in print, electronic, digital, analog, or other forms) are included in this group.
This group does not cover:
- the activities of independent journalists, see subclass 9011;
- the activities of independent press photographers, see subclass 7420;
- the production of television or video news programs, see subclass 5911.

This group covers:
- other publishing activities, whether in print, electronic, digital, analog, or other forms, of:
* directories, mailing lists, and telephone books;
* compilations, such as case law, pharmaceutical compendia, and the like;
* catalogues;
* photographs, engravings, and postcards;
* calendars;
* forms;
* posters;
* reproductions of artworks;
* unbound leaflets and advertising material;
* statistics and other information;
* datasets or databases without associated data-processing services.
This group does not cover:
- the retail trade of software on physical media, see subclass 4740;
- the publishing of advertising newspapers, see subclass 5812;
- the production of films, videos, and television programs, see subclass 5911;
- software publishing activities, see group 582;
- the activities of social-networking sites, blogs, and wikis, and of online gaming or video-game sites, see subclass 6039;
- application hosting services, see subclass 6310;
- the activities of web search portals and the compilation of information or directories on a fee or contract basis, see subclass 6390.

This group covers
- the activities of translation and interpretation of various languages, including sign language, both spoken and written;
- the activities of translation from a source language into a target language, including the parameters of terminological equivalence, sense of language, culture, and others.
This subclass does not cover
- the development of translation tools and the training of translation machines, see group 621;
- the publishing of translation software, see subclass 5829;
- language teaching activities, see subclass 8559.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- aktivitas penga:
This group covers:
- sampling activities to determine the characteristics of materials or processes;
- calibration/metrology activities in the measurement of temperature, mass, volume, pressure, force, torque, flow, hardness, density, length, electricity, magnetism, time, frequency, acoustics, vibration, photometry, radiometry, and Ionizing Radiation Analytical Instruments;
- testing comprising physical, mechanical, chemical, biological, microbiological, electrical, nuclear, visual/checklist, model/prototype design, forensic, or other analyses of various types of substances/materials/products in the fields of industry, trade, energy and mineral resources, construction, transport, telecommunications, pharmaceuticals, food, agriculture, forestry, or environment (water, air, and soil quality and other environmental indicators);
- conformity assessment of physical characteristics, composition, and performance;
- the periodic operation of laboratories;
- periodic testing or calibration of medical equipment;
- quarantine testing of animals, plants, and fisheries;
- marine testing;
- testing of ionizing-radiation machines and equipment, such as survey meters, contamination meters, dosimeters, and X-ray multimeters;
- calibration of industrial instruments, such as machinery, equipment, and industrial measuring instruments;
- testing of electronics and other technologies.
This group also covers:
- calibration/metrology and stamping/verification activities to check/test a measuring instrument or calibration device so that the instrument is deemed valid.
This group does not cover:
- calibration/metrology activities for repairing measuring, gauging, and weighing instruments and legal-metrology equipment so that they meet technical requirements, see group 33131;
- testing of animal specimens for sanitary reasons unrelated to food production, see subclass 7500;
- diagnostic imaging and the testing and analysis of medical and dental specimens, see Division 86;
- testing in medical laboratories, see subclass 8699;
- sampling and weighing within goods-handling activities, see subclass 5229;
- penetration testing of computer systems, ethical hacking, and cybersecurity, see Division 62;
- DNA sequencing for general research on biological processes, see subclass 7210;
- DNA sequencing for the diagnosis or treatment of specific diseases, see subclass 8699.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- aktivitas pengo:
This group covers:
- the activity of operating natural baths or sites and facilities for bathing that make use of hot springs and/or waterfalls as the principal business, such as Ciater Natural Baths (West Java), Umbul Ponggok Klaten Natural Baths (Central Java), and Soa Natural Baths (NTT);
- the activity of managing cave tourism, or caving adventure and exploration activities, as the principal activity in a particular area, which may be complemented by the provision of guides;
- the activity of managing tourism that involves exploration or travel entailing risk and requiring special skills and physical exertion, such as paragliding, paramotoring, hang gliding, bungee jumping, gliding, canyoning, orienteering, off-roading, and mountain biking.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- aktivitas penul:
This group covers:
- writing and editing activities carried out by individual authors, for various types of writing/topics, whether on their own behalf or on behalf of others, whether fiction or non-fiction, whether in print or digital, such as short stories and novels;
- scriptwriting activities, such as scripts for films, television, radio, computer games, and animation;
- the activities of independent bloggers;
- technical writing activities.
This group also covers the activities of poets and the creation of other similar literary works.
This group does not cover:
- the production, reproduction, and distribution of books and music, see Section J;
- translators for book editing, see group 743;
- the activities of independent musicians and actors in various types of video and audiovisual content, see subclass 9020.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- aktivitas yang:
This group covers:
- activities relating to the assessment and measures for preventive conservation, conservation, and curative restoration, including consultancy that takes into account the tangible and intangible significance of cultural heritage and sustainability. For each type of material and surface, these activities cover movable and immovable archaeological assets, leather, archival documents, graphic and printed documents and wooden panels, art objects, ceramic tiles, goldsmithing, canvas paintings, mural paintings, photography, sculpture, textiles including embroidery, stained glass, and scientific and industrial objects;
- activities relating to the digitization of cultural heritage (both movable and immovable), data collection, collection management, virtual replicas, and other activities through digital means to ensure the preservation of cultural heritage.
This group does not cover:
- the restoration of organs and other historic musical instruments, see subclass 3319;
- the renovation and restoration of historic sites and buildings, see Section F;
- architectural activities relating to the rehabilitation and restoration of cultural-heritage property, see subclass 7110;
- conservation science (research and development directed at cultural heritage), see Division 72;
- archaeological excavation, see group 722;
- services such as the restoration of artworks and museum collection objects and the preventive conservation of artworks carried out in-house by units classified in group 912, see group 912;
- furniture restoration (except museum-type restoration), see subclass 9524;
- the repair of musical instruments (except organs and historic instruments), see subclass 9529.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- ekstraksi dan p:
This group covers:
- the extraction and digging of peat;
- the agglomeration of peat;
- the preparation of peat to improve quality or to facilitate transport or storage.
Such extraction operations comprise digging, crushing, washing, screening, and storage.
This group does not cover:
- support services for peat digging, see subclass 0990;
- the manufacture of briquettes from peat, see subclass 1920;
- the manufacture of soil mixtures for growing media, e.g., from peat, natural soil, sand, clay, and mineral fertilizers, see subclass 2012;
- the manufacture of articles made of peat, see subclass 2399.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- ekstraksi garam:
This group covers
- extraction of table salt from underground, including by dissolution and pumping;
- production of table salt by evaporation of sea water or other brines, for example in salt pans or ponds;
- crushing, separation and refining of table salt by salt farmers.
This group does not cover
- processing of salt into culinary salt, such as iodized salt, see group 10772;
- production of drinking water by evaporation of brine, see subgroup 3600.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- jasa penunjang:
This group covers
- support services on a fee or contract basis required in mining activities under divisions 05, 07 and 08:
* exploration services, for example by traditional methods such as taking ore samples and making geological observations at prospective mining sites;
* pumping and dewatering services for mining output on a fee or contract basis;
* test excavation and the drilling of mining wells or fields;
- agglomeration and concentration of iron ore performed by third parties;
- securing of mine shafts and tunnels;
- demolition of building structures and dismantling of components or equipment at underground mining facilities.
This group does not cover
- operation of mines or quarries on a fee or contract basis, see divisions 05, 07 and 08;
- specialised repair of mining machinery, see subgroup 3312;
- geophysical survey services on a fee or contract basis, see subgroup 7110.

This group covers
- incidental support services for fish capture and aquaculture activities, both at sea and in fresh water, such as feeding services, harvesting services, auction-preparation services, sorting and grading services, and quality-testing services;
- handling and preservation of caught or farmed fish prior to sale, such as chilling services to maintain freshness;
- protection of fish from predators;
- fisheries control and fish guarding;
- marine ecosystem restoration activities.
This group does not cover
- processing of fish and aquaculture products on factory ships or in onshore plants, see group 102;
- processing of fish, crustaceans and molluscs, see group 102;
- distribution of fishery and aquaculture products, see divisions 46, 47 or 52;
- fishing activities carried out for sport or recreation and related services, see subgroup 9319;
- operation of sport fishing facilities, see subgroup 9319.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- jasa perantara:
This group covers
- aviation intermediary services acting on behalf of an air operator to obtain flight approval from the authorities competent in civil or military aviation, comprising
* arranging overflight permits;
* landing permits;
* airport time slots;
* various other operational clearances;
- intermediary services for administrative and representative arrangements related to flight approval.
This group does not cover
- operation of aircraft with an operator, see subgroups 5110 and 5120.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- kegiatan fotogr:
This group covers:
- photography or picture-taking activities, whether for individuals or for business purposes, such as:
* photography for passports, schools, weddings, and the like;
* photography for commercial, publication, fashion, real estate, or tourism purposes;
* underwater photography and video recording for events, such as weddings and meetings.
- the processing and printing of photographic output, including:
* developing, printing, and enlarging from negatives or cine-film supplied by the client;
* film-developing and photo-printing laboratories;
* one-hour photo shops (photo developing outlets, not part of a camera store);
* slide mounting and the duplication, restoration, or minor retouching of transparencies in connection with photography;
- photojournalism activities and the production of microfilm from documents;
- 3D object scanning;
- the processing and conversion of photographs into digital format and uploading them to the cloud.
This group does not cover:
- the production of films for cinema and video and their distribution, see division 591.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- kegiatan jasa k:
This group covers
- forestry service activities, such as forest inventory, forest-management consulting services, timber appraisal, forest fire prevention, forest pest control, and the rental of forestry equipment and machinery with operator;
- timber harvesting service activities, such as the transport of logs within the forest associated with timber harvesting.
This group does not cover
- propagation of forest tree seedlings, see subgroup 0210;
- drainage of forestry land, see subgroup 4312;
- clearing of construction sites, see subgroup 4312;
- water management in forest areas, see subgroup 3600;
- geothermal energy exploitation in forest areas, see group 06202;
- carbon capture and storage activities, see subgroup 3900;
- activities of botanical gardens, zoos and nature reserves, see group 914;
- generation of solar and wind power in forests, see subgroup 3511.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- kegiatan jasa p:
This group covers
- oil and gas extraction service activities on a fee or contract basis, such as:
* exploration services in connection with oil or gas extraction by traditional methods, for example making geological observations in prospective mining areas;
* drilling and re-drilling; rig installation at mining sites; repair and dismantling; cementing of oil and gas wells; well lining; well plugging and abandonment;
* liquefaction and regasification of natural gas for transport purposes, performed at the mining site;
* pumping and conveyance services for mines on a fee or contract basis;
* test drilling in connection with petroleum and gas extraction.
This group also covers
- oil and gas field firefighting services.
This subgroup does not cover
- operator services at oil and gas fields, see subgroups 0610, 0620;
- specialised repair and maintenance of drilling and mining machinery and equipment, see subgroup 3312;
- specialised offshore installation, and repair and maintenance of equipment that forms an integral part of floating platforms, see division 43;
- liquefaction and regasification of natural gas for transport purposes, performed away from the mining site, see subgroup 5221;
- geophysical survey services on a fee or contract basis, see subgroup 7110.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- kegiatan lembag:
This group covers
- the activities of rent-collecting agencies;
- the management of non-residential real estate, for example the management of non-residential real estate property held in joint ownership (mostly carried out on a fee or contract basis);
- consultancy activities on a fee or contract basis in connection with the buying, selling, and renting of real estate, as well as other real estate provision activities on a fee or contract basis.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- kegiatan operas:
This group covers
- operation of botanical gardens and zoos, including children's zoos where children may interact directly with animals;
- operation of ex-situ conservation areas (outside natural habitats) for the breeding and/or rescue of flora and fauna while preserving species purity, used as places for education, exhibition and research and for the advancement of science and for recreational purposes, such as wildlife parks, special wildlife parks, special wildlife training centres, botanical gardens, herbaria, and special plant gardens;
- operation of aquariums.
This subgroup does not cover
- gardening and landscaping activities, see subgroup 8130;
- operation of sport fishing and hunting in wildlife sanctuaries and nature reserves, see subgroup 9319.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- kegiatan organi:
This group covers
- activities of organisations not directly affiliated with a political party that pursue community causes or issues through public education, political influence, fundraising and the like, such as non-governmental organisations (NGOs/LSM), the Indonesian National Youth Committee (KNPI), the Indonesian Women's Congress (KOWANI), protest movements or citizen initiatives (demonstrations); ecological and environmental movements; organisations supporting public facilities and educational facilities not elsewhere classified; organisations for the protection and advancement of special groups, such as ethnic and minority groups; and associations for patriotic purposes including war-veteran associations;
- consumer associations;
- automobile associations;
- associations for social-acquaintance purposes such as Rotary clubs and the like;
- youth associations, teenage associations, student associations, fraternal clubs and groups and the like;
- activities of associations aimed at improving health;
- activities of animal-protection associations;
- associations for the pursuit of cultural or recreational activities or hobbies (other than sports and games) such as poetry, literature, book clubs, history clubs, gardening clubs, photography clubs, music and arts clubs, collectors' and craft clubs, social clubs, carnival clubs and the like.
This group also covers
- granting of assistance by membership or other organisations;
- activities of non-governmental organisations, for example to protect the interests and rights of citizens;
- philanthropic intermediation and the promotion of volunteering;
- international cooperation and solidarity activities.
This group does not cover
- activities of professional artists' organisations or groups, see division 90;
- activities of sports clubs, see subgroup 9312;
- activities of professional associations, see subgroup 9412;
- activities of sports federations and associations, see subgroup 9319;
- activities of international organisations established under international treaties between states, see subgroup 9900.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- kegiatan pembua:
This group covers
- the manufacture of ready-to-drink distilled alcoholic beverages, whether by modern or traditional methods, for example whisky, brandy, gin, vodka, tequila, arak, genever, soju, liqueurs, and "mixed beverages";
- the blending of distilled alcoholic beverages or the process of mixing alcoholic-beverage raw materials to achieve the desired ethanol content;
- the production of neutral alcoholic beverages (without flavour).
This group does not cover
- the manufacture of alcohol without distillation, see subclasses 1102 and 1103;
- the manufacture of synthetic ethyl alcohol, see subclass 2011;
- the manufacture of ethyl alcohol from fermented materials, see subclass 2011;
- bottling and labelling, see subclass 4633 (if the packaging is carried out as part of wholesale trade activities) or subclass 8292 (if the packaging is carried out on a fee or contract basis).

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- kegiatan pengol:
This group covers
- processing of gaseous fuels that can be used directly as fuel, where production is accompanied by gas-quality improvement such as purification, blending and other processes, produced from natural gas, including liquefied petroleum gas (LPG); carbonisation and gasification of coal; or other gases;
- production of hydrogen gas fuel produced by electrolysis, photolysis, thermochemical, biological, geological and other methods, using new and renewable energy sources or fossil energy sources;
- processing of biogas fuel produced from by-products of agriculture, plantations, livestock farming, or waste, where production is accompanied by gas-quality improvement such as purification, blending and other processes.

This group covers
- processing and preservation of meat and meat products by canning, smoking, salting, freezing, sweetening, irradiation (by irradiator) and the like;
- production of frozen meat in carcass form;
- production of frozen meat in cut form;
- production of frozen meat in individual portions;
- production of dried, salted or smoked meat;
- production of meat products such as sausages, salami, puddings, "andouillettes", saveloy, bologna, pâtés, rillettes, meatballs and ham;
- processing of whale meat on land or on specialised vessels.
This group does not cover
- preparation of ready-to-eat meals from meat and poultry, see group 10750;
- preparation of soups containing meat, see group 10799.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- kegiatan penyed:
This group covers
- the provision of visual-communication-design/graphic-design services, whether produced manually or digitally, whether static (non-moving) or dynamic (moving, interactive), on print media or screens (devices, TV, computers, LED screens, and the like), whether offline, online, or virtual, relating to the creation of materials with identification, information, and persuasion functions implemented in brand identity, logos, advertising design, infographics, and stationery;
- the creation of communication designs (in the form of posters, brochures, books, or other printed materials) for profiles, websites, applications, social media, report materials, presentations, and other promotional material designs;
- packaging design, particularly the design of packaging surfaces;
- environmental graphic design for exhibition/event boards, product displays, billboards, wayfinding, signage, building/retail markers, and so on.
This group also covers the design of brand visual identity, including research, the formulation of brand strategy, through to the visual design of the logo/identity, the preparation of standardization guidelines for the use of the brand's visual identity/logo, the provision of lettering services, typeface design, and the creation of illustrations.
This group does not cover
- computer-based graphic-design activities for animation, see subclass 5912;
- the creation of fine-art works, whether digital or non-digital, see group 90120.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- kegiatan perbur:
This group covers
- hunting and trapping of animals for commercial purposes;
- capture of wildlife (dead or alive) for food, or for their fur and skins, for population control, or for use in research, for placement in zoos or as pets;
- production of animal fur, reptile skins or bird skins from hunting or trapping activities;
- catching of frogs and toads in the wild;
- collection of snails in the wild;
- catching of marine mammals such as dugongs, sea lions and seals carried out on land;
- hunting of foxes, mink and wolves to protect livestock; hunting for animal population control;
- production of mammal horns and reptile or other animal organs from hunting and trapping activities.
This group does not cover
- production of animal fur, reptile or bird skins from animal husbandry, see subgroup 0149;
- raising of game animals on farms, see subgroup 0149; control of pests (including rabbits) related to agricultural activities, see subgroup 0161;
- whale catching, see subgroup 0311;
- production of hides from slaughterhouses, see subgroup 1011;
- hunting for sport or recreation and related service activities, see subgroup 9319;
- activities of organisations supporting hunting and trapping, see subgroup 9499.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- kegiatan sekola:
This group covers
- driving-school activities for private (non-commercial) drivers;
- educational activities provided by aviation, maritime and shipping schools that do not issue commercial certificates or licences.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- layanan investi:
This group covers
- investigation services in the private, commercial, insurance and legal fields;
- guarding, patrol or security services;
- support services for cash collection and storage services;
- secure data destruction and disposal services;
- armoured-car services.
This group also covers
- guarding and security service activities, for example for shops and trauma centres;
- screening of luggage and passengers at airports, railway stations and similar places;
- activities of security personnel for events, concerts, fairs and exhibitions.
This group does not cover
- risk analysis, security advice and consulting, see subgroup 8019;
- safety services of concierges, receptionists and doormen, see subgroups 8110, 8210;
- security including cybersecurity training, see subgroup 8559;
- remote monitoring activities, see subgroup 8019;
- public order and safety activities, see subgroup 8423.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pelayanan navig:
This group covers
- navigation, shipping and berthing services;
- transfer of cargo between large and small vessels;
- lighthouse activities;
- operation of waterways and the like;
- operation of floating production, storage and offloading (FPSO) and floating, storage and offloading (FSO) vessels;
- vessel cargo survey activities;
- river-route information services;
- vessel storage during winter.
This group also covers
- maintenance work on waterway infrastructure.
This group does not cover
- construction and dredging of waterways, see subgroup 4291;
- construction of underwater cables or underwater pipelines, see groups 422, 429;
- cargo handling, see group 52240;
- operation of marinas (tourist or recreational docks), see subgroup 9329;
- ship-crew recruitment service activities, see subgroup 7810.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pelayanan tekni:
This group covers
- technical and operational services to support the ground operation of aircraft for passengers and cargo (ground handling), including refuelling, water uplift, waste handling and aircraft towing;
- passenger services at airports, such as check-in, boarding and transit processes;
- handling of baggage, cargo and mail, for both loading and unloading;
- inspection of cargo and/or container loads using ionising radiation sources (radioactive substances and ionising-radiation generators).
This group also covers
- documentation, weighing, security and special-handling services for dangerous or high-value goods.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pembelian, penj:
This group covers:
- the purchase and sale of residential buildings, such as apartment buildings and dwellings;
- the development of houses, flats, or apartments, with or without furnishings, for more permanent, year-round use;
- the development of residential mobile-home sites for primary residence;
- the development of residential building projects for sale.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pembersihan eks:
This group covers
- exterior cleaning of all types of buildings, including offices, factories, shops, institutions and other business and professional premises and residential or multi-unit housing buildings;
- specialised cleaning of buildings, such as cleaning of windows, chimneys and furnaces or fireplaces, stoves, incinerators, refuse burners, boilers or kettles, pipes or ventilation ducts, and flues or vents;
- swimming-pool cleaning and maintenance services;
- cleaning of industrial machinery;
- bottle washing;
- cleaning of trains, buses, aircraft and the like;
- cleaning of the interiors of ships and tanker trucks;
- control of disease vectors, disease-carrying animals and household pests;
- street cleaning and snow and ice removal;
- other building and industrial cleaning activities;
- post-construction cleaning of new buildings;
- steam cleaning, sand blasting and similar activities for building exteriors.
This group does not cover
- agricultural pest control, see subgroup 0161;
- cleaning of sewage or water drains, see subgroup 3702;
- car washing and vehicle cleaning, see subgroup 9531.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pembuatan alat:
This group covers
- manufacture of voltage regulators;
- manufacture of electric circuit breakers;
- manufacture of surge suppressors for distribution voltage levels;
- manufacture of control panels for electric power distribution and switchgear and their components or parts, such as automatic control panels, lighting distribution boards, circuit breakers and control desks, and enclosed switch assemblies;
- manufacture of electrical relays;
- manufacture of conduits or ducts for electric-current switchboard equipment;
- manufacture of electrical fuses;
- power-switching equipment;
- manufacture of electric power switches (except push-button, snap, solenoid and tumbler) and kWh meters.
This subgroup does not cover
- manufacture of electrical components such as transformers and switches, see subgroup 2619;
- manufacture of environmental-control and industrial-process-control equipment, see subgroup 2651;
- manufacture of plugs for electrical circuits such as push-buttons and snap switches, see subgroup 2733;
- manufacture of electric soldering and welding equipment, see subgroup 2790;
- manufacture of solid-state inverters, rectifiers and converters, see subgroup 2790;
- manufacture of turbine generator sets, see subgroup 2811;
- manufacture of starter motors and generators for internal combustion engines, see subgroup 2930.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pembuatan arloj:
This group covers
- manufacture of watches and all types of clocks, such as wristwatches, pocket watches, pendant watches, wall clocks, alarm clocks and bells, including clock-panel devices and clocks containing radioactive substances.
This group also covers
- manufacture of parts of clocks/watches, such as movement parts, jewels, dials, plates, hands, bridges, springs, clock plates, hands and other parts;
- manufacture of watch and clock cases, including cases of precious metal;
- manufacture of outer protective casings for clocks of various materials;
- manufacture of time-recording equipment and equipment for measuring, recording and displaying time intervals driven by a clock or watch movement or a synchronous motor, such as alarms for watches, instrument panel clocks, chronometers, stopwatches, parking meters, employee time clocks (attendance time recorders), time/date stamps and process time recorders;
- manufacture of time switches and other outputs driven by a watch or clock movement or by a synchronous motor, such as time locks.
This group does not cover
- manufacture of non-metal watch straps (fabric, leather, plastic), see subgroup 1512;
- manufacture of smart watches, see subgroup 2639;
- manufacture of watch straps of precious metal, see subgroup 3211;
- manufacture of watch straps of non-precious metal, see subgroup 3212.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pembuatan asam:
This group covers
- manufacture of inorganic acids, such as hydrochloric acid and carbonic acid;
- manufacture of inorganic bases, such as sodium hydroxide (caustic soda), potassium hydroxide and lithium hydroxide;
- manufacture of inorganic salts formed from the reaction of acids and bases, such as sodium chloride, sodium carbonate (soda ash) and potassium chloride;
- manufacture of acid oxides, basic oxides and salt oxides that do not function as pigments.
This group does not cover
- manufacture of iodized table salt and industrial salt for various foods, see groups 10772, 10773;
- manufacture of pharmaceutical salts, see subgroup 2101;
- manufacture of ammonia, see group 20121.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pembuatan atau:
This group covers
- manufacture or assembly of electric, diesel, steam and other railway locomotives;
- manufacture of self-propelled railway carriages or electric railcars, or trams, vans and trucks;
- manufacture of railway or electric-railway carriage maintenance or service vehicles;
- manufacture of railway or electric-railway carriages that are not self-propelled, such as passenger carriages, goods wagons, tank wagons, workshop wagons, crane wagons, dump wagons and trains, and carts;
- manufacture of specialised parts for railways or electric railways or carriages, such as bogies, axles, axle boxes and wheels, brakes and brake parts, coupling and hook equipment, buffers and buffer parts, shock absorbers, locomotive and carriage frames; bodies/coachwork, inter-corridor connectors and the like.
This group also covers
- manufacture of mechanical and electromagnetic signalling equipment, safety equipment and signal-control equipment for railways, electric railways, water traffic, highways, parking facilities, airfields and the like;
- manufacture of mine locomotives and mining railway wagons;
- manufacture of railway transport simulators.
This group does not cover
- manufacture of unmounted rails, see subgroup 2410;
- manufacture of installed railway track fittings or electric-railway track, see subgroup 2599;
- manufacture of electric motors not for electric vehicles, see subgroup 2711;
- manufacture of electrical signalling, safety or signal-control equipment for railways or electric railways, see subgroup 2790;
- manufacture of engines and turbines, except for motor vehicles, aircraft and motorcycle propulsion engines, see subgroup 2811.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pembuatan bola:
This group covers
- manufacture of ball and roller bearings, including balls, rollers, rings and other parts of bearings;
- manufacture of gears, gearing, gear boxes and other speed changers;
- manufacture of clutches and clutch shafts;
- manufacture of flywheels and pulleys;
- manufacture of articulated link chain;
- manufacture of power transmission chains (timing chains).
This group also covers
- manufacture of components and spare parts for mechanical transmission equipment, including camshafts, crankshafts, cranks, plain shaft bearing housings, gears, gearing, bearing blocks, clutches and clutch shafts, flywheels and pulleys, articulated link chain, power transmission chains (timing chains) and the like.
This group does not cover
- manufacture of other chains, see subgroup 2595;
- manufacture of hydraulic transmission equipment, see subgroup 2812;
- manufacture of hydrostatic transmissions, see subgroup 2812;
- manufacture of clutches for motor vehicles, see subgroup 2930;
- manufacture of gears, gear boxes and the like for motor vehicles, see subgroup 2930;
- manufacture of power-transmission subassemblies suitable for use or principally with engines as part of vehicles or aircraft, see divisions 29 and 30.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pembuatan gener:
This group covers
- manufacture of steam generators or other steam-raising boilers, including their components and accessories;
- manufacture of radiators for non-electric central heating systems;
- manufacture of condensers for steam-power generating units;
- manufacture of auxiliary installations used with steam generators, such as condensers, superheaters, steam collectors and accumulators;
- manufacture of marine boilers or power boilers;
- manufacture of nuclear reactors together with their components and accessories, except isotope separators.
This group does not cover
- manufacture of electric ovens and electric water heaters, see subgroup 2751;
- manufacture of turbine boiler sets, see subgroup 2811;
- manufacture of household heating equipment, see subgroup 2815;
- manufacture of isotope separators, see subgroup 2829.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pembuatan kabel:
This group covers
- manufacture of insulated cables and wire of steel, copper or aluminium, such as electrical cables and telecommunication cables;
- manufacture of computer cables, printer cables and USB cables not fitted with connectors.
This group does not cover
- drawing of steel or other metal wire without insulation, see subgroups 2410 and 2420;
- manufacture of electrical cables fitted with insulated wire and connectors, see subgroup 2790;
- manufacture of cable harnesses for automotive devices, see subgroup 2930.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pembuatan kenda:
This group covers
- manufacture of hand-propelled vehicles, such as goods trucks, handcarts, sledges, shopping trolleys, pushcarts, wheelbarrows and carts, including other multipurpose tools;
- manufacture of animal-drawn vehicles, such as horse carriages (delman), lorries, sulkies, donkey-drawn carts and hearses (biers).
This group does not cover
- manufacture of works trucks, whether or not fitted with lifting or handling equipment, whether or not self-propelled, or used in industry or factories (including hand trucks and barrows), see subgroup 2816;
- manufacture of decorative restaurant trolleys, such as dessert trolleys and food trolleys, see subgroups 3101, 3102.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pembuatan kompr:
This group covers
- manufacture of air and gas compressors, compressors for refrigerators and air conditioners, compressors for motor vehicles, laboratory pumps, water pumps, air pumps, vacuum pumps or air pumps, other air and gas compressors, pumps for liquids whether or not fitted with a measuring device, pumps designed for internal combustion engines, such as fuel, oil and water pumps for motor vehicles and the like.
This group also covers
- manufacture of vacuum pumps or air pumps, and other air and gas compressors;
- manufacture of pumps for liquids, whether or not fitted with a measuring device;
- manufacture of pumps designed for internal combustion engines, such as fuel, oil and water pumps for motor vehicles and the like;
- manufacture of valves and taps for industrial use, including regulating valves and inlet-pipe taps;
- manufacture of taps and valves for sanitary use;
- manufacture of taps and valves for heating;
- manufacture of hand pumps.
This group does not cover
- manufacture of valves of unhardened vulcanised rubber, valves of glass, or valves of ceramics, see subgroups 2219, 2312 or 2393;
- manufacture of inlet and exhaust valves of internal combustion engines, see subgroup 2811;
- manufacture of hydraulic transmission equipment, see subgroup 2812.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pembuatan kotak:
This group covers
- manufacture of packing cases, boxes, wooden crates, wooden drums and similar packaging of wood;
- manufacture of pallets, pallet boxes and other loading boards of wood;
- manufacture of barrels, casks, buckets and other wooden products;
- manufacture of wooden cable reels.
This group does not cover
- manufacture of luggage, see subgroup 1512;
- manufacture of containers of plaited materials, see subgroup 1629.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pembuatan mesin:
This group covers
- manufacture of hand- or power-operated lifting, handling, loading and unloading machinery, such as block-and-tackle hoists, winches, capstans and jacks; derricks, cranes, mobile lifting frames, straddle carriers and the like; works trucks, whether or not fitted with handling and lifting equipment, whether or not self-propelled, and works trucks used in factories (including hand trucks and barrows); mechanical manipulators and robots specially designed for handling, lifting, loading and unloading; mechanical manipulators and industrial robots specially designed for lifting, handling, loading or unloading;
- manufacture of driverless forklifts and robots, and pallet load/unloaders;
- manufacture of goods-lifting and conveying equipment (conveyors) and the like;
- manufacture of lifts, escalators and pedestrian movers (moving walkways);
- manufacture of parts suitable for lifting and handling equipment.
This group also covers
- manufacture of automated handling equipment and lifting equipment for warehouses.
This group does not cover
- manufacture of machinery for vertical farming, see subgroup 2821;
- manufacture of continuous-action goods elevators and conveyors for underground use, see subgroup 2824;
- manufacture of mechanical shovels, excavators and shovel loaders, see subgroup 2824;
- manufacture of industrial robots for multiple uses, see subgroup 2829;
- manufacture of truck cranes, railway wagon cranes and floating cranes, see subgroups 2910, 3011, 3020;
- installation of lifts and elevators, see 4329.

This group covers
- manufacture of hydraulic machinery and components and hydraulic and pneumatic power engines, including hydraulic and pneumatic pumps, cylinders and valves;
- manufacture of air-processing equipment used in pneumatic systems;
- manufacture of hydraulic liquid- and gas-fluid power systems;
- manufacture of hydraulic transmission equipment;
- manufacture of electric linear actuators;
- manufacture of gas-spring cylinders.
This subgroup does not cover
- manufacture of hydraulic or pneumatic tubes, rubber hydraulic or pneumatic pipes and hoses, see subgroup 2211;
- manufacture of hydraulic or pneumatic tubes, and plastic pipes and hoses, see subgroup 2220;
- manufacture of compressors, see subgroup 2813;
- manufacture of pumps other than hydraulic fluid-power pumps, see subgroup 2813;
- manufacture of mechanical transmission equipment such as hydrostatic and hydromechanical equipment, see subgroup 2814.

This group covers
- the manufacture of machinery and equipment for hot metalworking, such as converters, ingot moulds, ladles and casting machines used in metallurgy or metal foundries;
- the manufacture of metal-rolling mills and rolls for such rolling mills.
This group also covers
- the manufacture of metal-rolling machinery, whether hot or cold.
This group does not cover
- the manufacture of draw benches, see subgroup 2822;
- the manufacture of moulding boxes and various moulds (except ingot moulds), see subgroup 2593;
- the manufacture of machinery for forming casting moulds, see subgroup 2829.

This group covers
- the manufacture of dryers for agricultural products;
- the manufacture of machinery for the dairy products industry, such as cream separators, milk-processing machines (e.g. homogenizers), milk-transforming machines (e.g. butter-making and moulding machines) and cheese-making machines (e.g. homogenizers, moulding, pressing);
- the manufacture of machinery for the rice or grain milling industry, such as machines for cleaning, sorting or grading paddy seed or grain and dried leguminous vegetables (winnowing machines, sifting belts, separators, grain-brushing machines and others); and machines for producing flour and foodstuffs and the like (grain-milling machines, sifters, flour sieves, fillers, blenders, paddy huskers, rice mills, pea splitters and others);
- the manufacture of presses and crushers and the like, such as those used to make wine, cider and fruit juice;
- the manufacture of machinery for the bakery products industry or for making macaroni, spaghetti and the like, such as bakery ovens, mixers, dough-makers, moulds, cutters and bread-making machines;
- the manufacture of machinery and equipment for processing various foods, such as machines for making confectionery, cocoa or chocolate, machines for sugar manufacture, machines for brewing, machines for processing meat and poultry, machines for processing fruit, nuts and vegetables, machines for processing fish, shellfish and other seafood; machines for distilling and refining; and other machinery for processing food and beverages;
- the manufacture of machinery for the extraction and processing of animal and vegetable oils and fats;
- the manufacture of machinery for processing tobacco and for making cigarettes and cigars or for pipe tobacco, chewing tobacco or snuff;
- the manufacture of machinery and equipment for cooking and warming food in hotels and restaurants.
This group does not cover
- the manufacture of milk and food irradiation equipment, see group 267;
- the manufacture of packing, wrapping and weighing machines, see subgroup 2819;
- the manufacture of machines for cleaning, sorting or grading eggs, fruit or other agricultural produce (except paddy seed and dried leguminous vegetables), see subgroup 2821.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pembuatan minum:
This group covers
- the manufacture of non-alcoholic beverages, except non-alcoholic beer and wine;
- the manufacture of flavoured and/or sweetened non-alcoholic soft drinks, such as lemonade, orangeade, cola, fruit-flavoured drinks, milk-flavoured drinks, coffee-flavoured drinks, tea-flavoured drinks, and tonic water;
- the manufacture of other non-alcoholic beverages, such as soy-based beverages;
- the manufacture of beverages from fruit nectar;
- the manufacture of powdered soft drinks.
This group does not cover
- the manufacture of fruit and vegetable juices, see group 10306;
- the manufacture of milk-based beverages, see subclass 1050;
- the manufacture of tea, coffee, and mate products, see subclass 1076;
- the manufacture of alcoholic beverages, see subclasses 1101 to 1103;
- the manufacture of non-alcoholic wine, see group 11020;
- the manufacture of non-alcoholic beer, see group 11030;
- the manufacture of ice for consumption, see group 35302;
- bottling and labelling, see subclass 4633 (if the packaging is carried out as part of a wholesale trade activity) or subclass 8292 (if the packaging is carried out on a fee or contract basis).

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pembuatan pasta:
This group covers
- the manufacture of pasta, such as macaroni, noodles, spaghetti, rice vermicelli and mung-bean vermicelli, whether cooked or not;
- the manufacture of semolina (couscous) and rice analogues.
This group does not cover
- the manufacture of prepared foods based on pasta or couscous, see subgroup 1075;
- the manufacture of soups containing pasta, see subgroup 1079.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pembuatan peral:
This group covers
- the manufacture of household electrical appliances, such as refrigerators, dishwashers, washing machines and clothes dryers, vacuum cleaners, floor polishers, electric waste bins, electric appliances for processing and preparing food (grinders, blenders, can openers, juicers and so on), electric toothbrushes, electric shavers and other electric personal-care appliances, electric knife sharpeners, and ventilation hoods.
This group does not cover
- the manufacture of commercial refrigerators and freezers, air conditioners, attic fans, permanent space heaters, commercial ventilation/exhaust fans, commercial cooking equipment, commercial laundry and dry-cleaning equipment, commercial vacuum cleaners and the like for commercial purposes, see division 28;
- the manufacture of sewing machines, whether for household use or not, see group 28262;
- the installation of central or built-in vacuum-cleaning systems, see subgroup 4329.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pembuatan perhi:
This group covers:
- the manufacture of imitation jewellery containing neither pearls (whether natural or cultured), precious or semi-precious stones, nor (except as plating or as an ancillary material) precious metals or metals clad with precious metals, such as rings, bracelets, brooches, earrings, necklaces and similar small articles, as well as personal articles of jewellery made of base metal clad with precious metals; and imitation jewellery containing imitation stones (such as imitation gemstones and imitation diamonds);
- the manufacture of metal watch straps (except of precious metal).
This group does not cover:
- the manufacture of jewellery made of precious metal or base metal clad with precious metal, see subclass 3211;
- the manufacture of jewellery containing genuine gemstones, see subclass 3211;
- the manufacture of watch straps of precious metal, see subclass 3211.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pembuatan perka:
This group covers
- the manufacture of machine tools for working metal and other materials (wood, bone, stone, hard plastic, hard rubber, cold glass and others), including those using laser beams, electromagnetic waves, plasma arcs, magnetic vibration and others;
- the manufacture of machine tools for turning, drilling, milling, planing, grinding and others;
- the manufacture of pressing and stamping machine tools;
- the manufacture of percussion presses, hydraulic presses, hydraulic brakes, hammers and forging machines;
- the manufacture of draw benches, thread rollers, or machines for working wire;
- the manufacture of stationary machines for nailing, stapling, gluing or otherwise assembling wood, cork, bone, hard rubber, or plastic and others;
- the manufacture of stationary rotary or rotary-percussion machines for drilling, boring, riveting, cutting sheet metal and others;
- the manufacture of presses for the particle-board industry and the like;
- the manufacture of electroplating machines;
- the manufacture of parts and accessories for machine tools, such as work holders, dividing heads and other special parts incorporated into machine tools.
This group does not cover
- the manufacture of interchangeable tools for hand tools or machine tools (drills, punches, dies, milling-machine cutters, turning tools, saw blades, cutting blades and others), see subgroup 2593;
- the manufacture of hand-held electric soldering irons, see subgroup 2790;
- the manufacture of power-driven hand tools, see subgroup 2818;
- the manufacture of machinery used in metal rolling or metal casting, see subgroup 2823;
- the manufacture of machinery for mining and quarrying, see subgroup 2824.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pembuatan pupuk:
This group covers
- the manufacture of straight nitrogen, phosphate, or potassium fertilizers; urea, natural phosphates, and natural potassium salts; ZA, TSP, and DSP fertilizers;
- the manufacture of related nitrogen compounds, such as nitric and sulphonitric acids, nitrous acid, ammonia, ammonium chloride, ammonium carbonate, as well as potassium nitrites and nitrates.

This group covers
- the manufacture of fertilizers containing microorganisms or fertilizer formulations derived from industrial by-products whose main component is a micronutrient content;
- the manufacture of growing media with humus/peat as the principal ingredient, including the manufacture of mixed growing media from natural soil, sand, clay, and minerals;
- the manufacture of ameliorant materials (soil conditioners and improvers) such as agricultural lime, phosphate lime, dolomite, zeolite, and ameliorant materials containing organic matter.

This group covers
- the manufacture of fertilizers containing at least two primary macronutrients through a chemical-reaction process, such as monoammonium phosphate (compound nitrogen-phosphate fertilizer), potassium ammonium chloride (compound nitrogen-potassium fertilizer), potassium metaphosphate (compound phosphate-potassium fertilizer) and ammonium potassium phosphate (compound nitrogen-phosphate-potassium fertilizer);
- the manufacture of fertilizers containing at least two primary macronutrients through the physical blending of fertilizers without altering the chemical properties and characteristics of the original fertilizers;
- the manufacture of fertilizers containing secondary macronutrients of the calcium, magnesium, and sulphur types, such as kieserite (magnesium and sulphur) and magnesium oxide (magnesium).

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pembuatan senja:
This group covers
- the manufacture of military weapons, such as artillery, cannons, rocket launchers, flame-throwers, grenade launchers, torpedo tubes and the like, machine guns, and other heavy projectile weapons used by the military;
- the manufacture of small firearms, such as pistols, revolvers, rifles, and shotguns, whether for military or police use;
- the manufacture of gas guns, spring guns, and air guns;
- the manufacture of war munitions;
- the manufacture of cartridges for shotguns, revolvers, and pistols;
- the manufacture of explosive devices, such as bombs, grenades, torpedoes, mines, rockets, and missiles used by the military.
This group also covers
- the manufacture of firearms and their ammunition for hunting, sport, or protection;
- the manufacture of intercontinental ballistic missiles (ICBMs).
This group does not cover
- the manufacture of percussion caps, detonators or signalling flares, see subgroup 2029;
- the manufacture of optical sights for firearms, see subgroup 2670;
- the manufacture of short knives or daggers, swords, bayonets and the like, see subgroup 2593;
- the manufacture of armoured vehicles for the transport of bank funds and the safeguarding of other valuables, see subgroup 2910;
- the manufacture of military aircraft and spacecraft, see subgroup 3030;
- the manufacture of tanks and other armoured motorized combat vehicles, see subgroup 3040;
- the manufacture of warships and other military vessels, see subgroup 3011.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pembuatan tangk:
This group covers
- the manufacture of tanks, reservoirs, vats, and similar containers of metal, generally made as fixtures, for storage, or for industrial purposes, whether lined or thermally insulated;
- the manufacture of gas cylinders and other pressurized tanks for compressed or liquefied gas, such as autoclaves, liquefied petroleum gas (LPG) cylinders, and silo tanks.
This group does not cover
- the manufacture of casks, drums, cans, pails, boxes and the like of metal generally used for transporting and packing goods, see subgroup 2594;
- the manufacture of transport containers, see subgroup 2920;
- the manufacture of tanks (armoured military vehicles), see subgroup 3040.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pembuatan tekst:
This group covers
- the manufacture of textile floor coverings, such as carpets, rugs and carpet tiles, including the manufacture of prayer mats and the like, made of fibres, whether natural, synthetic or blended fibres, and produced by weaving (woven), tufting, braiding, flocking and needle-punching processes;
- the manufacture of artificial-grass carpets (synthetic turf).
This group does not cover
- the manufacture of mats of plaited material, see subgroup 1629;
- the manufacture of floor coverings of cork, see subgroup 1629;
- the manufacture of heavy-duty floor coverings, e.g. vinyl and linoleum, see subgroup 2220;
- the manufacture of carpets made of cork, rubber or plastic materials, see group 16299, 22191 or 22201;
- the manufacture of prayer mats/floor coverings made by joining and/or sewing together several textile materials, see group 13921;
- the manufacture of floor cloths with a hard surface layer, see group 13999.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pembuatan wadah:
This group covers
- the manufacture of metal containers, such as food/beverage cans, paint/other chemical cans, casks, drums, pails, boxes, and jerrycans, including components for metal cans;
- the manufacture of metal closures, including metal bottle caps, such as crown corks and lug caps.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pembuatan wine:
This group covers
- the production of wine (whether from grapes or fruits other than grapes), such as grape wine, still grape wine, sparkling wine, mead, fruit wine, rice wine, glutinous rice wine, Balinese brem wine, vegetable wine, tuak (palm wine), tonic wine, sake;
- the production of sparkling wine;
- the production of wine from concentrated grape must;
- the production of alcoholic beverages from undistilled fermentation, such as sake, apple cider, perry (pear cider), mead, wine from other fruits, and mixed beverages containing alcohol;
- the production of vermouth and the like;
- the blending of wine;
- the production of low-alcohol or non-alcoholic wine.
This group does not cover
- the production of vinegar, see subclass 1079;
- the bottling and labeling of wine, see subclass 4633 (if the packaging is carried out as part of wholesale trade) and 8292 (if the packaging is carried out on a fee or contract basis).

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- penangkapan ika:
This group covers
- the catching of fish for commercial purposes in inland freshwater bodies;
- the taking of crustaceans (shrimp, crabs and the like), molluscs (clams, squid and the like), amphibians (frogs and the like), reptiles (crocodiles, sea turtles, tortoises, monitor lizards, water snakes and the like), aquatic plants, and other freshwater biota;
- the catching of fish and other freshwater biota that are protected, listed in the appendices of the Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species of Wild Fauna and Flora (CITES), and/or restricted under the prevailing laws and regulations, such as super red arowana, jardini arowana, freshwater crocodile, eel, and sharks and rays;
- the taking of freshwater animals/biota;
- the gathering of freshwater materials.

This group covers
- the catching of fish for commercial purposes in the oceans and coastal waters, comprising finfish (tuna, skipjack, sharks and rays), crustaceans (shrimp, swimming crabs, crabs and the like), molluscs (clams, oysters, squid, octopus, snails and the like), coelenterates (jellyfish and the like), echinoderms (sea cucumbers, sea urchins and the like), amphibians (frogs and the like), reptiles (crocodiles, sea turtles, tortoises, monitor lizards, water snakes and the like), algae (seaweed and other plants that live in water), and other aquatic biota;
- the catching of fish and other marine biota that are protected, listed in the appendices of the Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species of Wild Fauna and Flora (CITES), and/or restricted under the prevailing laws and regulations, such as whales, dugongs, sea turtles, dolphins, Napoleon fish, seahorses, saltwater crocodiles, hard corals and soft corals, Banggai cardinalfish, and sharks and rays.
This subgroup also covers:
- the gathering of marine biota and other marine materials, such as natural pearls, coral reefs, sponges, seaweed, and algae.
This subgroup does not cover:
- the catching of marine mammals on land, such as sea lions and seals, see subgroup 0170;
- the processing of whales on factory ships, see group 101;
- the processing of fish, crustaceans, and molluscs in factories, whether on ships or on land, see group 102;
- the chartering of pleasure boats with crew for sea transport (e.g. for cruises), see subgroup 5011;
- patrol, inspection, and fisheries-protection services, see subgroup 8423;
- sport or recreational angling activities and related services, see subgroup 9319;
- the operation of sport-fishing facilities, see subgroup 9319.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pencucian dan d:
This group covers
- washing and dry-cleaning, ironing, etc., of all kinds of garments (including fur) and textiles, provided by mechanical equipment, by hand, or by coin-operated machines, whether for the general public or for industrial or commercial clients;
- collection and delivery of laundry;
- carpet and rug washing and curtain and drape cleaning, whether at the client's premises or not;
- the provision of laundering and dry-cleaning services, ironing, pressing, etc., for all kinds of garments (including fur) and textiles, combined rental and servicing of textiles including the washing and cleaning of textiles, e.g. linen, work uniforms and other related goods;
- reusable diaper supply services.
This group does not cover
- repair and alteration of garments, see subclass 9529;
- rental of garments other than work uniforms, the washing of which is integrated with the rental activity, see subclass 7729.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pencucian rambu:
This group covers:
- washing of hair, trimming and cutting, styling, dyeing, colouring, perming, straightening and similar activities;
- hair styling;
- shaving and trimming of beards, moustaches, and sideburns.
This group does not cover:
- the manufacture of wigs, see subclass 3290.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pengolahan gula:
This group covers
- the processing of sugar and/or sweeteners into other forms, such as sugar cubes, liquid sugar, and powdered sugar;
- the manufacture of sugar substitutes from cane juice, beet, maple, stevia, and palm plants, such as coconut and sugar palm;
- the manufacture of molasses, non-fruit sweet sauce toppings, and brown sugar whose main raw material is not derived from palm sap.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pengoperasian f:
This group covers
- the operation of arts facilities, such as auditoriums (halls) for concert and theatre performances, as well as cultural centres/cultural parks;
- the operation of arts facilities that support the creation of fine-art works and other arts facilities.
This group also covers
- the operation of venues for live music performances, music clubs, and similar facilities where artists perform.
This group does not cover:
- the retail trade of paintings and sculptures (the commercial activities of art galleries), see subclass 4769;
- the operation of cinema buildings, see subclass 5914;
- the booking and sale of tickets for theatre and sporting performances, as well as other entertainment and recreation activities, see subclass 7990;
- the operation of arts facilities used by an arts group for its own performances, see subclass 9020;
- the operation of various types of museums, see subclass 9020;
- the operation of dance floors and ballrooms where the serving of beverages is not the main activity, see subclass 9329.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pengoperasian s:
This group covers
- the operation of transmission systems that convey electricity from generating facilities to distribution systems or convey electric power between systems through high-voltage power networks (between 35 kilovolts and 245 kilovolts) and/or extra-high-voltage networks (greater than 245 kilovolts), including their substations, whether from own production or from third-party production;
- the operation of distribution systems (such as lines, poles, meters, and cables) that convey electric power received from generating facilities or transmission systems to final consumers, usually at medium voltage and below (below 35 kilovolts), including their distribution substations, whether from own production or from third-party production;
- the leasing and lending of electric-power distribution networks;
- the distribution of electric power through electricity networks;
- the sale of electricity to consumers using own transmission/distribution network assets;
- the operation of electricity-capacity and power-transmission exchanges, except through intermediaries;
- the conveyance of stored electric power through electricity networks.
This group does not cover
- the sale of electricity through networks owned by third parties, see group 35401;
- the production of electricity not derived from storage, see subgroups 3511, 3512;
- the operation of public electric-vehicle charging stations (SPKLU) integrated with a generating facility, see group 35140.

This group covers:
- the operation of websites that use a search engine to generate and maintain large databases of internet addresses and content in an easily searchable format;
- the operation of websites for price comparison, product specifications and the like, as well as media sites that provide periodically updated content by providing links to other sites;
- the operation of websites or information portals related to organisations, institutions, or companies that provide information on a periodic basis, for both internal and external purposes, such as websites of schools, hospitals, company information systems, and the like.
This group also covers other information services, such as telephone-based information services, information search services on a contract or fee basis, news clipping or press clipping services, as well as the compilation of information or directories on a contract or fee basis.
This group does not cover:
- the operation of websites, applications, or other digital platforms that facilitate electronic transactions resulting in the transfer of ownership of goods and/or services, such as marketplace activities, digital advertising, and on-demand online services. These activities are classified under their respective groups according to the main business sector served, for example:
* intermediation services related to retail trade of physical goods, see division 47;
* intermediation services related to accommodation, see division 55;
* intermediation services related to post and courier, see division 53;
* intermediation services related to telecommunications, see division 61;
* and so on;
- publishing activities such as newspapers, see division 58;
- broadcasting activities, see division 60;
- the activities of news syndicates and news agencies, see subclass 6031;
- call centre activities, see subclass 8220;
- financial technology (fintech) activities, such as peer-to-peer (P2P) lending fintech (see subclass 6495) and the operation of payment systems (see division 66).

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pengoperasian t:
This group covers
- the operation of coke ovens;
- the production of coke and semi-coke;
- the production of pitch and pitch coke;
- the production of coke-oven gas (illuminating gas);
- the production of crude coal tar and lignite tar;
- the agglomeration of coke.
This group does not cover
- the manufacture of coal briquettes, see subgroup 1920;
- the distillation of gas by gas works distributed through pipelines, see group 35202;
- the manufacture of gas and coke combined with iron and steel processing activities, see group 24101-24103.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- penguburan dan:
This group covers
- the burial and cremation of human or animal corpses and related activities, such as:
* preparing the deceased for burial or cremation, embalming, and undertaker services;
* providing burial or cremation services;
* renting of equipped space in funeral homes;
- the rental or sale of graves;
- the upkeep of graves and mausoleums and matters relating to the burial process serving the public.
This group does not cover
- gardening activities at cemeteries, see subclass 8130;
- religious funeral ceremony activities, see subclass 9491.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pengumpulan lim:
This group covers
- the collection of non-hazardous solid waste or refuse within a local area, for example the collection of household and business waste using waste bins, waste containers and the like, which may contain various recoverable materials;
- the collection of recyclable materials (whether separated or not);
- the collection of non-hazardous waste of animal or plant origin;
- the collection of used cooking oils and fats;
- the collection of refuse in public places;
- the collection of construction and demolition waste;
- the collection and clearing of debris or rubble;
- the collection of waste from industrial plants;
- the operation of waste-transfer facilities for non-hazardous waste.
This group does not cover
- the collection of wastewater, see division 37;
- the collection of hazardous waste, see subgroup 3812;
- the operation of sites for the disposal and permanent storage of non-hazardous waste, see subgroup 3821;
- the operation of facilities for sorting recoverable waste, see subgroup 3830.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pengumpulan/pen:
This group covers
- the collection/pick-up, sorting/processing, transport and delivery of letters, documents, parcels, goods, and packages, whether domestic or international, operating outside the universal service obligation using one or more modes of transport, where the activities may use own (private) transport or public transport.
This group also covers
- the delivery of non-prepared meals that have been preserved or packaged in such a way as to allow further processing and not be easily perishable during the process of collection, processing, transport, and distribution as part of the parcel service type;
- door-to-door delivery services, including food delivery.
This group does not cover
- the transport of goods, see subgroup (according to mode of transport), see subgroups 4912, 4923, 5012, 5022, and 5120;
- money remittance activities, see subgroup 6419;
- logistics services other than postal, see subgroup 5229;
- the delivery of furniture which may include disassembly or installation, see subgroup 4923;
- the home delivery of ready-to-eat meals carried out by the unit that also cooks them, see division 56.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- penyaluran gas:
This group covers
- the distribution of gas through networks at extra-high pressure (more than 10 bar); at high pressure (between 4 bar and 10 bar); and at medium pressure and below (below 4 bar), whether from own production or third-party production, to consumers or customers;
- the trade of gas to consumers through pipelines;
- the activities of gas agents that trade gas through gas distribution systems operated by third parties;
- the operation of commodity and capacity exchanges for the transport of gaseous fuels.
This group also covers
- distribution activities through networks for gaseous hydrogen fuel produced through electrolysis, photolysis, thermochemical, biological, geological, and/or other methods, utilizing new and renewable energy sources or fossil energy sources;
- the distribution of biogas and other gases through networks.
This group does not cover
- the conveyance of gas through pipelines on a fee or commission basis, see group 49300.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- penyediaan jasa:
This group covers
- the provision of intermediary services for the purchase of road, rail, water, or air transport tickets for passengers, whether for domestic or international destinations.
This group also covers
- the operation of online platforms for booking transport tickets;
- ticket reservation services for passenger transport.
This group does not cover
- the operation of online platforms for booking ridesharing services, see group 52329;
- intermediation of transport services such as taxi-hailing services, without providing the transport service itself, see group 52329;
- the development/creation of applications for booking transport tickets via computer or internet, see subgroup 6219.

This group covers
- the provision of social, counselling, welfare, referral, and similar services aimed at the elderly and persons with disabilities, at home or elsewhere, organized by non-profit Social Welfare Institutions (LKS):
* home-visit activities for the elderly and persons with disabilities;
* day-care activities for the elderly and persons with disabilities;
* service activities that assist the elderly or persons with disabilities in carrying out activities of daily living (ADL);
* social rehabilitation, habilitation, and vocational training activities for persons with disabilities, with a limited educational component.
This group also covers
- care activities;
- home nursing activities as part of home-care services.

This group covers
- the provision of social, counselling, welfare, referral, and similar services aimed at the elderly and persons with disabilities, at home or elsewhere, organized by the government:
* home-visit activities for the elderly and persons with disabilities;
* day-care activities for the elderly and persons with disabilities;
* service activities that assist the elderly or persons with disabilities in carrying out activities of daily living (ADL);
* social rehabilitation, habilitation, and vocational training activities for persons with disabilities, with a limited educational component.
This group also covers
- care activities;
- home nursing activities as part of home-care services.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- penyewaan dan p:
This group covers
- the leasing and operation of own or leased real estate, such as other non-residential buildings, including data centres;
- the development of other non-residential building projects for own operation;
- the development of other non-residential building projects for sale;
- the leasing of factories, whether or not equipped with machinery and equipment.
This group also covers
- the leasing of the roof of non-residential buildings, for example for the installation of solar power panels.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- perdagangan bes:
This group covers
- wholesale of furniture;
- wholesale of lighting equipment;
- wholesale of carpets;
- wholesale of mattresses and spring mattresses;
- wholesale of outdoor furniture;
- wholesale of furniture for warehouses, churches, medical facilities, and others.

This group covers
- the wholesale of spare parts, components, equipment, and accessories for cars, whether new or used, such as tyres;
- the wholesale of batteries and accumulators for cars.
This group does not cover
- the activities of agents involved in the wholesale of spare parts and accessories for cars and light vehicles, see subgroup 4610;
- the wholesale of ships, aircraft, trains, including their spare parts and accessories, see subgroup 4659.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- perdagangan ece:
This group covers
- the retail sale of games and toys of various materials, such as dolls, marbles, jacks, congklak, Scrabble, carrom, toy musical instruments, toy cars, toy weapons, toy cooking sets and toy household furnishings;
- the retail sale of party items, for example costume disguises, masks, party favours (make-up, novelty gags and others) and conjuring tricks.
This group also covers
- the retail sale of toy drones.
This group does not cover
- the retail sale of game consoles and video games on physical media, see subgroup 4740;
- the retail sale of used games and toys, see subgroup 4774;
- the distribution of video games through streaming and downloading by their publisher, see subgroup 5821;
- the distribution of audio through streaming and downloading by its publisher, see subgroup 5920;
- the publishing and editing of games and board games, see subgroup 5819;
- content distribution and sharing platforms for video games, see subgroup 6039.

This group covers:
- the retail trade of metal construction materials, such as wire rope, mosquito-mesh wire, nails, nuts or bolts, hinges, latches, locks, keys, water tanks, water towers, rolling doors, awnings, and sheet zinc;
- the retail trade of porcelain construction materials, such as toilets, bidets, washbasins, urinals, wash sinks, bathtubs, and wall tiles;
- the retail trade of wooden construction materials, such as boards, joists, batten boards, moulding boards, telephone poles, electricity poles, sleeper beams, window/door frames, door/window leaves, wooden tiles, wooden roofing (shingles), plywood (three-ply), interior plywood, teak wood, particle board, chip board, veneer wood, and plywood for concrete formwork;
- the retail trade of construction materials made of clay, lime, cement, or glass, such as pressed roof tiles, interlocking roof tiles, pressed bricks, hollow bricks, fire bricks, floor tiles, wall tiles, concrete-block tiles, ventilation blocks, bathtubs, toilets, ceiling boards, irrigation pipes, and concrete pipes (buis);
- the retail trade of other building materials, such as plastic pipes and hoses, formica, corrugated plastic sheeting, flat asbestos cement, layered asbestos cement, asbestos-cement conduit pipes, cement, lime, sand, stone, nails, and sanitary fittings.

This group covers
- retail sale of carpets and rugs;
- retail sale of curtains and drapes;
- retail sale of wall and floor coverings such as wallpaper, tiles, laminate, and vinyl flooring;
This group does not cover
- retail sale of floor tiles (building materials), laminate, and vinyl, see subclass 4752.

This group covers
- the retail trade of sporting goods and equipment, including fishing gear, weapons and ammunition for hunting, camping goods, and others;
- the retail trade of boats;
- the retail trade of bicycles, including electric bicycles, unicycles, hoverboards, kick scooters, segways;
- the retail trade of specialized sports footwear, for example football boots, ice skates, and ski boots;
- the retail trade of specialized sports apparel and equipment for skiing, martial arts, ballet, and others;
- the retail trade of parachutes, tents, sleeping bags, and others.
This group does not cover
- the retail trade of non-specialized sports footwear, for example tennis shoes, basketball shoes, gym shoes, training shoes and others, see subclass 4771.

This group covers
- the retail trade of media recordings;
- the retail trade of musical instruments, sheet music and related accessories, for example strings, music stands, metronomes;
- the retail trade of philatelic, numismatic and collectors' items such as stamps and coins;
- the activities of commercial art galleries.
This group also covers
- the retail trade of art supplies, including beads, clay, canvas, oil and water paints, and others.
This group does not cover
- the retail trade of video games in physical media form, see subclass 4740;
- the retail trade of souvenirs, handicrafts and religious goods, see subclass 4778;
- the retail trade of antiques, second-hand and antique books, second-hand musical instruments, and second-hand media recordings, see subclass 4774;
- the distribution of audio through streaming media and downloading by its publisher, see subclass 5920.

This group covers
- the retail sale of spare parts, components, equipment, and accessories for cars, whether new or used.
This group does not cover
- the retail sale of automotive fuel, see subclass 4730;
- the retail sale of cars, see subclass 4781;
- the repair and maintenance of cars and motorcycles, see group 953.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pertambangan ba:
This group covers
- coal mining: underground or surface mining, including mining by liquefaction methods;
- cleaning, sizing, grading, crushing, and compacting of coal to classify it, improve its quality, or facilitate its transport or storage.
This group also covers
- recovery of coal from culm banks (mine waste piles)
This group does not cover
- lignite mining, see subclass 0520;
- extraction and agglomeration of peat, see subclass 0892;
- support services for coal mining, see subclass 0990;
- test drilling for coal mining, see subclass 0990;
- coke oven operations to produce solid fuels, see subclass 1910;
- manufacture of coal briquette fuels, ovoids, and similar solid coal fuels, see subclass 1920;
- development or preparation of land for coal mining, see subclass 4312;
- beneficiation of coal without carrying out mining activities, see group 05102.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pertambangan bi:
This group covers
- mining of ores containing uranium and thorium concentrates, such as uranium ore (pitchblende);
- concentration of uranium and thorium;
- production of yellowcake.
This group does not cover
- upgrading of the grade and quality of uranium and thorium ores, see subclass 2011;
- production of uranium metal from uranium and thorium ores or other ores, see subclass 2420;
- further processing of uranium, such as smelting and refining, see subclass 2420.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- pertambangan li:
This group covers
- lignite (brown coal) mining: underground or surface mining, including mining by liquefaction methods, comprising the extraction, crushing, washing, screening, blending, and compacting of lignite to improve its quality and facilitate its transport and storage;
- washing, agglomerating, crushing, and compacting of lignite to improve its quality or facilitate its transport or storage.
This group does not cover
- coal mining, see subclass 0510;
- peat extraction, see subclass 0892;
- support services for lignite mining, see subclass 0990;
- test drilling for coal mining, see subclass 0990;
- manufacture of briquette fuels from lignite, ovoids (oval-shaped), and other similar solid coal fuels, see subclass 1920;
- development or preparation of land for lignite mining, see subclass 4312.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- reparasi dan pe:
This group covers
- repair and maintenance of motorcycles, both conventional and electric;
- spray-painting and painting of motorcycles and their accessories;
- repair of vehicle bodies;
- conversion, washing, polishing of motorcycles, and other servicing.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- transportasi ba:
This group covers
- freight transport by rail over long distances as well as short-distance dedicated freight lines, such as agricultural produce, mining and quarrying products (including fuel oil, crude oil, processed products, LPG, LNG, and CNG), carbon-free fuels as energy carriers (hydrogen, ammonia, and other compounds), dangerous goods, hazardous and toxic waste, and industrial products. This transport may be carried out in gaseous, solid, or liquid form depending on the needs and storage conditions.
This subclass also covers
- freight transport by cable car or aerial cableway;
- traction/haulage services provided over long distances.
This subclass does not cover
- warehousing and storage, see subclass 5210;
- freight station activities, see group 52212;
- operation of railway infrastructure and related activities such as switching and marshalling of rail consists, see group 52212;
- cargo handling on behalf of third parties, see subclass 5224.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n- transportasi mi:
This group covers
- transport of petroleum and natural gas (crude oil, fuel oil, processed products, and natural gas), liquids, water, slurry, carbon dioxide (CO2), and other commodities via pipeline;
- transport of natural gas via pipeline from producers, production-sharing contractors, or processing refineries to local distribution systems;
- transport of carbon via pipeline for carbon injection into geological formations.
This group also covers
- distribution of carbon-free fuels as energy carriers, such as hydrogen, ammonia, and other compounds, via pipeline;
- operation of pump stations for pipeline transport.
This group does not cover
- distribution of natural or manufactured gaseous fuels, steam, or water carried out by the producer itself to end-user locations via local or regional pipelines, see subclasses 3520, 3530, and 3600;
- distribution of water by truck, see subclass 3600;
- transport of liquids and others by truck, see subclass 4923.

Kelompok ini mencakup\n.\n.\n- pembuatan:
This group covers
.
.
- manufacture and remanufacture of electric vehicles, hybrid combustion-engine vehicles, and autonomous vehicles;
- manufacture and remanufacture of passenger cars, such as sedans, jeeps, buses, ambulances, and station wagons;
- manufacture and remanufacture of commercial vehicles, such as vans, lorries, road tractors for semi-trailers, and others;
- manufacture and remanufacture of buses, trolleybuses, and railway carriages;
- manufacture of motor vehicle engines, including electric drive motors;
- manufacture and remanufacture of other motor vehicles for special purposes, such as snowmobiles, golf carts, amphibious vehicles, fire engines, street sweepers, travelling libraries, armoured cars and others, road-sweeping trolleys, tow trucks, all-terrain vehicles (ATVs), as well as go-karts and the like, including racing cars;
- manufacture and remanufacture of multipurpose four-wheeled vehicles, such as rural multipurpose mechanical implements (AMMDES);
- remanufacture of motor vehicle engines.
This group does not cover
- manufacture of lamps for motor vehicles, see subclass 2740;
- manufacture of pistons, piston rings, and carburettors, see subclass 2811;
- manufacture of agricultural and forestry tractors, see subclass 2821;
- manufacture of tracklaying excavators, see subclass 2824;
- manufacture of off-road dumping trucks, see subclass 2824;
- manufacture of bodies for motor vehicles, such as fire engines, travelling libraries, and concrete-mixer trucks, see subclass 2920;
- manufacture of armoured vehicles for the transport of goods, see subclass 2920;
- manufacture of electrical parts for motor vehicles, see subclass 2930;
- manufacture of parts and accessories for motor vehicles, see subclass 2930;
- manufacture of tanks and other military combat vehicles, see subclass 3040;
- repair and maintenance of motor vehicles, see subclass 9531;
- manufacture of trucks fitted with cranes, see subclass 2816.

Kelompok ini mencakup\nKelompok ini menc:
This group covers
This group covers the provision of a combination of day-to-day office administrative services, such as reception, financial planning, billing and recordkeeping, as well as personnel and mail services, for others on a fee or contract basis.
This group covers:
- document preparation, for example editing, proofreading, typing, word processing, and pre-filing;
- other secretarial support services;
- document transcription;
- letter or resume writing;
- the provision of mailbox rental and other postal and mail-delivery services, for example pre-sorting and addressing;
- duplicating;
- blueprinting;
- the operation of self-service photocopying machines;
- digitization of files (without further data processing);
- electronic-book formatting.
This group does not cover:
- the printing of documents (offset printing, quick printing, digital printing, photocopying, etc.), see subclass 1811;
- prepress services, see subclass 1812;
- the storage of paper files, see subclass 5210;
- courier services, see subclass 5320;
- data processing and file digitization associated with further data processing, see subclass 6310;
- the storage of data files, see subclass 6310;
- the rental of unfurnished offices, co-working spaces, and fully furnished offices, see subclass 6812;
- shared service center (SSC) activities involving strategic and managerial/centralized activities, see subclass 7010;
- the development and organization of direct-mail advertising campaigns, see subclass 7310;
- the rental of containers for use as offices, see subclass 7739;
- public stenography services and specialized stenotype services such as court reporting, see subclass 8299;
- the archiving of all types of documents (in paper or electronic form), see subclass 9112.

Kelompok ini mencakup\naktivitas pencari:
This group covers
the search, rescue, diving, removal, or salvage of vessels/cargo that have been involved in an accident or are in distress in waters, whether holding cultural-heritage status, suspected cultural-heritage objects, or objects other than suspected cultural-heritage objects.
This group does not cover
- construction and dredging of waterways, see subclass 4291;
- construction of underwater cables or underwater pipelines, see groups 422, 429;
- cargo handling, see group 52240.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas\n- pener:
This group covers the activities of
- publishing of books, brochures, and similar publications;
- publishing of dictionaries and encyclopaedias;
- publishing of atlases, maps, and charts;
- publishing of electronic books (e-books) and audio books;
- publishing of comic books and graphic novels.
All possible forms of book publishing (whether in print, electronic, digital, analogue, or other forms) are included in this group.
This group does not cover
- manufacture of globes, see subclass 3290;
- publishing of advertising material, see subclass 5819;
- publishing of music and sheet-music books (scores), see subclass 5920;
- joint publishing and distribution of podcasts, see subclass 5920;
- on-demand audio distribution and streaming services (on request by third parties), see subclass 6010;
- activities of independent authors, see subclass 9011.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas angkutan:
This group covers international sea-freight transport for special cargo, for example the transport of dangerous goods, hazardous and toxic waste, including fish and other aquatic organisms. Specialized sea transport serves irregular and non-scheduled routes (tramping) between domestic ports and foreign ports.
This group covers
- foreign distribution of carbon-free fuels in gaseous, solid, or liquid form depending on the needs and storage conditions, as energy carriers (hydrogen, ammonia, and other compounds), using specially designed vessels;
- foreign sea transport of fish by Indonesian-flagged fish carrier vessels;
- foreign sea transport of fish by foreign-flagged fish carrier vessels;
- chartering of sea-transport vessels together with their operators.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas gadai ya:
This group covers pawnbroking activities conducted on a conventional basis, comprising
- disbursement of loans secured under pledge law;
- disbursement of loans secured under fiduciary security;
- safekeeping services for valuables;
- appraisal services.

This group covers pawnbroking activities conducted entirely on the basis of sharia principles, comprising
- disbursement of loans secured under pledge law;
- disbursement of loans secured under fiduciary security;
- safekeeping services for valuables;
- appraisal services.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas jasa int:
This group covers intermediation-service activities for business-support activities not elsewhere classified. This group covers units that bring together clients and service providers on a remuneration or contract basis.
These intermediation activities may be carried out through digital platforms or through non-digital channels (face-to-face, door-to-door, telephone, mail, etc.). The remuneration or commission may be received from the client or the service provider. Income for intermediation activities may include other revenue sources, such as advertising income.
This group also covers:
- the reservation and sale of tickets for theatre, sports, and other entertainment events.
This group does not cover:
- the activities of brokers and agents for electricity and natural gas, see group 354;
- intermediation activities for specialised construction services, see group 434;
- wholesale trade on a remuneration or contract basis, see group 461;
- intermediation-service activities for retail sale, see subclass 4790;
- intermediation-service activities for transport, see group 523;
- intermediation-service activities for post and courier activities, see subclass 5330;
- intermediation-service activities for accommodation, see subclass 5540;
- intermediation-service activities for food and beverage service activities, see subclass 5640;
- intermediation-service activities for software publishing, see group 582;
- intermediation-service activities for telecommunications activities, see subclass 6120;
- intermediation-service activities for finance and insurance, see category L;
- intermediation-service activities for real estate activities, see subclass 6821;
- patent-brokerage (marketing) service activities, see subclass 7491;
- intermediation-service activities for the rental and leasing of tangible goods and non-financial intangible assets, see group 775;
- travel-agency activities, see subclass 7911;
- intermediation-service activities for courses and tutoring, subclass 8561;
- intermediation-service activities for medical, dental, and other health services, see subclass 8691;
- intermediation-service activities for residential care activities, see subclass 8791;
- intermediation-service activities for the repair and maintenance of computers, personal and household goods, as well as motor vehicles and motorcycles, see subclass 9540;
- intermediation-service activities for personal services, see subclass 9640.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas jasa kon:
This group covers consulting, design, and development services for custom-built (not off-the-shelf) integrated system solutions by modifying existing hardware, such as sensors and microcontrollers. Such modifications are performed on IoT hardware and/or the software embedded within it.
This group does not cover:
- the manufacture of chips, see group 26120;
- the publishing of internet-of-things (IoT)-based software, see group 58290;
- IoT-based software development activities, see group 62199;
- the manufacture of transmission equipment or connectivity modules, such as bluetooth, Radio Frequency (RF), GSM, and other forms of connectivity used in IoT, see group 26399;
- IoT-based product manufacturing activities, which are classified in their respective groups according to the type of final product, such as:
* electrical monitoring and control devices/modules with connectivity (IoT) capability, see group 26512;
* electronic monitoring and control devices/modules with connectivity (IoT) capability, including embedded systems, data loggers, real-time monitoring units, early warning systems, and similar devices, see group 26513;
* the manufacture of electromedical and electrotherapeutic devices equipped with IoT features, see group 26602.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas jasa pel:
This group covers aircraft and passenger service activities, consisting of
- provision and/or development of facilities for the landing, take-off, manoeuvring, parking, and storage of aircraft (PJP4U), including the provision of aircraft hangars and all facilities located on the runway, such as taxiways and aprons;
- aircraft accident handling and fire-fighting;
- terminal facilities for passenger transport services (PJP2U), including the use of aerobridges (aviobridges) and the use of departure check-in counters.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas jasa per:
This group covers other intermediary service activities related to passenger transport without operating one's own means of transport and not elsewhere classified.
This group covers:
- the operation of online platforms for booking ridesharing services,
- the brokerage of passenger seat rentals on ships and aircraft,
- the arrangement of carpool and vanpool services,
- the arrangement of non-emergency medical transport, without providing social assistance services,
This group also covers:
- the arrangement of non-emergency medical transport, without providing social assistance services;
- intermediary transport services such as taxi-hailing services, without providing the transport service itself;
- reservation services for passenger transport;
- the management of travel itineraries;
- the handling of travel documents;
- representation services on behalf of passengers or transport operators;
This group does not cover:
- the operation of taxis and other types of road transport for passengers, see subclasses 4922 and 4929;
- the brokerage of freight transport on ships and aircraft, see subclass 5231;
- the operation of online platforms enabling a person to rent a vehicle (car, bicycle, scooter, etc.) for self-driving, see subclass 7751;
- units providing reservation services together with travel advice or other expertise, see subclass 7911.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas jasa ter:
This group covers land-transport-related service activities not elsewhere classified.
This group also covers
- towing assistance;
- liquefaction of gas for transport purposes;
- operation of toll-collection facilities;
- truck-freight cargo survey activities.
This group does not cover
- operation and maintenance of roads (including winter maintenance), bridges, and tunnels, see section F;
- liquefaction of natural gas for transport purposes carried out at the mine site, see subclass 0910;
- regasification of natural gas for distribution via pipeline networks, see subclass 3520;
- regasification of natural gas for transport purposes via pipeline, see subclass 4930;
- movement of freight goods at industrial sites with transport equipment not intended for public roads, see subclass 5224.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas kesehata:
This group covers animal health activities other than those covered in groups 75001 and 75002, such as:
- animal blood transfusion units/animal blood banks;
- eye banks, sperm banks for companion animals, organ transplant banks, cell and tissue banks;
- animal optical services;
- animal ambulance activities;
- other supporting animal health services.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas konsulta:
This group covers computer consultancy and other computer facilities management activities not already covered in other groups, comprising
- consultancy regarding the kind or type, configuration, and requirements of computer hardware and/or software;
- the planning and design of computer systems that integrate computer hardware, software, and communications technologies, with or without related services such as system installation, training, and user support;
- the provision of management and operation services for clients' computer systems and/or data processing facilities directly on the client's premises (on-site), as well as related support services such as software used on medical devices;
- consultancy related to the technical specifications and procurement of system components, both hardware and software, which may be provided directly or through a third party/vendor.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas lainnya:
This group covers other activities not covered elsewhere related or closely connected to insurance, guarantee, and pension-fund activities other than financial intermediation, claims adjustment, and insurance-agent activities, such as
- salvage administration;
- insurance and pension-fund consultancy activities.
This group does not cover
- ship salvage activities, see subclass 5222;
- publishing of insurance software/applications, see subclass 5829.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas pelayana:
This group covers seaport service activities related to water transport for passengers, animals, or goods.
This group also covers
- operation of terminal facilities such as ports and docks;
- operation of maritime navigation;
- inspection of cargo loads in containers and/or shipping containers using ionizing-radiation sources (radioactive substances and ionizing-radiation generators);
- operation of dangerous-goods stacking areas as part of seaport services;
- operation of shipping services and anchorage activities, mooring services, pilotage services, and towage.
This group does not cover
- cargo handling, see group 52240;
- operation of marina docks (tourism or recreational docks), see subclass 9329;
- operation of dangerous-goods stacking areas that are not part of seaport services, see group 52105.

This group covers fishing-port service activities related to water transport for fishing activities.
This group also covers
- operation of port and dock facilities;
- inspection of cargo loads in containers and/or shipping containers using ionizing-radiation sources (radioactive substances and ionizing-radiation generators);
- mooring and anchorage services for fishing vessels and pilotage services, fish loading and unloading services.
This group does not cover
- cargo handling, see group 52240;
- operation of marina docks (tourism or recreational docks), see subclass 9329.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas pemeriks:
This group covers physical, visual, or technical inspection activities for products, facilities, services, or processes carried out on-site to assess compliance with standards, specifications, or regulations, for example
- inspection activities in the agricultural field: agricultural processes and inspections;
- inspection activities in the fisheries field: IKI assessment, CKIB inspection, CKIB surveillance, CPIB inspection, HACCP inspection;
- inspection activities in the health field: inspection of health facilities and infrastructure;
- inspection activities in the technical-tracing field: technical-tracing inspection of exports, imports, and inter-island trade;
- inspection activities on infrastructure: oil and gas, electricity, disaster-protection facilities, non-destructive testing, commercial buildings within the environment, such as exhaust-gas emissions, ambient air quality, the working environment, and the commercial environment;
- inspection activities on manufactured goods (food and beverages, pharmaceuticals, textiles and textile products, production processes, and children's toys);
- safety-inspection activities;
- visual inspection.
This group also covers
- periodic inspection services;
- technical inspection services for installations, such as electric-power installations, geothermal installations, and technical installations in the construction sector;
- ship-classification inspection services;
- aerodrome-safety inspection services;
- inspection services for health facilities and infrastructure.
This group does not cover
- marine survey activities, such as quantity surveys, quality surveys, product sampling, and shipping, see group 71109;

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas pemrogra:
This group covers programming and/or application development activities based on blockchain technology, such as the design and writing of program code to create and implement smart contracts, the design of public blockchain and private blockchain infrastructure, as well as the development of applications based on other distributed ledger technology.
This group does not cover
- the trading of crypto assets or crypto commodity futures exchanges, see subclass 6612;
- data processing service activities based on blockchain technology and/or other distributed ledger technology, see subclass 6310;
- consultancy and system planning activities that integrate blockchain technology, see subclass 6220.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas pencipta:
This group covers activities for the creation and production of works of fine art through various media and methods, whether tangible or intangible.
This group covers:
- the activities of independent artists such as sculptors, painters, cartoonists, calligraphers, carvers, sketchers, and craft artists;
- the creation of digital works of fine art;
- the creation of works of art using light/lighting installations.
This group does not cover:
- the making and processing of stone statues, other than original works of art, see subclass 2396;
- the production of motion pictures and videos, see subclasses 5911, 5912;
- the operation of cinemas, see subclass 5914;
- the activities of individual theatre performers or arts agencies, see subclass 7499;
- casting activities, see subclass 7810;
- the booking and sale of tickets for theatre, sports, and other entertainment, see subclass 7990;
- photography activities, see subclass 7420;
- choreography activities, see subclass 9013;
- restoration services for works of art and museum collection objects and preventive conservation of works of art carried out by the museum itself, see division 912;
- restoration of works of art and museum collection objects and preventive conservation of works of art not carried out by other parties, see division 913;
- the creation and performance of light and sound, see subclass 9329;
- graphic design activities, see group 74192.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas peneliti:
This group covers systematic (regularly conducted) research and development activities relating to biotechnology.
This group also covers
- research and development in environmental biotechnology;
- research and development in industrial biotechnology;
- research and development in the application of biotechnology not involving genetic modification.
This group does not cover
- research and development in nanotechnology, see group 72102;
- research and development in medical biotechnology, see group 72103.

This group covers systematic (regularly conducted) research and development activities relating to medical science, life and health sciences, and health sciences.
This group also covers
- research and development in basic medical science;
- research and development in clinical medical science;
- research and development in health sciences;
- research and development in medical biotechnology;
- research and development in other medical and health sciences, such as art therapy; audiology; chiropractic; music therapy; naturopathy; occupational therapy; orthoptics; physiotherapy; podiatry; prosthetics and orthotics; speech-language pathology, as well as traditional and integrative medicine.
This group does not cover
- research and development in veterinary science, see group 72105.

This group covers systematic (regularly conducted) research and development activities relating to agricultural, livestock, forestry, fisheries, and marine sciences, as well as veterinary science.
This group also covers
- research and development in agricultural biotechnology;
- research and development in agricultural, fisheries, and forestry sciences;
- research and development in animal and dairy sciences (livestock and dairy farming);
- research and development in veterinary science;
- research and development in fertilisers;
- research and development in sustainable agricultural development.
This group does not cover
- research and development in the environmental field, see group 72101.

This group covers systematic (regularly conducted) research and development activities relating to engineering and technology. The activities covered in this group comprise research and development in engineering and technology sciences, as well as interdisciplinary sciences, particularly the natural sciences and engineering.
This group also covers
- research and development in civil engineering;
- research and development in chemical engineering;
- research and development in electrical engineering;
- research and development in electronics engineering;
- research and development in environmental engineering;
- research and development in materials engineering;
- research and development in mechanical engineering;
- research and development in medical engineering;
- research and development in agricultural engineering;
- research and development in instrumentation engineering;
- research and development in resource engineering, extractive metallurgy, and particle mechanics;
- research and development in nanotechnology;
- research and development in hydrogen technology;
- research and development in oil and gas technology;
- research and development in mineral and coal technology;
- research and development in electric power technology;
- research and development in meteorology, climatology, and geophysics engineering and technology.
This group does not cover
- research and development in computer and information sciences, see group 72101;
- research and development in biotechnology, see groups 72103 and 72104;
- research and development in nuclear technology, see group 72106.

This group covers research and development activities carried out in a regular (systematic) manner relating to technology and engineering not elsewhere classified, such as
- deoxyribonucleic acid (DNA) sequencing for general research on biological processes;
- research and development in the field of aerospace.

This group covers research and development activities conducted on a regular (systematic) basis relating to the natural sciences, comprising research and development in mathematics, physics, biology, chemistry, astronomy, geology, botany, zoology, and the like.
This group also covers
- research and development in the field of life sciences;
- research and development in the field of chemical sciences;
- research and development in the field of computer and information sciences;
- research and development in the field of earth and environmental sciences;
- research and development in the field of mathematical sciences;
- research and development in the field of physical sciences;

This group covers research and development activities carried out on a regular (systematic) basis relating to the social sciences, comprising the research and development of economics and business administration, psychology and cognitive science, education, sociology, anthropology, law, political science, government, commerce, media and communication, customs, traditions, and so forth.
This group also covers
- research and development in economics and business;
- research and development in education;
- basic research in law;
- research and development in media and communication;
- research and development in political science;
- research and development in psychology and cognitive science;
- research and development in social and economic geography;
- research and development in sociology;
- research and development in other social sciences, such as anthropology, criminology, demography, development studies, gender studies, policy and administration, and social work.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas penerbit:
This group covers the publishing of other ready-to-use (non-custom) software, including
- the publishing of operating systems;
- the publishing of business applications and other applications such as software using Distributed Ledger Technology (DLT) or financial technology software;
- the publishing of cybersecurity software;
- the publishing of modelling, design, and multimedia software;
- the publishing of marketplaces for software downloads;
- the publishing of Internet of Things (IoT)-based software;
- the publishing of artificial intelligence (AI)-based software;
- intermediation services for the publishing of software other than video games.
This group also covers the in-house development or production of software carried out by the publisher itself.

This group covers the publishing of newspapers, including advertising newspapers. All feasible forms of newspaper publishing (whether in print, electronic, digital, analogue, or other forms) are included in this group.
This group does not cover
- the production of television or video news programmes, see subclass 5911;
- news agency activities, see subclass 6031;
- the activities of independent photojournalists, see subclass 7420;
- the activities of independent journalists, see subclass 9011.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas pengangk:
This group covers the transport of goods using sea-going vessels specially designed to carry a particular type of goods, such as the transport of dangerous goods, hazardous and toxic waste, fuel oil, crude oil, refined products, liquefied petroleum gas (LPG), liquefied natural gas (LNG), and compressed natural gas (CNG), as well as fish and other aquatic biota.
This group covers
- the domestic distribution of carbon-free fuels in gaseous, solid, or liquid form as energy carriers (hydrogen, ammonia, and other compounds) using specially designed sea-going vessels;
- activities directly related to the transport of fish and other aquatic biota, comprising
* domestic sea transport of fish from fishing grounds;
* domestic sea transport of fish between ports;
- domestic sea transport in support of fishing operations;
- domestic sea transport in support of aquaculture operations;
- the chartering of sea transport together with its operator.

This group covers the transport of goods on rivers, canals, lakes, swamps, and other inland waters using vessels or cargo boats specially modified to carry only a single type of goods, including vessels meeting the technical/seaworthiness requirements appropriate to the special goods carried, comprising
- the transport of logs;
- the transport of bar, pipe, iron, or rail materials;
- the transport of bulk goods;
- the transport of liquid goods;
- the transport of goods requiring refrigeration facilities;
- the transport of plants and live animals;
- the transport of containers;
- the transport of heavy equipment;
- the transport of other special goods.

This group covers the transport of passengers using public passenger cars providing door-to-door service with fares based on agreement between the user and the transport provider, including charter, excursion, and other seasonal charter transport services.
This group also covers
- the rental of cars or other private vehicles with a driver via an application;
- the rental of cars or other private vehicles with a driver;
- the rental of bajaj, kancil, bentor, and the like with a driver, whether via an application or not.
This group does not cover
- taxi transport, see group 49293;
- motorcycle-taxi (ojek) transport, see group 49296.

This group covers passenger transport using intercity rail serving inter-regional journeys over relatively long distances, other than tourist rail transport, including the operation of trains that provide additional facilities such as sleeping cars or dining cars that form an integrated part of the passenger transport service provided by the intercity rail operator.
This group does not cover:
- urban rail and commuter rail passenger transport, see group 49211;
- the operation of aerial tramways, cable cars (gondolas), and other railways that are not part of urban transport, or that are not combined with the operation of amusement and recreation venues, see group 49291;
- the operation of aerial tramways, cable cars (gondolas), chairlifts, and other railways as part of the operation of amusement and recreation venues, see subgroup 9329;
- the operation of sleeping cars/carriages or dining cars/carriages carried out by separate units, see subgroups 5590 and 5610;
- passenger station activities, see subgroup 52212.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas pengelol:
This group covers the operation of warehouses under the Warehouse Receipt System (G-SRG), comprising the storage, maintenance, and issuance of warehouse receipts for goods stored in Warehouse Receipt System warehouses by their owners or other parties.
This group also covers:
- the operation of Warehouse Receipt System warehouses in free trade zones;
- the operation of cold-storage warehouses under the Warehouse Receipt System;
- the operation of physical-commodity storage facilities under the Warehouse Receipt System.
This group does not cover:
- the operation of oil and natural gas storage, see group 52104;
- the operation of hazardous and toxic materials storage, see group 52105;
- the operation of ionizing radiation source storage, see group 52106;
- the operation of radioactive associated minerals storage, see group 52107.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas pengemba:
This group covers video game development activities, comprising the design of structure and content, as well as the writing, modification (including updates and patches), customisation, testing, and support of the computer program code required to create and implement
* video game software;
* video game applications;
* video game support software;
* video game middleware.
This subclass does not cover
- video game software publishing activities, see subclass 5821;
- video game websites or online gaming website activities, see subclass 6039;
- gambling website activities, see subclass 9200.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas pengolah:
This group covers the processing and tabulation of various types of data, including big data (whether structured, semi-structured, or unstructured) and satellite imagery or remote-sensing data. This activity covers some or all stages of data processing, comprising:
- data preparation (for example data entry, data migration, data cleaning, and data normalisation);
- the development of algorithms for data storage and processing;
- data processing and the production of customised reports based on data supplied by the client/data owner, carried out by a data controller or data processor, including data processing using blockchain or distributed ledger technology (DLT).
This group also covers the sharing of computing facilities for data processing and analysis, document digitisation (for the purpose of further data processing), big data management, and the provision of information services derived from processed data.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas pengoper:
This group covers the operation, maintenance, and/or provision of telecommunications networks using telecommunications infrastructure that employs electromagnetic waves for the wireless transmission of voice, data, text, audio, or video over the Earth's surface, including:
- the provision of telecommunications network infrastructure for fixed services (for example, fixed broadband connections, broadband wireless access, or microwave link communication systems) and mobile services (for example, cellular or radio-based communication systems such as radio trunking);
- the leasing of wireless network capacity to other telecommunications network operators or telecommunications service operators.

This group covers the operation, maintenance, and/or provision of telecommunications networks using cable-based infrastructure (both terrestrial and submarine cable) for the transmission of voice, data, text, audio, and video, including:
- the provision of cable access or distribution networks to subscribers (for example, homes/residences and offices);
- the provision of telecommunications networks connecting regions, islands, and countries (whether through terrestrial cable or submarine cable communication systems), buildings, telecommunications exchanges, cellular towers, data centers, or core networks, with either access points or subscribers (homes/residences and offices);
- the leasing of cable network capacity to other telecommunications network operators or telecommunications service operators.
This group does not cover network cable installation activities without the operation of facilities, see group 43212.

This group covers the operation, maintenance, and/or provision of telecommunications networks using satellite-based telecommunications infrastructure for general connectivity, including:
- the provision of satellite-based technology, such as geostationary satellites, medium- and low-orbit satellites, earth stations, satellite control centers, gateway exchanges, and other interconnecting networks;
- the provision of network connectivity (network services) using satellite infrastructure, including fixed services (for example, point-to-point communication such as cellular backhaul using VSAT, or very small aperture terminals) and mobile services, without being specific to any particular application;
- the leasing of satellite network capacity to other telecommunications network operators as well as telecommunications service operators.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas pengujia:
This group covers technical testing and analysis other than certification, inspection, verification, validation, and testing not elsewhere classified.
This group does not cover:
- various certification and technical analysis activities, see group 71201;
- various inspection and technical analysis activities, see group 71202;
- various verification, validation, and technical analysis activities, see group 71203;
- various testing and technical analysis activities, see group 71204;
- the operation of laboratory security and order separate from testing activities, see group 80110;
- technical testing using ionizing radiation sources (radioactive substances and ionizing radiation generators), see group 71204;
- the organization of proficiency testing among testing laboratories, see groups 71201, 71202, 71203, 71204 according to the testing activity concerned;
- the preparation and development of technical standards as a reference for technical testing and analysis, see group 74999.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas penilaia:
This group covers objective assessment activities aimed at examining and ensuring that products, processes, and systems meet technical requirements and function in accordance with their established objectives.
This group also covers:
- validation services, namely confirming, through the provision of objective evidence, that the requirements for an intended future use or application have been fulfilled, for example:
* project validation in the greenhouse gas (GHG) environmental information sector;
* validation of carbon economic value projects;
- verification services, namely confirming, through the provision of objective evidence, that specified requirements have been fulfilled, for example:
* organizational verification in the greenhouse gas (GHG) environmental information sector;
* emission verification and project verification in the greenhouse gas environmental information sector;
* verification of carbon economic value projects;
* verification of emission reports;
* verification of domestic component level (TKDN);
* verification of company benefit weight (BMP);
* verification in the financial sector;
* verification of carbon footprint.
This group also covers:
- industrial process commissioning, quality assurance, and quality control services.
This group does not cover:
- various certification and technical analysis activities, see group 71201;
- various inspection and technical analysis activities, see group 71202;
- various testing and technical analysis activities, see group 71204;

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas penjuala:
This group covers resale and intermediation services for other telecommunications, including:
- the resale of cable, wireless, and satellite telecommunications services (for example, buying and reselling network capacity), including telecommunications brokerage activities and the resale of prepaid calling cards, as well as related activities;
- intermediation services for cable, wireless, and satellite telecommunications activities, including agency activities for telecommunications operators, the sale of mobile telephone service packages on an agency basis, agency activities for the sale of wireless telephone service packages selling on behalf of wireless telecommunications operators, and agency activities for mobile virtual network operators (MVNO);
- the provision of telephone and internet access at facilities open to the public, such as telephone kiosks (wartel) and internet cafés (warnet).

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas penunjan:
This group covers support activities in producing and staging live performances of art and stage entertainment, such as drama/theater performances, music performances/concerts, opera, plays, pantomime, dance, regional art performances (wayang orang, lenong), bands, and orchestras.
This group covers the activities of producers, stage managers, art managers, stage-set designers, and builders/scenographers/set artists (stage visual art/stage artistry), scene-shifters, lighting engineers, and sound engineers (sound systems).
This group also covers:
- the activities of directors, dramaturges, artistic directors, film promoters, and program makers and supervisors;
- the activities of curators;
- the activities of literary critics and art critics.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas penyedia:
This group covers the provision and management of digital identity as a representation of an entity (individual, organization, or device) within electronic systems. These activities encompass consulting, planning, development, operation, and maintenance of digital identity systems, including:
- registration, verification, and validation of digital identities;
- management of digital credentials such as unique numbers, user accounts, electronic certificates, or tokens;
- authentication and authorization of users within digital systems;
- management of identity attributes, such as biographic, biometric, legal identifier, and unique identifier;
- provision of digital identity services with various levels of assurance based on risk.
This group also covers the integration of digital identity into clients' information systems as part of information security solutions.

...
- the operation of catering/banquet (adiboga) restaurants;
- the operation of ice cream/yoghurt outlets.

This group covers the activities of providing electronic certification and related services, both as an electronic certification provider (certificate authority) and as a provider of cryptography-technology-based services, including in this group, among others:
- the issuance and management of electronic certificates (digital certificates);
- electronic signature (digital signature) and electronic seal services;
- electronic timestamps;
- registered electronic delivery services;
- website authentication;
- preservation and validation of electronic signatures or seals;
- the integration of electronic certificate services into information systems or client applications as part of digital security and identity solutions.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas penyelen:
This group covers the provision of internet access services by operators (ISPs) that own and operate their own infrastructure (whether via cable, wireless, or satellite) to end users, including:
- the provision of internet access over telecommunications networks;
- the provision of internet access with dedicated connectivity (dedicated connection);
- the provision of internet access for public spaces (hotspot);
- the provision of internet access on board transport (on-board connectivity), such as inflight internet access (inflight connectivity).

This group covers the provision of audio distribution and streaming services on demand (audio on demand), including:
- music streaming, audio podcast, and audio book services;
- distribution and downloading services for digital audio content, whether third-party content or self-produced original content;
- distribution services for digital audio content on a subscription basis as well as an advertising basis.
This group does not cover:
- radio broadcasting service activities using analog signals, see group 60101;
- radio broadcasting service activities using digital signals, see group 60102;
- the production of radio content or audio recordings (non-live), see group 59201.

This group covers the activities of providing video distribution and streaming services on demand (video on demand), including
- video on-demand channel programming services;
- subscription-based or advertising-based video on demand distribution services;
- digital video content download services, whether third-party content or self-produced original content;
- view-only video game streaming services, intended only for watching, not for playing.
This group does not cover
- television broadcasting and programming services using analogue signals, see group 60201;
- television broadcasting and programming services using digital signals, see group 60202;
- video content production or video recording (non-live) activities, see subclass 5911.

This group covers the provision of television broadcasting and programming services using analogue signals within television broadcasting studios and facilities for the transmission of video to the public, affiliates, and/or subscribers via terrestrial, cable, or satellite means.
This group excludes:
- television broadcasting and programming services using digital signals, see group 60202;
- video-on-demand distribution and streaming services, see group 60203;
- the production of video content or video recordings (non-live), see subclass 5911.

This group covers the provision of television broadcasting and programming services using digital signals within television broadcasting studios and facilities for the transmission of video to the public, affiliates, and/or subscribers via terrestrial, cable, or satellite means.
This group also covers the live broadcasting of theatrical performances.
This group excludes:
- television broadcasting and programming services using analogue signals, see group 60201;
- video-on-demand distribution and streaming services, see group 60203;
- the production of video content or video recordings (non-live), see subclass 5911.

This group covers the provision of radio broadcasting services using analogue signals within radio broadcasting studios and facilities for the transmission of audio to the public, affiliates, and/or subscribers via terrestrial, cable, or satellite means.
This group excludes:
- radio broadcasting services using digital signals, see group 60102;
- audio-on-demand distribution and streaming services, see group 60103;
- the production of radio content or audio recordings (non-live), see group 59201.

This group covers the provision of radio broadcasting services using digital signals within radio broadcasting studios and facilities for the transmission of audio to the public, affiliates, and/or subscribers via terrestrial, cable, or satellite means.
This group also covers linear radio broadcasting services over the internet (not on user demand).
This group excludes:
- radio broadcasting services using analogue signals, see group 60101;
- audio-on-demand distribution and streaming services, see group 60103;
- the production of radio content or audio recordings (non-live), see group 59201.

This group covers the provision of special telecommunications services that use satellite technology and/or networks, whether for communication, navigation, monitoring, or remote sensing needs, but not as a provider of general connectivity, including:
- the provision of special telecommunications applications, such as satellite tracking, communication telemetry, and the operation of radar stations;
- the operation of satellite terminal stations (earth stations) and related facilities on the earth's surface that are operationally connected to one or more terrestrial communication systems, for the purpose of transmitting or receiving communications from satellites;
- the operation of satellites in orbit for remote sensing, navigation, and special telecommunications purposes, for example the operation of low earth orbit (LEO) telecommunications satellites.

This group covers the provision of other telecommunications services not elsewhere classified, including:
- the provision of advanced data services (SMS+, MMS+) without owning or operating one's own data transmission infrastructure;
- the provision of SMS push and notification services based on telephone networks (for example, bank SMS notifications or advertising).

This group covers the operation of ferry or coastal ports related to water transport for passengers, animals, or goods.
This group also covers:
- the operation of terminal facilities such as ports and docks;
- the operation of ferry shipping navigation;
- the inspection of cargo loads in freight and/or containers using ionising radiation sources (radioactive substances and ionising radiation generators);
- the operation of shipping services and berthing activities, mooring services, and pilotage and towage services.
This group excludes:
- cargo handling (loading and unloading), see group 52240;
- the operation of marina docks (tourism or recreational docks), see subclass 9329.

This group covers the operation of river, canal, lake, swamp, and other inland-water ports related to water transport for passengers, animals, or goods.
- the operation of terminal facilities such as ports and docks;
- the operation of river and lake shipping navigation;
- the inspection of cargo loads in freight and/or containers using ionising radiation sources (radioactive substances and ionising radiation generators);
- the operation of shipping services and berthing activities, mooring services, and pilotage and towage services.
This group excludes:
- cargo handling (loading and unloading), see group 52240;
- the operation of marina docks (tourism or recreational docks), see subclass 9329.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas penyimpa:
This group covers the storage of goods that require storage facilities suited to the nature/characteristics of hazardous and toxic materials.
This group also covers:
- the operation of cold storage for hazardous and toxic goods;
- the operation of hazardous and toxic goods storage in free-trade zones;
- the operation of hazardous and toxic goods storage under the warehouse-receipt system;
- the operation of storage facilities for hazardous and toxic physical commodities.
This group excludes:
- the operation of oil and gas storage, see group 52104;
- the operation of storage for ionising radiation sources and radioactive goods, see groups 52106 and 52107.

This group covers the storage of ionising radiation sources (radioactive substances and ionising radiation generators).
This group also covers:
- the operation of ionising radiation source storage under the warehouse-receipt system;
- the operation of refrigerated warehouses for the storage of ionising radiation sources;
- the operation of ionising radiation source storage in free-trade zones;
- the operation of storage facilities for ionising radiation source physical commodities (radioactive substances and ionising radiation generators).
This group excludes:
- the operation of storage for naturally occurring radioactive goods, see group 52107.

This group covers storage activities comprising the receipt, collection, holding, and dispatch of petroleum, fuel oil, gaseous fuel, and/or processed products at locations above and/or below ground and/or above the water surface.
This group also covers:
- the operation of oil and gas storage in free-trade zones;
- the storage of carbon-free fuels as energy carriers (hydrogen, ammonia, and other compounds), whether in the form of geological formations, compressed gas, solid form, liquid form, or other forms;
- the operation of cold storage for oil and gas;
- the operation of oil and gas storage under the warehouse-receipt system;
- the operation of storage facilities for oil and gas physical commodities.

This group covers the storage of naturally occurring radioactive substances classified as naturally occurring radioactive material (NORM) or radioactive associated minerals derived from the mining and processing of oil and gas, phosphate, tin, zircon, and the like.
This group also covers:
- the operation of radioactive associated mineral storage under the warehouse-receipt system;
- the operation of refrigerated warehouses for the storage of radioactive associated minerals;
- the operation of radioactive associated mineral storage in free-trade zones;
- the operation of storage facilities for radioactive associated mineral physical commodities.
This group excludes:
- the operation of ionising radiation source storage facilities, see group 52106.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas perantar:
This group covers intermediation activities in postal and courier services, namely connecting clients with service providers in return for a fee or commission, without the intermediary itself performing the postal or courier service directly. This intermediation may be carried out through digital platforms or non-digital channels (face-to-face, including door-to-door services, telephone, mail, etc.). The fee or commission may be received from the client or from the postal/courier service provider. Revenue from these intermediation activities may also include other sources, such as advertising income.
This group covers:
- any intermediation service performed by a third party in respect of the access points of postal and courier service providers, and offered to business and household clients;
- the conduct of the collection and processing of items, whether domestic or international, without performing transport and delivery;
- collection and processing or transport and delivery activities performed under assignment from a postal and courier operator, without operating services in one's own name or entering into direct contracts with the public.
This group excludes:
- food delivery services, see subclass 5320;
- the operation of online platforms enabling the public to order food delivery, see group 53301;
- the home delivery of ready-to-eat food by a unit that also cooks it, see division 56;
- financial intermediation services, such as payments through post offices, see subclass 6419.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas perbanka:
This group covers banking activities that primarily accept deposits of precious metals (such as gold or silver) in the form of bars or coins and extend loans of such precious metals, conducted on the basis of sharia principles.
This group excludes:
- conventional bullion banking activities, see group 64996;
- bullion trading on one's own account, see group 64994;
- bullion trading on behalf of others (brokerage), see group 66129;
- bullion custody or safekeeping activities, see group 66132.

This group covers banking activities that primarily accept deposits of precious metals (such as gold or silver) in the form of bars or coins and extend loans of such precious metals, conducted on a conventional basis.
This group excludes:
- sharia bullion banking activities, see group 64997;
- bullion trading on one's own account, see group 64994;
- bullion trading on behalf of others (brokerage), see group 66129;
- bullion custody or safekeeping activities, see group 66132.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas pergudan:
This group covers warehousing and storage activities other than warehouse-receipt-system warehouses, cold storage, bonded warehouses, oil and gas storage, hazardous and toxic goods storage, ionising radiation source storage, and radioactive associated mineral storage.
This group also covers:
- the management or operation of warehouses, comprising enclosed warehouses, silos/tanks, and other warehouses, serving to store goods before they are shipped to their final destination;
- container depot activities involving the storage and/or stacking of containers, which may be equipped with other facilities;
- warehouse services used for trade through electronic systems (PMSE);
- the operation of storage tanks for storing products in liquid and gaseous form, such as water and liquefied gas;
- the operation of storage facilities for physical commodities not elsewhere classified.
This group excludes:
- the operation of oil and gas storage, see group 52104.

This group covers warehousing activities forming part of the customs territory that is accorded special treatment as though located outside the customs territory.
This group also covers:
- the operation of storage facilities for physical commodities in bonded zones.
This group excludes:
- the operation of warehouse-receipt-system warehouses in free-trade zones, see group 52101;
- the operation of cold storage in free-trade zones, see group 52102;
- the operation of oil and gas storage in free-trade zones, see group 52104;
- the operation of hazardous and toxic goods storage in free-trade zones, see group 52105;
- the operation of ionising radiation source storage in free-trade zones, see group 52106;
- the operation of radioactive associated mineral storage in free-trade zones, see group 52107.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas perwakil:
This group covers the operational representation of cargo-only air transport in selling and marketing air-transport services, including all aspects of marketing.
This group excludes:
- the operational representation of air transport for passengers, see group 52323;
- aircraft ticket sales agency activities for passengers, see group 52321;
- airline representative office activities without conducting sales, see group 70100;
- the marketing of air-transport services as part of advertising, see group 73100.

This group covers the operational representation of passenger air transport in selling and marketing air-transport services, including all aspects of marketing.
This group excludes:
- the operational representation of cargo-only air transport, see group 52313;
- aircraft ticket sales agency activities for passengers, see group 52321;
- airline representative office activities without conducting sales, see group 70100;
- the marketing of air-transport services as part of advertising, see group 73100.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas sertifik:
This group covers the certification of products, processes, services, and systems, comprising:
- quality management system certification;
- environmental management system certification;
- food safety management system certification;
- hazard analysis and critical control point (HACCP) system certification;
- energy management system certification;
- medical device management system certification;
- supply-chain security management system certification;
- laboratory biorisk management system certification;
- anti-bribery management system certification;
- information technology service management system certification;
- compliance management system certification;
- sustainable event management system certification;
- tourism activity certification;
- ecolabel certification;
- information security management system certification not related to the information security of applications, software, or networks, such as information security management and information security processes;
- occupational safety and health management system certification (SMK3);
- organic system certification;
- sustainable forest-products forest management system certification;
- timber legality certification;
- Indonesian Sustainable Palm Oil (ISPO) certification;
- organiser of umrah and special hajj certification;
- sustainable forest management certification;
- business entity certification;
- independent appraiser and verifier certification;
- IndoGAP certification;
- product halal certification;
- organic food certification;
- Indonesia forestry certification cooperation certification;
- green industry certification;
- construction services certification;
- warehouse certification;
- hydrogen safety certification;
- ship certification;
- nuclear product certification, such as ionising radiation sources, equipment related to nuclear use (reactor control rods and the like), and radiation protection equipment;
- industrial certification, such as industrial quality and products, green industry, domestic component level, industry 4.0, and industrial activity certification.
This group excludes:
- certification related to penetration testing of computer systems, ethical hacking, and cyber security, see division 62;
- technical testing and analysis activities without performing certification, see subclasses 71202, 71203, 71204, and 71209;
- person certification activities, see subclass 8569;
- educational organisation management system certification activities, see subclass 8569.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas situs je:
This group covers the activities of social networking sites and platforms for the distribution (sharing) of content or other information, including blog and wiki sites, video game (online game) sites, and the provision of electronic books (e-books) for download not connected with publishing activities.
This group also covers intermediation service activities for the trade of digital video game goods not connected with publishing, such as the sale of vouchers, credits, in-game items, or premium access through a distribution platform or digital marketplace.
This group does not cover:
- electronic book (e-book) publishing activities, see subclass 5811;
- news agency activities, see subclass 6031;
- vlog (video blogging) creation activities, see subclass 5911;
- independent actor activities (including influencers in vlogs), see subclass 9020;
- independent blogger activities, see subclass 9011;
- video game and other software publishing activities, see group 582;
- video game streaming site activities that are view-only, see subclass 6020;
- the provision of computing infrastructure and hosting services, see subclass 6310;
- web search portal activities, see subclass 6390;
- online gambling site activities, see subclass 9200;
- retail trade intermediation service activities, see subclass 4790;
- passenger transport intermediation service activities, see subclass 5232;
- accommodation intermediation service activities, see subclass 5540;
- library and archive activities, see group 911.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas swasta d:
This group covers private-sector activities in the operation and conservation of heritage sites/remains resulting from human intervention in the environment, whether in the form of landscapes, parks, buildings or sites (built cultural heritage or natural heritage) that hold significant value for history, science and culture, and are deemed to hold significant value for history, science, education, religion and culture, such as temples, the tombs of saints (wali), and historic mosques.
This group also covers private-sector activities in:
- the operation and conservation of historic sites and buildings;
- the operation and conservation of archaeological sites open to visitors.
This group does not cover
- the renovation and restoration of historic sites and buildings, see category F;
- architectural activities relating to the rehabilitation or restoration of cultural-heritage property, see 7110;
- archaeological excavation, see 7220;
- the restoration of works of art and museum collection objects and the preventive conservation of works of art where not carried out by units classified in group 912, see group 913.

Kelompok ini mencakup aktivitas transpor:
This group covers the transport of passengers, or of passengers and cargo, by aircraft on fixed and regular flight routes and schedules, against payment of certain published tariffs.
This group does not cover
- charter flights for passengers, see group 51102;
- sightseeing flights, see group 51102;
- the renting of air transport with operator for passenger transport purposes, see group 51102;
- the renting of air transport without operator, see group 77313;
- passenger transport by flying clubs for training purposes, see subgroup 8553;
- air ambulances, see group 869.

This group covers the transport of passengers, or of passengers and cargo, by aircraft on non-fixed and irregular flight routes and schedules, against payment of a tariff agreed between the air transport service provider and the service user and not published.
This group covers
- charter flights for passengers;
- sightseeing flights.
This subclass also covers
- the renting of air transport with operator for passenger transport purposes.
This subclass does not cover
- scheduled air transport for passengers on fixed routes and schedules, see group 51101;
- the renting of air transport without operator, see group 77313;
- passenger transport by flying clubs for training purposes, see subgroup 8553;
- air ambulances, see group 869.

This group covers passenger transport activities using non-motorised vehicles.
This group also covers
- horse-cart transport (delman/bendi/andong/dokar);
- pedicab (becak) transport;
- bicycle-taxi (ojek sepeda) transport;
- non-motorised rental transport for passengers.
This group does not cover
- non-motorised transport for passengers in tourist areas, see group 49292;
- non-motorised transport for goods, see group 49233.

This group covers passenger transport activities by sea using vessels between domestic ports and ports abroad, operating on fixed and regular routes (liner) with a schedule, or on non-fixed and irregular routes (tramper).
This group also covers
- the renting of sea transport together with its operator;
- international community shipping (pelayaran rakyat) sea transport for passengers using sailing vessels, traditional motorboats and motorised sailing vessels of a certain size;
- other international sea transport for passengers, such as pioneer (perintis) transport.

Kelompok ini mencakup angkutan barang de:
This group covers the transport of goods using at least two different modes of transport, on the basis of a single contract as a multimodal transport document, from one place where the goods are received by the multimodal operator to a specified place for delivery of the goods to the consignee of the multimodal transport. This group also covers
- freight-forwarding services, warehousing services, cargo-consolidation services, the provision of cargo space, and customs clearance as part of multimodal transport.
This group does not cover
- freight-forwarding services carried out by a separate unit, see group 52311;
- warehousing services carried out by a separate unit, see subclass 5210;
- customs-clearance services carried out by a separate unit, see group 52319.

Kelompok ini mencakup berbagai macam lay:
This group covers a wide variety of services generally provided to commercial clients. This group covers activities that require professional, scientific and technical skills, but does not cover ongoing routine business that is generally of short duration.
This group covers
- business broker activities, namely arranging the purchase and sale of small and medium-sized businesses, including professional practices, but excluding real estate brokers;
- valuation other than for real estate and insurance (for antiques, jewellery, etc.);
- auditing of freight bills and transport rate information;
- security consulting;
- consulting in the field of occupational safety at the workplace;
- agronomy consultancy services;
- environmental consultancy services;
- energy-saving advisory services;
- other technical consultancy;
- consultancy services other than architectural, engineering and management consultancy;
- construction economist activities.
This group also covers
- activities carried out by agents and agencies on behalf of individuals usually involving engagement in films or motion pictures, theatre productions or other entertainment or sporting attractions and the placement of books, games, works of art, photographs, etc., with publishers, producers, etc.;
- economist services for construction projects, namely construction economists;
- supervisory board activities;
- activities of preparing and developing technical standards as a reference for technical testing and analysis.
This group does not cover
- the activities of commission agents, commodity brokers and other wholesale traders who trade on behalf of others without at any time owning the goods being intermediated, see subclass 4610;
- intermediary service activities (for retail trade), see subclass 4790;
- real estate broker activities, see subclass 6821;
- bookkeeping activities, see subclass 6920;
- management and consulting activities, see subclass 7020;
- architectural and engineering consultancy activities, see subclass 7110;
- quantity surveyor activities, see subclass 7110;
- industrial and machine design, see subclass 7110 and class 741;
- testing and control of animals related to food production, see subclass 7120;
- sales promotion service activities, see subclass 7330;
- advertising display and other advertisement design, see subclass 7310;
- the making of stands and structures as well as other display stands, see subclass 7310;
- convention and trade fair activities, see subclass 8230;
- independent auctioneer activities, see subclass 8299;
- administration of loyalty programmes, see subclass 8299;
- consumer credit and debt counselling, see subclass 8299;
- environmental engineering activities, see subclass 7110;
- patent broker activities, see subclass 7491;
- management of industrial property rights, such as patents, licences, trademarks, and franchises, see subclass 7491;
- management of intellectual property rights such as copyrights and the income therefrom, see subclass 7491;
- medical doctor consultancy, see subclass 8620.

Kelompok ini mencakup entitas legal, tid:
This group covers legal entities, not acting as collective investment schemes, engaged in the holding of securities, estates and other financial assets, without managing them, on behalf of shareholders or beneficiaries. Their portfolios are tailored to achieve specific investment characteristics, for example diversification, risk, rate of return and price volatility. These entities earn interest, dividends and other property income, but have little or no employment and no revenue from the sale of services. This group covers
- trusts, estates and agencies, on behalf of beneficiaries under the terms of a trust agreement, will, or agency agreement;
- the activities of trusts, estates and similar financial entities;
- the activities of companies that hold financial assets for individuals and families (family trusts).
This group also covers
- the activities of holding companies that do not hold or control equity;
- venture companies whose source of financing is solely from shares and that do not receive a fee.
This group does not cover
- raising funds by issuing shares or units and acting as a collective investment scheme, see groups 64310 and 64320;
- conducting securities transactions by issuing financial instruments, see subgroup 6494;
- trusts, estates and agency accounts that earn income by selling goods and services, see the KBLI classification according to their principal activity;
- trustees representing securities holders on a fee or contract basis, see subgroup 6619.

Kelompok ini mencakup instalasi atau pem:
This group covers the specialised installation or fitting of industrial machinery and equipment. However, the installation of equipment that forms part of a building or the like, for example the installation or fitting of escalators, electrical cabling, burglar alarms, or air-conditioning (AC) systems, is classified under construction activities.
This group also covers the assembly/integration of industrial equipment and systems, both hardware and software, whether partially or wholly, on a large or small scale.
This group covers
- the installation of industrial machinery in a factory;
- the installation of industrial process control or monitoring equipment and assemblies;
- the installation of other industrial equipment, such as communications equipment, mainframe and similar computers, irradiation equipment, as well as medical-gas and electromedical equipment;
- millwright activities;
- machine rigging;
- the installation of bowling-alley equipment;
- the installation of warehouse machinery and equipment;
- the installation of large-scale racking and warehouses (not part of a building);
- the installation of stand-alone charging stations;
- the installation of industrial facilities, such as loading and discharging stations, winding shafts, chemical plants, iron foundries, blast furnaces, and coke ovens;
- the installation of treatment systems and purification equipment for converting seawater, brackish water and fresh water into pure water at power plants.
This group does not cover
- dismantling services for large-scale machinery and equipment, see group 33202;
- the installation of wall-box charging stations, see category F;
- the construction of complete warehouses, see group 410;
- the installation of air-conditioning (AC) systems, see subgroup 4322;
- the installation of elevator, escalator, automatic door and vacuum-cleaning systems, see subgroup 4329;
- the installation of doors, house stairs, shop fittings, furniture and the like, see subgroup 4330;
- the erection of structural steel for warehouse storage racks, see subgroup 4390;
- personal computer (PC) installation services, see subgroup 6290.

Kelompok ini mencakup jasa intermediasi:
This group covers intermediation services in wholesale trade, namely facilitating transactions between sellers and buyers for the ordering of goods in return for a fee or commission, without providing or taking ownership of the intermediated goods and services. The intermediation activity may be carried out through digital platforms or non-digital channels. The fee or commission may be received from either the seller or the buyer. Income from intermediation activities may also include other sources, such as advertising revenue.
This group also covers
- the activities of commission agents, commodity brokers, and other wholesalers trading on behalf of others without holding title to the intermediated goods;
- activities that bring sellers and buyers together;
- activities of carrying out transactions on behalf of companies, including online;
- the activities of buying centers, if they act only as an intermediary and do not hold title to the intermediated goods;
- the activities of auction houses for wholesale trade;
- commission-based agency for wholesale trade in radioactive substances and ionizing-radiation generators;
- the operation of commodity auction markets for wholesale trade.
This group does not cover
- wholesale trade on own account, see groups 462 to 469;
- the activities of commission agents that hold title to goods, even though they act on behalf of third parties, see groups 462 to 469;
- the activities of opaque intermediaries (intermediaries acting on behalf of third parties), see groups 462 to 469;
- intermediation service activities for retail trade, see group 479;
- intermediation service activities for real estate, see subgroup 6821;
- goods-search websites that connect customers and sellers.

Kelompok ini mencakup jasa keagenan peng:
This group covers agency services for handling the interests of sea-transport vessels, comprising
- reporting the planned and actual arrival and departure of vessels;
- handling port services;
- appointing a stevedoring company;
- completing vessel documents;
- booking and disbursement of cargo;
- issuing the bill of lading for and on behalf of the shipowner;
- arranging the bunkering of fuel oil and fresh water;
- meeting equipment and provisioning needs;
- other agency services agreed between the shipowner or vessel operator and the party carrying out the vessel agency activities.
This group also covers
- brokerage services for handling the operations of fishing/fish-carrier vessels at sea.

Kelompok ini mencakup jasa pracetak dan:
This group covers prepress and premedia services, as well as bookbinding and related services.
This group covers
- binding of printed sheets, for example into books, brochures, magazines, catalogues and the like, by folding, assembling, stitching, gluing, collating, adhesive binding, trimming and gold stamping;
- composing, typesetting, phototypesetting, prepress data input into a form usable in various printing processes and represented in other visual media, including scanning and optical character recognition, as well as electronic make-up;
- preparation of data files for multimedia applications (printing on paper, CD-ROM, internet);
- platemaking services, including image setting and plate setting (for letterpress and offset printing processes);
- cylinder preparation: engraving or etching of cylinders for intaglio/gravure printing;
- plate processing: "computer to plate" (CTP) (including photopolymer plates);
- preparation of plates and dies for relief printing and stamping;
- preparation of technical artwork, such as the preparation of stones and wood blocks for lithography; presentation media of sketches, layouts, dummies, and the like; production of proofs;
- commercial bookbinding, sample mounting, and post-press services in support of printing activities, for example binding and finishing of books, brochures, magazines, and catalogues, by folding, cutting and trimming, assembling, stitching, thread binding, adhesive binding, cutting and mounting of covers, gluing, collating, gathering, gold stamping; spiral binding and plastic-wire binding;
- binding and finishing of printed paper or paperboard, by folding, stamping, drilling, perforating, embossing, mounting, gluing, and laminating;
- finishing services for CD-ROMs;
- mailing finishing services, such as customization and preparation of envelopes;
- other finishing activities, such as die-cutting, embossing or stamping, and Braille transcription.
This group does not cover
- graphic design activities for visual content to communicate information using printing presses and other media, see subgroup 7419.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan\n- pemasa:
This group covers the activities of
- installation of various foundations and piles;
- concrete pouring and reinforcement of foundations for buildings, roads/bridges, water structures, docks, offshore structures and the like as part of the work covered under building construction and other civil engineering works;
- correction of tilt, displacement, and settlement in building and civil structures;
- translation, rotation, and/or elevation of an entire building structure as a whole, including heritage buildings;
- structural strengthening for capacity upgrading (such as the addition of floors), seismic retrofitting, and change of building use;
- replacement of critical primary structural elements (columns, beams, slabs) in buildings.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan\n- penyep:
This group covers the activities of
- metal plating, anodizing, and so forth;
- heat treatment of metal;
- deburring, sandblasting, tumbling, and cleaning of metal;
- colouring and engraving or chasing of metal;
- non-metallic coating of metal, such as coating with plastic, enamel or porcelain, and lacquer/varnish;
- hardening and polishing of metal;
- drilling, machining, milling, abrading, forming, turning, broaching, levelling, sawing, grinding, sharpening, buffing, welding, splicing, and so forth as part of metalworking;
- laser cutting or writing on metal.
This group also covers
- plating, polishing, colouring, engraving, hardening, buffing, welding, cutting, and various specialized working services on metal or metal products.
This subgroup does not cover
- the activities of farriers, see subgroup 0162;
- rolling of precious metal onto base metal or other metals, see subgroup 2420.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan aktivitas:
This group covers industrial design activities to produce communication-equipment and electronics products. This group covers
- design for information-technology, communication, and control products;
- design for sound- or image-recording products;
- design for data-storage products;
- design for power-generation and motor-drive products;
- design for power-storage and power-amplifier products;
- design for electricity-distribution and -control products;
- design for refrigeration machines, washing machines, as well as drying and cleaning machines.
This design activity is also carried out through specialized software.

This group covers industrial design activities to produce products in the household equipment and furniture industry. This group covers
- design for glassware products, tableware, and cooking, serving, and food-storage utensils;
- design for fireplace fittings products;
- design for bedding, table, and chair products;
- design for storage furniture (fixtures) products;
- design for mirror and frame products;
- design for clothes-hanger products;
- design for curtain and drape products;
- design for wall/table ornaments, vases, and pots;
- design for medal and belt products;
- design for flag and festival-decoration products;
- design for artificial flower, fruit, and plant products.
These design activities are also carried out using specialized software.

This group covers industrial-design activities to produce products within an industry not yet covered in groups 74111 through 74118, such as:
- design for timekeeping equipment, measuring equipment, and office equipment;
- design for products used for brushing;
- design for tools and hardware;
- design for photographic, cinematographic, and optical equipment;
- design for musical instruments;
- design for office stationery;
- design for sales and advertising equipment;
- design for hunting and fishing equipment;
- design for fluid-distribution products, ventilation and air-conditioning equipment, and heating equipment;
- design for solid-fuel products;
- design for lighting products;
- design for construction elements;
- design for fire-fighting equipment;
- design for animal-care products;
- design for food products;
- design for tobacco and cigarette products;
- design for craft products.
These design activities are also carried out through specialized software.

This group covers industrial design activities to produce packaging products. This group covers
- design for bottles, tubes, containers, waste/scrap bins;
- design for cans, drums, storage barrels, boxes;
- design for closures, baskets, wooden crates, pallets, bags, capsules.
The design activities here are also carried out by means of specialised software.

This group covers industrial design activities for producing textile, fashion, and garment products. These design activities are also carried out using specialised software.
This group covers
- design for fabric and woven products;
- design for crocheted products;
- design for clothing and underwear products;
- design for headwear products;
- design for footwear, socks, stockings, and shoelace products;
- design for bag, suitcase, and trunk products;
- design for necktie, shawl, scarf, and handkerchief products;
- design for glove, umbrella, walking-stick, and fan products;
- design for ribbon, hair-tie, clothing-accessory, and other ornament products;
- design for jewellery products.

This group covers industrial design activities to produce products, production support equipment, and components in the manufacture of transport equipment and machinery. This group covers
- design for bicycle products and animal-drawn vehicles;
- design for handcart, pushcart, baby carriage, wheelchair, and stretcher products;
- design for rail vehicle products;
- design for chairlift and ski lift products;
- design for elevator and lifting equipment products;
- design for motor vehicle, ship and aircraft, and spacecraft products;
- design for tyre and anti-slip chain products and vehicle components and accessories;
- design for machinery, pump, and compressor products;
- design for agricultural and construction machinery as well as textile machinery products.
These design activities are also performed through specialized software.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan angkutan:
This group covers passenger transport activities on rivers, canals, lakes, swamps, and other inland waters carried out on a fixed and regular route network, with a fixed timetable and scheduled service.
This group covers
- transport services within a regency/city on inland waters;
- transport services between regencies/cities within a province on inland waters;
- cross-border transport services between countries on inland waters;
- inter-provincial transport services on inland waters.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan atau usah:
This group covers the activity or business of staging artistic performances and live stage entertainment, whether by individuals or groups, such as drama/theatre performances, music recitals/concerts, opera, plays, pantomime, dance, and regional artistic performances (wayang orang, lenong).
This group also covers:
- group performance activities such as circus, orchestra, or band;
- the activities of performing artists such as actors (including stand-up comedians), dancers, singers/musicians (including solo-organ acts), backing singers, and conductors;
- the activities of photographic models;
- the activities of influencers, content creators, and YouTubers who appear in vlogs/content;
- the activities of independent musicians and actors who appear in various kinds of video and audiovisual content;
- the operation of arts facilities used for the artists' own group;
- wayang performance activities by a dalang (puppeteer);
- monologue activities, theatre/drama script reading (dramatic reading), and poetry set to music.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan bank sent:
This group covers the activities of the central bank, which has the duties to
- issue and manage printed and digital money;
- set and implement monetary policy;
- supervise and control the money supply;
- accept deposits used for clearing between monetary intermediaries;
- supervise monetary operations and other financial activities conducted by banks or non-banks, namely activities in the fields of monetary policy, macroprudential policy, payment systems, the money market, and the foreign exchange market (except supervision conducted by other entities);
- manage the country's foreign exchange reserves;
- act as banker to the government;
- set and implement macroprudential policy.
This group also covers
- central banking system activities;
- regulating and safeguarding the smooth operation of the payment system and the management of the rupiah currency.
This group does not cover
- financial supervision activities other than insurance and pension funds not conducted by the central bank (see 6611);
- financial supervision activities for insurance and pension funds not conducted by the central bank (see 6629);
- financial regulation relating to business conduct and consumer protection as well as other broader financial regulatory activities (see 8414);
- the activities of international organizations, for example the IMF and the World Bank (see 9900).

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan dari peru:
This group covers the activities of holding companies, for example units that hold the assets (owning and managing the equity level) of one or more subsidiaries and are responsible solely as the owner of the subsidiaries. Holding companies in this group do not provide other services to the companies whose equity is held by the holding company; for example, the holding company does not direct and manage other units. These holding companies may carry out activities such as control, financial consolidation, and being responsible for the activities of each subsidiary, but not the active management of those subsidiaries, for example a financial-conglomerate holding company.
This group does not cover
- transacting in financial markets for the holding company's own account, see subclass 6499;
- the activity of asset management on a fee or contract basis, see subclass 6630;
- the provision of managerial services, for example strategic planning, decision-making, and head-office administrative services, see subclass 7010;
- the active management of companies and corporate units, strategic planning, and decision-making of the company, see subclass 7010.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan hiburan d:
This group covers entertainment and recreation activities not covered in 93291 to 93297, such as:
- the operation of ski hills, whether standalone or combined with ski lifts;
- the rental of recreation and entertainment equipment that forms an inseparable part of recreational facilities, the operation of fairs and natural recreation shows, and other entertainment and recreation activities;
- the activities of producers or promoters of live entertainment and recreation events other than sports or arts performances, with or without facilities;
- the activities of independent animators at entertainment and recreation facilities;
- the operation of computer rooms for playing computer games;
- the operation of self-service entertainment equipment such as rocking chairs, horses, cars, and spaceships;
- the operation of airsoft and paintball fields;
- virtual reality (VR) or geolocation games/experiences;
- the operation of billiard halls/auditoriums;
- the operation of escape rooms;
- the operation of bowling halls/auditoriums;
- light and sound shows;
- the activities of underwater tour guides;
- the manufacture and display of fireworks;
- the operation of picnic grounds not related to nature conservation;
- the operation of laser games;
- the operation of mechanical rides, games, and shows by independent providers, for example at fairgrounds, folk festivals, and Christmas markets;
- the technical planning, provision, arrangement, and operation of audiovisual equipment and special effects related to the management of live entertainment and recreation events;
- the management of space tourism and astronomy tourism.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan jasa keua:
This group covers other financial service activities not elsewhere classified:
- the activities of financial vehicle corporations (FVCs) other than securitisation;
- the writing of swaps, options, and other hedging arrangements;
- securitisation transactions of assets other than loans by issuing financial instruments;
- the issuance of digital financial assets and their associated liabilities on one's own account, for example crypto assets;
- other financial service activities not elsewhere covered.
This group does not cover:
- transacting in financial markets on one's own account, see group 64994;
- securitisation, see group 64940;
- activities acting as a counterparty for the clearing and settlement of transactions, see group 64993.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan jasa pemb:
This group covers cleaning services and the management of other waste and refuse by the government and the private sector, such as:
- the decontamination of soil and groundwater at polluted sites, both in situ and ex situ, using mechanical, chemical, or biological methods;
- the decontamination of industrial sites or plants, including nuclear sites and installations;
- the decontamination and cleaning of surface water following pollution, for example due to the accumulation of pollutants or other chemicals;
- the cleanup of oil spills and other pollution on land, in surface water, in oceans and seas, including coastlines;
- the abatement of asbestos, lead paint, and other toxic materials; other specialised pollution-control activities;
- disinfection spraying and other similar cleaning services.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan jasa repa:
This group covers the repair of other household and personal goods not elsewhere classified, such as bicycles, jewellery, watches, clocks and their parts, sports equipment (except sporting firearms), books, musical instruments, toys and similar goods, and other personal and household goods, including piano tuning and key duplication.
This group covers:
- repair and maintenance of bicycles, electric bicycles, monowheels, hoverboards and kick scooters;
- repair and alteration or modification of jewellery;
- repair of watches, clocks and their parts, such as watch straps, watch cases and movement frames of various materials;
- repair of sports equipment (except sporting firearms);
- repair of books;
- repair of musical instruments;
- repair of toys and similar goods;
- repair of other personal and household goods;
- piano tuning.
This group does not cover:
- engraving of metals, see subclass 2592;
- repair of sporting and recreational firearms, see subclass 3311;
- repair of power-driven hand tools, see subclass 3312;
- restoration of organs and other historical musical instruments, see subclass 3319;
- repair of time locks, time/date stamps and other time-recording equipment, see subclass 3313.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan klub olah:
This group covers the activities of professional, semi-professional, or amateur sports clubs that give their members the opportunity to take part in sporting activities, whether or not they provide premises and facilities for sport, other than the sports clubs covered in groups 93121 to 93128.
This group covers the operation of sports clubs such as:
- winter sports clubs;
- chess clubs;
- athletics clubs, such as running, jumping, throwing;
- shooting clubs;
- e-sports clubs;
- card-game clubs, such as trump/bridge clubs.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan konstruks:
This group covers other specialised construction activities not elsewhere classified in groups 43901 to 43905 that require specialised skills or equipment, such as:
- moisture-proofing and waterproofing work, including waterproofing work on various types of storage tanks;
- dehumidifying of buildings;
- shaft sinking;
- installation of chimneys and ovens for industrial purposes;
- work requiring climbing skills and the use of related equipment, for example work on tall buildings;
- underground work;
- installation of road safety barriers and traffic signs;
- road painting and other markings;
- installation of noise-reduction walls, for example along roads;
- installation of street furniture;
- conservation, repair, and restoration of cultural heritage buildings;
- concrete pavement work; asphalt pavement work; granular pavement work;
- drilling and pressurised cement injection construction work;
- structural concrete work; post-tensioned concrete construction work;
- installation of fire-resistant structures (furnaces, annealing units, flares, incinerators) for residential and non-residential buildings as well as other civil structures.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan kreasi ak:
This group covers creative industrial design activities to produce strategic and defence products. This group also covers:
- design for national defence products;
- design for military products;
- design for weapons products;
- design for security and policing products;
- design for disaster emergency-response products.
The design activities of this group are also carried out using specialized software.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan organisas:
This group covers the activities of religious organizations engaged in conducting religious activities and the propagation of religion.
This group covers the activities of religious organizations or individuals providing services directly to congregations worshipping in mosques, churches, temples, or other places of worship, the activities of organizations providing monastic services, religious retreat activities, and other religious activities. This group also covers religious funeral service activities.
This group does not cover:
- education provided by such organizations, see section 85;
- health activities provided by such organizations, see section 86;
- social work activities provided by such organizations, see sections 87, 88.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan pascapane:
This group covers post-harvest activities on a fee or contract basis, comprising:
- the preparation of agricultural products for the primary market, such as cleaning, sorting, grading, hulling, sun-drying, and disinfection;
- the ginning of cotton;
- the preparation of tobacco leaves, such as sun-drying;
- the preparation of cocoa beans, such as shelling;
- the waxing of fruit;
- the natural drying of fruit, vegetables, spices, and medicinal herbs;
- the sorting, cleaning, and cutting of medicinal herbs;
- the retting of textile fiber plants (jute, flax, coir, etc.) not connected with the cultivation of those plants;
- the artificial ripening of fruit as a service, such as the ripening of bananas.
This group does not cover:
- the preparation of agricultural products by farmers, see groups 011, 012, or 013;
- post-harvest activities aimed at improving seed quality, see subgroup 0164;
- the cleaning and redrying of tobacco, see subgroup 1200;
- marketing by commission traders and cooperative associations, see section 46;
- the wholesale trade of agricultural products, whether or not accompanied by preparation to improve product quality, see subgroup 4620;
- the processing of grains to produce oil, see subgroup 1041;
- research to develop or engineer new seed varieties, see subgroup 7210.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan peleburan:
This group covers the smelting, alloying, and casting of non-ferrous metals in basic forms, such as castings of copper and its alloys, castings of aluminium and its alloys, and castings of nickel and its alloys. This group also covers:
- casting of semi-finished products of aluminium, magnesium, titanium, zinc, and others;
- casting of light metal castings;
- casting of heavy metal castings;
- casting of precious metal castings;
- die-casting of non-ferrous metals.

This group covers the smelting, mixing, and casting of ferrous metals and steel, producing castings in rough form, such as cast iron, cast steel, and cast alloy steel. This group also covers:
- casting of semi-finished iron products;
- casting of grey cast iron;
- casting of spheroidal graphite cast iron;
- casting of malleable cast iron;
- casting of semi-finished steel products;
- casting of cast steel;
- manufacture of tubes, pipes, and hollow profiles, as well as tube and pipe fittings made of cast iron;
- manufacture of seamless steel tubes and pipes by centrifugal casting;
- manufacture of tube and pipe fittings made of cast steel.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan pemasanga:
This group covers the installation of other building fixtures and the installation, maintenance, and repair of other civil-structure fixtures, such as:
- installation of lightning rods;
- installation of integrated central vacuum cleaning systems;
- installation of heat, sound, or vibration insulation, such as acoustic cladding panels, glass wool, and rock wool.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan pembangun:
This group covers the construction, maintenance, and/or reconstruction of jetty and trestle structures, sea, river, and lake port infrastructure, and the like for non-fishing ports, including land-fill works in waters or coastal areas for the construction of port structures.
This group also covers:
- construction of waterways or canals, ports and river-route facilities, marinas, docks, locks (Panama Canal lock, Hoover Dam), and others;
- dredging or normalization and maintenance of rivers, ports, swamps, lakes, navigation channels, basins, and canals, whether of light, medium, or heavy work nature;
- construction of port support structures, such as dedicated terminals.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan pemberian:
This group covers the provision of guarantees by a guarantor for the fulfillment of the guaranteed party's financial obligations to the guarantee beneficiary, carried out on a conventional basis, including:
- guarantees of credit and financing extended by financial institutions;
- guarantees of loans disbursed by savings-and-loan cooperatives or cooperatives having a savings-and-loan business unit to their members;
- guarantees of credit and/or loans under partnership programs disbursed by state-owned enterprises within the framework of partnership and community-development programs;
- guarantees of debt securities, guarantees of goods purchases by installment, guarantees of trade transactions, guarantees of the procurement of goods and/or services (surety bonds), guarantees of bank guarantees (counter bank guarantees), guarantees of domestic documentary letters of credit, guarantees of letters of credit, customs guarantees (customs bonds), excise guarantees, the provision of management-consultancy services related to guarantee business activities, and other guarantee activities.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan pembuatan:
This group covers the manufacture of sports and athletic equipment (excluding clothing and footwear) for competitive and recreational sport, for both professional and amateur use. This group covers:
- the manufacture of sports goods and equipment or accessories, both indoor and outdoor, from various materials, such as:
* hard balls, soft balls, and inflatable balls, such as footballs, basketballs, and volleyballs;
* tennis racquets, badminton racquets, golf clubs, hockey sticks, bats, and other striking implements;
* volleyball nets, table-tennis nets, and table-tennis tables;
* skis, bindings, and poles;
* ski boots, ice skates, cross-country ski boots;
* sailboards and surfboards;
* equipment for sport fishing, including landing nets;
* equipment for hunting or shooting;
* mountaineering and climbing equipment and gear;
* special sports gloves and headgear made of leather and composition leather;
* swimming pools and paddling/children's pools;
* ice skates, roller skates;
* bows and arrows;
* equipment for agility sports, gymnastic equipment (including mats), fitness-centre equipment, or athletics equipment.
This group does not cover:
- the manufacture of boat sails, see group 13999;
- the manufacture of sports clothing, see group 14111;
- the manufacture of saddlery and horse apparel, see group 15122;
- the manufacture of whips and riding equipment, see group 15122;
- the manufacture of sports footwear, see group 15202;
- the manufacture of rubber wet suits and diving suits, see subgroup 2219;
- the manufacture of weapons and ammunition for sport, see group 25200;
- the manufacture of metal weights for weightlifting, see subgroup 2599;
- the manufacture of vehicles for sport other than toboggans and the like, see divisions 29 and 30;
- the manufacture of sport bicycles, see group 30921;
- the manufacture of sport boats/canoes, see group 30120;
- the manufacture of billiard tables, see group 32401;
- the manufacture of ear and nose plugs (for example for swimming and nose protection), see subgroup 3290.

This group covers the manufacture of metal cutting tools, such as machetes, serrated knives, razors, razor blades, scissors, hair clippers, daggers or short knives, swords, and bayonets, including the manufacture of traditional weapons, knives and blades for machines or mechanical equipment, as well as saws and saw blades.
This group does not cover:
- the manufacture of sickles, harvesting hooks (egrek), oil-palm chisels (dodos), and axes, see group 25931;
- the manufacture of grinding knives for hand-tool accessories, see group 25931;
- the manufacture of metal cutlery, see group 25933.

This group covers the manufacture of sensing, measuring, testing, monitoring, and control instruments, such as:
- analytical instruments, scales, balances, and laboratory incubators, as well as other laboratory instruments for measurement and testing;
- electronic measuring and inspection instruments, whether or not related to scientific investigation, such as automatic electronic regulating apparatus, speedometers, taxi meters, cathode-ray electronic apparatus, radar and radar equipment, radio controls, electronic sensors, and radiation detectors, and global positioning systems (GPS);
- navigation, meteorological, geophysical, hydrological, and spectrophotometer instruments;
- digital measuring instruments, such as thermometers, barometers, and digital scales.
This group also covers the manufacture of proton and electron microscopes (excluding optical microscopes), electronic monitoring and control devices/modules with communication capabilities (Internet of Things), including embedded systems, data loggers, real-time monitoring units, early warning systems (including fire and burglar alarm systems that transmit signals to a control station), and other devices.

This group covers the manufacture of motor vehicle bodies or bodywork, such as:
- the manufacture of bodywork, including seats, for motor vehicles such as fire engines, mobile libraries, armoured cars, and concrete-mixer trucks;
- the manufacture of equipment for all types of motor vehicles, trailers and semi-trailers;
- the manufacture of trailers and semi-trailers, such as tankers, enclosed and open-body trailers, caravans;
- the repair and customisation of motor vehicles to order;
- the manufacture of containers (including containers for transporting liquids) specially designed and equipped for carriage by one or more modes of transport;
- the manufacture of chassis or frames for trailers.
This group does not cover:
- the manufacture of trailers and semi-trailers specially designed for use in agriculture, see subgroup 2821;
- the manufacture of body parts and accessories for motor vehicles, see subgroup 2930;
- the manufacture of animal-drawn vehicles, see subgroup 3099;
- the manufacture of tanks and military combat vehicles, see subgroup 3040.

This group covers the manufacture of fresh, frozen, or dry bakery products, such as:
- the manufacture of plain bread and bread rolls;
- the manufacture of pastries, cakes, pies, and tarts;
- the manufacture of toast, biscuits, and other dry bakery products;
- the manufacture of preserved pastry and cake products;
- the manufacture of snack foods (cookies, crackers, pretzels, etc.), whether sweet or savoury;
- the manufacture of tortillas;
- the manufacture of frozen bakery products, such as pancakes, waffles, and bread rolls.
This group does not cover:
- the manufacture of flour mixes and dough for bread, biscuits, or pancakes, see subclass 1061;
- the manufacture of pasta, see group 10740;
- the manufacture of potato-based snack foods, see subclass 1030;
- the heating of bakery products for immediate consumption, see section 56.

This group covers the manufacture of articles of paper and paperboard or board not covered in other subgroups, such as the manufacture of ready-to-use writing and printing paper, the manufacture of ready-to-use computer printout paper, the manufacture of ready-to-use carbon-copy paper, the manufacture of ready-to-use gummed or adhesive paper, the manufacture of registers, accounting books, binders, albums, and writing materials of a commercial or similar educational nature, the manufacture of boxes, cellulose cigarette filters, bags, pouches, absorbent pads, and notebooks containing an arrangement of paper, the manufacture of wallpaper and other types of wall coverings, including vinyl-coated and textile wallpaper, the manufacture of labels, filter paper and filter paperboard, the manufacture of paper and paperboard rolls, paper and paperboard spools, and so on, the manufacture of egg trays and other articles made from moulded paper pulp and so on, and the manufacture of novelty paper.
This group also covers:
- the processing of paper and paperboard by any means, such as coating, glazing, gumming, laminating; the manufacture of carbon paper and stencil sheets in pieces ready for sale to consumers;
- the manufacture of ECG paper, the manufacture of unprinted office stationery, such as envelopes and letter paper, and the manufacture of tableware (plates, cups, straws, and others) of paper and the like;
This group does not cover:
- the manufacture of printed office stationery and cards, see group 18111.

This group covers the manufacture of finished articles of fur skin, such as ready-made clothing and clothing accessories, for example fur coats; assemblies of fur skin, such as "dropped fur", plates, mats, rugs, and strips; as well as various articles of fur skin, such as carpets, unstuffed pouffes, and industrial polishing cloths.
This group does not cover:
- the production of raw fur skins, see groups 014 and 017;
- the production of raw hides and skins, see subgroup 1011;
- the manufacture of imitation fur (long-pile fabric obtained by weaving or knitting), see subgroups 1312, 1391;
- the manufacture of fur hats, see subgroup 1413;
- the dressing and dyeing of fur skins, see subgroup 1511;
- the manufacture of boots or shoes with parts containing fur, see subgroup 1520.

This group covers the manufacture of plastic goods not classified in subgroup 2220, such as:
- office/educational equipment; medical/laboratory equipment made of plastic, e.g. infusion bags and infusion tubing;
- film or cellophane sheets;
- artificial stone made of plastic; signs made of plastic (non-electrical);
- various plastic goods, such as headwear, insulating fittings, parts of lighting fixtures, articles of apparel (only sealed or assembled, not sewn), furniture fittings, statues, plastic adhesive tape, plastic wall coverings, durable plastic footwear, plastic cigar and cigarette holders, combs, plastic hair curlers, and novelty plastic items.
This group also covers the processing and finishing of plastic goods, such as coating with metal or other coating substances and painting (except for plastic motor-vehicle spare parts and accessories).
This group does not cover:
- the manufacture of sports equipment, including children's plastic swimming pools, see group 32300;
- the manufacture of children's plastic toys, see group 32402;
- the manufacture of bags, wallets, and the like made of leather and artificial leather, see group 15121.

This group covers the manufacture of various precious goods of precious metal not classified in groups 32112 to 32114, including:
- the manufacture of coins of precious metal, whether legal tender or not;
- engraving services on personal goods, whether of precious metal or not;
- the manufacture of precious-metal goods for technical and laboratory use (excluding instruments and their components), such as spatulas, crucibles, cupels, platinum grills for catalysts, and electroplating anodes;
- the manufacture of similar precious-metal goods for other uses, e.g. watch straps, watch bands, cufflinks, and cigarette cases.
This group does not cover:
- the manufacture of precious-metal jewelry, see group 32112;
- the manufacture of watch cases and watch jewelry, see group 26520;
- the manufacture of watch straps of non-metal materials (such as fabric, leather, and plastic), see subgroup 1512.

This group covers the manufacture of various goods with cement as the main constituent, including those mixed with other mineral materials and/or fibrous materials (such as plant fibers), used for:
- decorative purposes, such as: statues, flower pots, urns, furniture, relief images, reservoir products, troughs or tubs, ponds, sinks, and window frames, etc.;
- building-material purposes, such as tiles; bricks; concrete blocks; autoclaved aerated concrete; paving blocks; sheets; panels; cement vents; corrugated fiber-cement sheets/boards free of asbestos; flat fiber-cement sheets/boards free of asbestos; pressurized fiber-cement pipes free of asbestos; laminated fiber-cement sheets/boards; flat calcium-silicate sheets/boards; and so on;
- construction purposes, both structural and non-structural, applied to roads and bridges; residential buildings and other buildings; and water structures, such as concrete electricity poles; prestressed spun piles (hollow round-section piles); square piles (square-section piles); prestressed concrete sheet piles for soil-retaining systems; girders; box culverts and their covers; concrete pipes; beam, column, and wall components; and so on.

This group covers the manufacture of various kinds of optical lenses (except spectacle lenses) for photography, cinematography, medical, industrial, and scientific use, such as camera lenses, projector lenses, microscope lenses, telescope lenses, spectrometer lenses, and others.
This group also covers:
- the manufacture of objective lenses for cameras and projectors;
- the manufacture of zoom camera lenses;
- the manufacture of ground coated lenses.

This group covers the manufacture of various chemical materials and products not yet classified in any group, such as:
- the manufacture of gelatin;
- the manufacture of peptones, peptone derivatives, other protein substances and their derivatives;
- the manufacture of animal, vegetable, or microbial fats and oils and their fractions that have been boiled, oxidised, dehydrated, sulphurised, blown, polymerised by heating under vacuum or inert gas, or otherwise chemically modified;
- the manufacture of heat-insulating materials other than plastics and rubber; polishes;
- the manufacture of lubricating-oil additives; light-sensitive film; photographic paper;
- the manufacture of materials used for textiles and leather;
- the manufacture of powders and pastes used in brazing, metal joining, and welding;
- the manufacture of substances used for metals; formulated additives for cement;
- the manufacture of formulated rubber accelerators;
- the manufacture of catalysts;
- the manufacture of anti-knock preparations; antifreeze preparations;
- the manufacture of composite diagnostic or laboratory reagents;
- the manufacture of brake fluid;
- the manufacture of other chemical products for industrial use.

This group covers the manufacture of optical-fibre cables for the direct transmission of data or images, whether or not fitted with connectors.
This group does not cover:
- the manufacture of glass fibre/fibreglass or strands thereof, see subgroup 2312;
- the separate manufacture of connectors for optical fibres, optical-fibre bundles, and optical-fibre cables, see group 27330;
- the installation of optical-fibre cables and other cables, see subgroup 4321.

This group covers the creation of advertising campaigns and the placement of advertisements, the creation of brand identity, brand development, campaign management, and the development of creative advertising materials, such as in periodicals, newspapers, dailies, radio, television, the internet, digital media or other media for content in the field of sport as well as other fields, as well as the design of display-location structures. These advertising activities are generally provided by advertising agencies and media representatives.
This group covers:
- the creation and execution of advertising campaigns in the field of sport and other fields, comprising:
* the creation and placement of advertisements in newspapers/dailies and periodicals, on radio and television, through the internet and other media;
* the creation and placement of outdoor advertisements, for example on billboards, notice boards, panels, types of posters and pictures, leaflets, pamphlets, circulars, brochures and frames, window advertisements, shop-window display/decoration, and car and bus advertisements;
* media representation, namely the sale of space and time for various kinds of media for the placement of advertisements;
* aerial advertising;
* the distribution or delivery of advertising materials or samples;
* the provision of advertising space on billboards and the like;
* the construction of stands and exhibition structures as well as other advertising locations;
- the execution of marketing campaigns and other advertising services aimed at attracting and retaining customers in the field of sport and other fields, comprising:
* product promotion;
* point-of-sale marketing;
* direct-mail advertising;
* marketing consultancy as part of advertising.
This group does not cover:
- the publishing of advertising materials, see subclass 5819;
- the production of commercial messages for radio, television, and film, see subclass 5911;
- public-relations activities, see subclass 7330;
- market research, see subclass 7320;
- advertising photography, see subclass 7420;
- the organization of conventions and trade fairs, see subclass 8230;
- mailing services, see subclass 8210;
- marketing consultancy without the creation and placement of advertisements, see subclass 7020;
- advertising services used to fund the principal activity of a business that may be provided free of charge, see its principal activity.

This group covers the manufacture of current-carrying and non-current-carrying wiring devices for electrical circuits, made of any material. This group covers:
- busbars, electrical conductors (except the switchgear type), such as fittings, switches, and outlets;
- the manufacture of ground fault circuit interrupters (GFCI);
- the manufacture of lamp holders;
- the manufacture of lightning arresters and coils;
- the manufacture of plugs for electrical wiring devices (e.g. pressure, push-button, snap, tumbler switches);
- the manufacture of plugs, connectors, and electrical sockets;
- the manufacture of boxes for electrical wiring equipment (such as junction, outlet, and switch boxes);
- the manufacture of cable-protection conduits and their fittings;
- the manufacture of transmission poles and line hardware;
- the manufacture of plastic for non-current-carrying wiring devices, including plastic junction boxes, face plates and the like, plastic pole-line hardware, and plastic switch covers.
This group does not cover:
- the manufacture of ceramic insulators, see subgroup 2393.

This group covers the manufacture of special papers, such as cardiopan, litmus paper, metallic paper, acid-proof paper, pattern paper, coated paper, and cellophane paper. The processing of paper by coating it in any way, such as coating, glazing, gumming, and laminating. This group does not cover:
- the manufacture of carbon paper and stencils when in cut form ready for sale to consumers, see group 17099;
- the manufacture of photographic paper, see group 20299;
- the manufacture of abrasive paper (sandpaper), see group 23991.

This group covers the manufacture of components and spare parts for four-wheeled or larger motor vehicles, including components and spare parts such as:
- the manufacture of leaf springs, radiators, fuel tanks, mufflers, brakes, gearboxes, axles, road wheels, suspension shock absorbers, silencers, exhaust pipes, catalytic converters, clutches, steering wheels, steering column systems, and steering boxes;
- the manufacture of parts and accessories for motor vehicle bodies, such as seat belts, doors, bumpers, and airbags;
- the manufacture of car seats;
- the manufacture of motor vehicle electrical equipment, such as generators, alternators, spark plugs, ignition wiring harnesses/starters, automatic door and window opening and closing systems, the fitting of speedometers into instrument panels, voltage regulators, and lamps.
This group also covers
- the manufacture of chassis or frames (without engines) for motor vehicles;
- the manufacture of inverter modules and fuel cells for four-wheeled or larger motor vehicles;
- the manufacture of plastic components and spare parts for four-wheeled or larger motor vehicles, such as car interiors, coolant reservoirs, car mirror covers, and car battery holders;
- the finishing of plastic spare parts and components for four-wheeled or larger motor vehicles, such as coating with metal or other coating substances and painting.
This subgroup does not cover
- the manufacture of tyres, see subgroup 2211;
- the manufacture of rubber hoses and belts and other rubber products, see subgroup 2219;
- the manufacture of plastic hoses and belts and other plastic products, see subgroup 2220;
- the manufacture of batteries for motor vehicles, see subgroup 2720;
- the manufacture of lighting equipment for motor vehicles, see subgroup 2740;
- the manufacture of pistons, piston rings, and carburettors, see subgroup 2811;
- the manufacture of pumps for engines and motor vehicles, see subgroup 2813;
- the maintenance, repair, and modification of motor vehicles, see subgroup 9531.

This group covers the manufacture of matches in stick form. This group does not cover:
- the manufacture of flints, see group 23999;
- the manufacture of lighters, see group 32909.

This group covers the production of ready-to-eat foods (processed, seasoned, and cooked). These foods are processed and preserved, for example stored in cans or frozen, and are usually packaged and labelled for resale. This group does not cover the preparation of food for immediate consumption, such as in a restaurant or catering. To be regarded as a prepared dish, such processed food must contain at least two different main ingredients (other than seasonings). This group covers
- the production of meat or poultry dishes;
- the production of fish dishes, such as pepes, presto, fish jerky (dendeng), fried baby fish, battered shrimp, battered fish, and fish and chips;
- the production of dishes containing pasta and rice;
- the production of vegetable dishes;
- the production of frozen pizza and croque-monsieur.
This group does not cover
- the production of fresh food or food with fewer than two kinds of main ingredients, see division 10;
- the production of perishable ready-to-eat foods made from fruits and vegetables only, see subclass 1030;
- the production of soups, broths, and other foods, see subclass 1079;
- the retail trade of ready-to-eat foods, see subclasses 4711 and 4721;
- the wholesale trade of processed foods, see group 463;
- food service contractor activities, see subclass 5640.

This group does not cover
- the reproduction of recorded media (such as computer media, sound, and video), see subgroup 1820;
- the manufacture of light-sensitive film, see group 20299;
- sound recording on media such as cassette tape and vinyl records, see group 59201, whereas film image and video tape recording, see subgroup 5911;
- data recording on tape, disk/diskette, and the like using computer services, see group 62900.

This group covers the manufacture of machinery for the preparation and cultivation of agricultural and forestry land, for example tractors and ploughing machines.
This group covers
- the manufacture of tractors used in agriculture and forestry;
- the manufacture of single-axle (walk-behind) tractors;
- the manufacture of lawn mowers, including home garden mowers;
- the manufacture of self-loading or self-unloading trailers or semi-trailers for agriculture;
- the manufacture of agricultural machinery for preparation and planting, such as ploughs, harrows, fertilizer spreaders, seed spreaders, and fertilizer distributors;
- the manufacture of harvesting or threshing machines, such as mowers, threshers, harvesters, and others;
- the manufacture of milking machines;
- the manufacture of agricultural or horticultural spraying equipment;
- the manufacture of handsprayers;
- the manufacture of rice threshers and corn shellers;
- the manufacture of various agricultural machines, such as poultry-heating machines, beekeeping machines, equipment for preparing animal feed, and machines for cleaning, sorting, and grading eggs and fruit;
- the manufacture of machines for vertical farming.
This group also covers
- the manufacture of components and attachments for agricultural machinery.
This group does not cover
- the manufacture of agricultural hand tools operated without electric power of various types used in agriculture or forestry, see subgroup 2593;
- the manufacture of goods-carrying equipment for agricultural purposes, see subgroup 2816;
- the manufacture of hand tools powered by electricity, see subgroup 2818;
- the manufacture of earth-moving machinery, see subgroup 2824;
- the manufacture of cream separators, see subgroup 2825;
- the manufacture of machines for cleaning, sorting, or grading seeds, grains, or dried leguminous vegetables, see subgroup 2825;
- the manufacture of road tractors for semi-trailers, see subgroup 2910;
- the manufacture of trailers or semi-trailers for non-agricultural use, see subgroup 2920.

This group covers the manufacture of prime-mover engines using internal combustion, whether spark-ignition or compression-ignition engines, such as diesel engines, gasoline engines, gas/alcohol-fuelled internal-combustion engines, and the like, including the manufacture of engines for industrial applications and internal-combustion piston engines (except motor-vehicle, aircraft, and rotary-drive engines), such as marine engines and railway-locomotive engines. This group also covers the repair of ship and boat engine factories.
This group does not cover:
- the manufacture of internal-combustion engines for four-wheeled or larger motor vehicles, which is included in group 29100;
- the manufacture of internal-combustion engines for two- and three-wheeled motor vehicles, which is included in group 30912;
- the manufacture of internal-combustion engines for aircraft, see subgroup 3030.

This group covers the manufacture of other basic inorganic chemical products not yet covered, such as:
- the manufacture of phosphorus and its derivatives, sulphur and its derivatives, and nitrogen and its other derivatives;
- the manufacture of metallic elements and other oxide compounds;
- the manufacture of raw materials for explosives;
- the manufacture of products used as fluorescent brightening agents or as luminophores.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan pemunguta:
This group covers the gathering of wild-growing non-timber forest products, for example mushrooms, truffles, berries, nuts, balata and other gums, cork, lac and resins, balsam, acorns, horse chestnuts, mosses, and lichens, as well as eelgrass.
This group also covers:
- the tapping of rubber latex, gutta-percha, jelutong, and benzoin;
- the gathering of rattan, pine resin, dragon's blood (jernang), copal, and shellac;
- the gathering of wild-growing bamboo;
- the gathering of silkworm cocoons, resin, honey, and swiftlet nests;
- the gathering of agarwood leaves/fruit/bark, sandalwood leaves/twigs/bark, lawang bark, and cinnamon;
- the gathering of pandan leaves and cajuput leaves;
- the collection of wild-growing spices and their natural drying.
This group does not cover:
- agriculture producing the products mentioned above (except the cultivation of cork trees), see division 01;
- the cultivation of mushrooms and truffles, see group 0113;
- the cultivation of berries and assorted nuts, see group 0125;
- the collection of firewood, see group 0220.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan pengangku:
This group covers the transport of passengers by various urban rail transport modes, such as trams, monorails, electric trains, underground trains, and elevated trains.
This group also covers
- the operation of cable-drawn trams, cable cars, hill railways, cable railways (gondolas), monorails, driverless or autonomous rail trains (ART), and the like, where they form part of an urban or commuter route system;
- rail transport on city-to-airport or city-to-port routes.
This group does not cover
- long-distance (inter-city) rail transport of passengers, see subclass 49111;
- short-distance (urban) tourist rail transport, see group 49211;
- the operation of cable cars, cable railways (gondolas), and other railways that are not part of urban transport, see group 49291;
- the operation of cable cars, cable railways (gondolas), chairlifts, and other railways as part of the operation of amusement and recreation grounds, see subclass 9329.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan pengaweta:
This group covers the preservation of fruits and vegetables by methods other than those covered in groups 10301 to 10308, such as:
- the manufacture of foods made principally from fruits or vegetables, except frozen or canned ready-to-eat meals;
- the manufacture of perishable foods from fruits and vegetables, for example the preparation of fruit salads or vegetable salads;
- the processing and preservation of soybeans and legumes other than tofu and tempeh, such as natto, yuba/tofu skin, fu zhu, and douchi, including tempe gembus and tempe bongkrek;
- the roasting of various kinds of nuts, such as the roasting of green peas, salted peanuts, egg peanuts, bambara groundnuts, atom peanuts, cashew nuts, and enting-enting.
This group does not cover the manufacture of processed foods from vegetables, see subclass 1075.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan pengerjaa:
This group covers the execution of flooring, wall, and ceiling works for the completion of residential and non-residential buildings as well as civil engineering structures.
This group covers:
- interior or exterior coating with plaster and stucco, including the associated lathing materials;
- interior finishing such as ceilings (e.g. of gypsum), wood wall coverings, and demountable partitions/dividers;
- the laying of floor and wall coverings of ceramic, concrete, or natural stone; the laying of parquet flooring and other wood floor coverings; the laying of linoleum, carpet, including floor coverings of rubber or plastic; the laying of floors and walls of terrazzo, marble, granite, or slate; and the hanging of wallpaper or other wall coverings.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan pengolaha:
This group covers the processing of seed aimed at improving the quality of seed propagation through the elimination of non-seed material, undersized seed, seed that is mechanically damaged or insect-damaged, and immature seed, and also at reducing seed moisture so that it is safe for storage. This activity covers drying, cleaning, grading, sorting and the like until the seed is marketed. The maintenance of modified seed is also included here.
This group does not cover:
- the preparation of agricultural products by farmers, see groups 011, 012 or 013;
- the redrying and cleaning of tobacco, see class 1200;
- marketing by commission traders and cooperative associations, see division 46;
- wholesale trade in agricultural products and live animals, see group 462;
- the planting of seed, see groups 011 and 012;
- the processing of seeds to produce oil, see class 1041;
- research to develop or modify seed into new forms, see class 7210.

This group covers the processing and preservation of finfish by other methods not covered under groups 10211 through 10218, such as:
- vessel operations used solely for the processing and preservation of fish;
- production of fish meal, whether for human consumption or animal feed;
- production of meal and solubles derived from fish unfit for human consumption;
- manufacture of fish meal concentrate;
- cutting of fish into fillets, loins, sakus, steaks, and chunks not accompanied by a freezing process;
- processing and preservation of fish using radiation (with an irradiator).
This group does not cover the cutting of fish into fillets, loins, sakus, steaks, and chunks accompanied by a freezing process, see group 10213.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan penjamina:
This group covers the guaranteeing of the fulfillment of a guaranteed party's financial obligations to the guarantee recipient based on sharia principles, including:
- financing guarantees based on sharia principles provided by financial institutions;
- guarantees of loans or financing disbursed by savings-and-loan cooperatives or cooperatives having a savings-and-loan business unit to their members;
- guarantees of partnership-program loans or financing disbursed by state-owned enterprises under partnership and community-development programs, carried out wholly on sharia principles;
- sharia-based activities such as guarantees of debt securities, guarantees of installment purchases of goods, guarantees of trade transactions, guarantees of the procurement of goods and/or services (surety bonds), guarantees of bank guarantees (counter-bank guarantees), guarantees of domestic documentary letters of credit (SKBDN), guarantees of letters of credit, customs guarantees (customs bonds), excise guarantees, the provision of management consultancy services related to guarantee business activities, and other guarantee activities.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan penyediaa:
This group covers the activity of providing architectural consultancy services, such as
- preparation of preliminary architectural studies;
- architectural design services;
- architectural advisory and pre-design services;
- other architectural services;
- building appraisal and feasibility assessment services;
- services for developing the utilization of space, regions, urban areas, the built environment and landscapes;
- design of buildings and their surroundings;
- design for the conservation of buildings and their surroundings;
- design of building layout and its surroundings;
- preparation of technical planning documents, and supervision of architectural aspects in the execution of building construction and its surroundings;
- urban planning and land use; project management and construction management, community facilitation, other construction.
- design of objects based on building classification in accordance with the International Building Code:
* assembly;
* business;
* educational;
* factory and industrial;
* high hazard;
* institutional;
* mercantile;
* residential;
* storage;
* utility and miscellaneous.
This group does not cover
- inspection services for buildings or structures, warehouses, and other civil engineering structures, see group 71202.

This group covers the provision of payment services to end users of payment-system services at the front end, encompassing activities such as:
- the administration of funding sources for payment, including the issuance of payment instruments or accounts;
- the forwarding of fund-transfer instructions (including remittance services) and the forwarding of payment transaction data, including acquiring and the operation of payment gateways.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan penyempur:
This group covers other textile finishing activities:
- dry finishing as an intermediate process in the textile industry, such as calendering; embossing; sueding; raising; shearing; singeing; brushing; sanding; decatising; pleating, crushing, pintucking, ecoprinting; and fabric printing using transfer printing methods, for example heat transfer and sublimation;
- the making of made-to-order embroidery on textiles;
- the making of headscarves/scarves without sewing, integrated with the printing process.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan penyewaan:
This group covers the renting and operational leasing (without purchase option) of recreational and sports equipment, such as
- recreational boats, canoes, sailboats, and yachts without operator;
- bicycles, including electric bicycles;
- beach chairs and umbrellas;
- other sports equipment, including ski equipment.
This group does not cover
- the renting of recreational boats and sailboats with crew, see subclasses 5011 and 5021;
- the renting of video cassettes and discs, see subclass 7729;
- the renting of other personal and household goods, see subclass 7729;
- the renting and leasing of water transport equipment for passengers or goods, for example boats, ships, and hovercraft without operator, see subclass 7731;
- the renting of equipment for hobbies and leisure as an integral part of recreational facilities, see subclass 9329.

This group covers renting and operating leasing without a purchase option (operational leasing) of various types of land-transport motor vehicles, such as passenger cars without a driver, trucks, motor caravans, trailers (towed wagons), and recreational vehicles. This group also covers the renting and operational leasing of private cars without a driver and of motorcycles. This group does not cover
- the renting or leasing without a purchase option of land-transport equipment together with its operator, see subclasses 4922 and 4923;
- the renting of bicycles, see group 77210;
- the renting of motorboats, see group 77312.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan perancang:
This group covers the design and development of health, cosmetics, and laboratory equipment products. This group also covers:
- the design of medical, laboratory, and hospital equipment and materials products;
- the design of medical devices;
- the design of prosthetic products;
- the design of pharmaceutical and cosmetic products;
- the design of cosmetics packaging and containers;
- the design of beauty salon and toiletry equipment products;
- the design of wigs and similar products.
These design activities are also carried out using specialised software.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan perantara:
This group covers intermediary activities for the sale of travel packages for tourism or other purposes such as tours or pilgrimage trips, whether online or offline, packaged by travel agencies in bulk or retail to the general public and commercial clients.
This group also covers
- intermediary activities for the sale of umrah and special hajj pilgrimage packages, whether online or offline, packaged by umrah and special hajj pilgrimage travel agencies;
- intermediary activities for the sale of sports tourism travel packages encompassing various forms of travel and experiences involving physical activity, competition, or sports-based entertainment, such as travel for sporting events, sports adventure tourism, and special travel for athletes and sports teams about to compete;
- intermediation activities in the conclusion of contracts for the provision of tourism services from travel agencies;
- intermediation services for travel packages at destinations.
This group does not cover
- intermediation services for passenger transport only, see subclass 5232;
- intermediation services for accommodation only, see subclass 5540;
- the sale of travel boxes: a form of distribution of services related to travel, but constituting a deferred service, which may be anything: hotels, restaurants, treatments, recreational activities, etc., see subclass 8299;
- activities involving factual and legal acts related to the conclusion of contracts for the provision of tourism services, at the customer's request, see main group 69.

This group covers brokerage activities, namely a party that carries out transactions in carbon units on behalf of another party or its clients.
This group does not cover:
- the trading of carbon units on one's own account; see group 64995;
- brokerage of securities other than carbon units; see group 66121;
- transacting in financial markets on one's own account (other than carbon unit trading activities); see group 64994.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan perawatan:
This group covers beauty care activities not performed by medical specialists, for example by cosmeticians.
This group covers
- beauty services primarily for the care and beautification of nails at a nail studio or with home visits, such as nail art and manicure-pedicure;
- beauty services primarily for the care and beautification of eyelashes at an eyelash studio or with home visits, such as eyelash extension, lash lift, lash perming, and lash tint;
- beauty services primarily for the care and beautification of eyebrows at a brow studio or with home visits, such as eyebrow embroidery, brow bomber, and brow lamination;
- beauty services primarily for hair removal at a wax studio or with home visits;
- facial make-up services by make-up artists (MUA);
- facial massage services;
- skin tanning services.
This group does not cover
- plastic surgery activities performed by medical specialists, see subclass 8620.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan perdagang:
This group covers trading in various financial instruments (e.g. shares, foreign exchange, commodity contracts, and crypto) on own account (trader) and in financial assets such as bullion, generally for short-term gain. This group also covers:
- investment and trading activities on own account;
- trading in receivables on own account;
- securities and derivatives dealers operating on own account;
- trading in swaps or options on own account;
- trading in commodity contracts on own account;
- trading in crypto assets together with their liabilities on own account;
- trading in derivatives on the money market and the foreign-exchange money market on own account;
- trading in bullion financial assets on own account.
This group does not cover:
- trading in carbon units on own account, see group 64995;
- transactions in securities and commodity contracts on behalf of others (brokerage), see subclass 6612;
- crypto-asset brokerage, see subclass 6612;
- trading in bullion on behalf of others (brokerage), see 66129;
- mortgage brokerage, see subclass 6619;
- trading and brokerage of crypto assets without associated liabilities (not by the monetary authority), see subclass 8299.

This group covers the wholesale trade of various sporting equipment and accessories:
- wholesale of equipment for physical exercise, gymnastics, or athletics, such as treadmills, dumbbells, and resistance bands;
- wholesale of outdoor sports equipment, such as balls, rackets, and surfboards;
- wholesale of outdoor play equipment, such as trampolines, basketball hoops, and swings;
- wholesale of bicycles, spare parts, and their accessories.

This group covers the wholesale trade of machinery, equipment, and supplies not yet classified in groups 46591 through 46594:
- wholesale of prime movers, turbines, and electricity-generating machines;
- wholesale of production robots other than for manufacturing;
- wholesale of other machinery not elsewhere classified for trade, navigation, and other services;
- wholesale of cables, switches, and other equipment installations;
- wholesale of machine tools of various types and for various materials;
- wholesale of weapons, weapons systems, and ammunition, including tanks and armoured combat vehicles;
- wholesale of computer-controlled machine tools other than for manufacturing;
- wholesale of measuring equipment and instruments;
- wholesale of mining, construction, and civil-engineering machinery and equipment, such as excavators;
- wholesale of traffic barriers, bollards, street lamps, traffic lights, traffic signs, and bus- and tram-stop fittings.

This group covers the trading of carbon units, that is, the right to emissions or to the absorption of emissions, acting on one's own behalf.
This group does not cover
- trading of financial instruments other than carbon units on one's own behalf, see group 64994;
- the operation of an exchange to facilitate the trading of carbon units, see group 66111;
- transactions in carbon units on behalf of others (brokerage), see group 66127;
- the measurement and verification of carbon units, see subclass 7120.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan perencana:
This group covers the activity of planning creative game content, including:
- game mechanics logic design;
- story design;
- artistic design, such as character visual design, user-interface design, and level design;
- technical design related to the technology used;
- the preparation of design documents;
- research and development;
- other supporting activities.
This group does not cover
- the activity of producing game equipment, see group 32401;
- video-game development, see group 62110.

This group covers creative content planning activities specifically for film, video, television programmes, as well as animation and comics, including:
- story design;
- character design and casting;
- artistic and visual design;
- production technical design;
- other support requirements.
This activity does not cover:
- the making of comics, see group 90120;
- the planning and making of computer animation, see subclass 5912.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan pertamban:
This group covers the mining of crude petroleum, including the prospecting of petroleum deposits, drilling, extraction, separation and stockpiling, the production of crude petroleum condensate, and processing to produce crude oil by means of stockpiling, filtering, drying, stabilization, and so forth. The products of petroleum mining include, among others, crude oil and condensate. This group also covers the mining of bituminous sands or oil shale and tar sands. Such mining activities include excavation, drilling, crushing, washing, screening and blending, as well as stockpiling, including the production of crude petroleum from oil shale and bituminous sands where it is associated with their mining.
This group covers
- the mining of crude petroleum.
This group also covers
- the mining of bituminous sands or oil shale and tar sands;
- the production of crude petroleum from bituminous shale and sands;
- processes to produce crude oil, such as stockpiling, filtering, drying, and stabilization;
- the production of condensate (petroleum with a high carbon content);
- carbon trading activities carried out by petroleum mining companies.
This group does not cover
- support services for oil and gas mining, see subgroup 0910;
- oil and gas exploration services, see subgroup 0910;
- petroleum refining, see subgroup 1920;
- the production of liquid petroleum gas (LPG) from petroleum refining, see subgroup 1920;
- pipeline operation, see subgroup 4930;
- the extraction of condensate or natural gas liquids (NGL), see subgroup 0620;

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan pihak yan:
This group covers the activities of a party that interposes itself between the parties to a financial transaction, thereby acting as a buyer to every seller and as a seller to every buyer.
This group covers activities acting as counterparty for the clearing and settlement of transactions in
- the capital market;
- the commodity futures market;
- the digital financial asset market, including crypto assets;
- the money market;
- the foreign exchange market;
- other financial markets.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan reparasi:
This group covers the repair and maintenance of motor cars, including trailers and semi-trailers, such as
- mechanical repair;
- electrical repair;
- repair of electronic injection systems;
- routine servicing;
- car bodywork repair;
- repair of car parts;
- spraying and painting;
- repair of glass and windows;
- repair of car seats;
- repair and diagnosis of mechatronic systems;
- repair, fitting, or replacement of inner and outer tires; anti-rust coating;
- fitting of parts and accessories that are not part of the processing/manufacturing process.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan usaha kre:
This group covers the business activities of creating industrial design work to produce sports and games equipment products. This group covers
- design for toy and entertainment products;
- design for sports equipment products;
- design for tent and outdoor equipment products.
The design activities of this group are also carried out using specialized software.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan yang berk:
This group covers activities related to the management, maintenance, preservation, and appraisal of libraries carried out by non-governmental parties, whether individuals, organizations, companies, foundations, or other private institutions, and not under the auspices of an educational institution or other cultural institution.
This group covers
- documentation and information activities of various private libraries (including digital libraries), reading rooms, listening rooms, and viewing rooms;
- the organization of private library collections, whether specialized or not;
- the cataloguing of private library collections;
- the lending and storage of books, maps, periodicals, films, recordings, (cassette) tapes, works of art, and so on in private libraries;
- the retrieval of private library documents for the purpose of meeting information needs, and so forth.

This group covers activities related to the management, maintenance, preservation, and appraisal of libraries carried out by government institutions, whether at the national, regional, or local level, and not under the auspices of an educational institution or other cultural institution.
This group covers
- documentation and information activities of various government libraries (including digital libraries), reading rooms, listening rooms, and viewing rooms;
- the organization of government library collections, whether specialized or not;
- the cataloguing of government library collections;
- the lending and storage of books, maps, periodicals, films, recordings, cassette tapes, works of art, and so on in government libraries;
- the retrieval of government library documents for the purpose of meeting information needs, and so forth.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan yang memp:
This group covers activities of permitting other parties to use intellectual property products or similar products in exchange for royalty payments or licensing fees to the owner of the product or the holder of the asset.
The use of such assets may take various forms, such as licensing for reproduction, use in subsequent processes or production, and the operation of a business under a franchise system. The current owner may or may not be the one who created the asset.
This group covers:
- operational leasing (without a purchase option) of intellectual property products (other than copyrighted works such as books or software);
- the receipt of royalties or licensing fees for the use of products, such as patented entities, trademarks and service marks, trade names, mineral/mining exploration rights, franchise agreements, internet domains, and rights to board games that have been designed or developed.
This group also covers the receipt of royalties or licensing fees for the results of scientific research.
This group does not cover:
- the receipt of income from rights and the publishing of books and software, films and music, see divisions 58, 59;
- the production, reproduction, and distribution of copyrighted works (books, software, films), see divisions 58, 59;
- the streaming of content, such as software and books, by content publishers, see division 58;
- the streaming of audiobooks not connected with their publishing, see subclass 6010;
- the leasing of real estate, see group 681;
- the renting of tangible goods (assets), see groups 771, 772, and 773.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan yang meny:
This group covers activities that provide other food-supply services on the basis of a contractual agreement with the customer, for a specified period of time, including catering services under agreement at sports facilities and other similar venues. Food may be prepared directly at the client's premises or at a central unit.
This group also covers
- the activities of food-service contractors, e.g. for transport companies;
- catering services providing long-term food supply at oil-drilling sites, mining locations, hospitals, and transport services;
- catering services under agreement at sports facilities and similar facilities;
- the activities of canteens or cafeterias (e.g. for factories, offices, hospitals, or schools) on a concession basis;
- catering services serving households;
- the provision of nutritious food and its distribution to target groups;
- the activities of food-supply contractors for restaurants/cloud kitchens.
This group does not cover
- the manufacture of non-perishable foods for resale, see group 10750;
- the retail trade of non-perishable foods, see division 472.

This group covers activities that provide wellness and care services by combining traditional and modern methods holistically. These activities use water and other supporting treatments in the form of massage using herbal preparations, aromatherapy, physical exercise, color therapy, music therapy, and food and beverages. The purpose of these activities is to balance the body, mind, and soul, so as to bring about a relaxed and fit condition for optimal health. These activities also represent an effort to preserve the nation's traditions and culture.
This group covers
- the activities of Turkish baths, saunas, and steam baths, day spas, solariums, slimming and body-reduction salons, and others.
This subclass does not cover
- physical well-being services as part of accommodation activities, see division 55;
- the activities of medical massage therapists, see subclass 8699;
- the activities of practitioners in the fields of shiatsu, Thai massage, watsu, tuina, and qigong, see subclass 8699;
- the activities of health, fitness, and body-building clubs and facilities, see subclass 9311.

Kelompok ini mencakup kegiatan yang terk:
This group covers activities related to the functions of regulation, supervision, examination, and investigation of
- financial services activities in the banking sector;
- financial services activities in the capital market, financial derivatives, and carbon exchange sectors;
- financial services activities in the financing institution, venture capital company, microfinance institution, and other financial services industry sectors;
- financial services activities in the commodity contract trading sector;
- activities in the financial-sector technology innovation, digital financial asset, and crypto asset sectors;
- the conduct of financial services business operators as well as the delivery of consumer education and protection;
- the financial sector on an integrated basis.
This group does not cover
- the regulation, supervision, and examination of financial services in the insurance, guarantee, and pension fund sectors, see group 66292;
- the activities of self-regulatory organizations, see group 66117.

Kelompok ini mencakup operasional transp:
This group covers the operation of freight transport by motor vehicle for goods that specifically carry a single type of cargo.
This group also covers:
- transport of fuel oil, petroleum, refined products, LPG, LNG, and CNG;
- transport of hazardous goods, hazardous and toxic waste;
- transport of carbon dioxide (CO2);
- transport of heavy-equipment goods;
- transport of containers;
- transport of live plants;
- transport of live animals;
- transport of motor vehicles;
- transport and distribution of fish and other aquatic biota;
- distribution of carbon-free fuels in gaseous, solid, or liquid form, depending on requirements and storage conditions, as energy carriers, such as hydrogen, ammonia, and other compounds, using motor transport.
This group does not cover:
- the supply/distribution of water by truck, see subclass 3600.

Kelompok ini mencakup pelayanan lalu lin:
This group covers air traffic services (ATS) such as:
- air traffic control, flight information, and alerting services;
- aeronautical telecommunication services (COM):
* aeronautical fixed service;
* aeronautical mobile and aeronautical radio navigation;
- aeronautical information service (AIS):
* aeronautical information and aeronautical chart services;
* issuance and dissemination of notices to airmen (NOTAM);
* aerodrome aeronautical information services;
- aeronautical meteorological service (MET):
* search and rescue (SAR) information services.
This group also covers:
- services providing the operation and support of air traffic activities:
* control towers;
* coordination related to air traffic activities;
- activities related to air traffic services, aeronautical telecommunications, construction of aeronautical navigation telecommunications, installation of aeronautical navigation equipment, and the provision of flight-related information:
* operation of aeronautical navigation, aeronautical telecommunication, aeronautical information, aeronautical meteorological information, and search-and-rescue information facilities or equipment, together with their supporting facilities or equipment, namely mechanical, electrical, electronic, and information technology.

Kelompok ini mencakup pemberian nasihat,:
This group covers the provision of advice, guidance, and operational assistance, including lobbying activities, to enterprises and other organizations in relation to public relations and communication.
This group also covers:
- lobbying activities;
- the activities of sales representatives for promotional purposes.
This group does not cover:
- lobbying consultancy activities, see subclass 7020;
- advertising agencies and media representation services, see subclass 7310;
- market research and public opinion polling, see subclass 7320;
- design and consultancy related to visual communication, see subclass 7419;
- educational consultancy activities, see subclass 8569.

Kelompok ini mencakup pembuangan dan pen:
This group covers the disposal and pre-disposal treatment of hazardous waste and non-radioactive specific hazardous waste managed by either the government or the private sector, including explosive materials, oxidizing materials, flammable materials, toxic materials, irritants, carcinogens, corrosives, or materials that can cause infection, and other substances and preparations hazardous to human health and the environment.
This group covers:
- the operation of facilities for the treatment of hazardous waste and non-radioactive specific waste;
- the treatment and disposal of toxic live or dead animals and other contaminated waste;
- the incineration of hazardous waste;
- the disposal of used goods such as refrigerators to eliminate hazardous waste.

Kelompok ini mencakup pembuatan alat-ala:
This group covers the manufacture of other communication transmission equipment, such as:
- private branch exchange (PBX) equipment;
- data communication equipment (bridges, routers, gateways);
- cable television equipment, transmitting (broadcast) and receiving antennas;
- television and radio studio equipment;
- broadcast equipment including television cameras;
- carrier-equipment modems;
- radio and television transmitters;
- communication equipment using infrared signals (e.g., remote controls);
- broadcasting studio equipment, such as broadcast reproduction equipment, transmitting and receiving antennas, and commercial video cameras;
- electronic data capture (EDC) equipment.
This group also covers:
- the manufacture of smart watches;
- the manufacture of transmission equipment/modules for Bluetooth, radio frequency (RF), GSM, and other connectivity used in the Internet of Things (IoT);
- the manufacture of set-top boxes for terrestrial and satellite reception;
- the manufacture of closed-circuit television (CCTV) surveillance cameras.

Kelompok ini mencakup pembuatan dan/atau:
This group covers the manufacture and/or assembly of computers, for example mainframe computers, desktop computers, laptops, and computer servers. Computers may be analog, digital, or hybrid, and may be PCs. Digital computers are the type most commonly used and can do the following: (1) store the processing program or programs and the data required for the execution of a program; (2) be programmed according to the user's needs; (3) perform the arithmetic calculations desired by the user; and (4) execute, without human intervention, a processing program that requires the computer to modify its execution by logical decisions during the course of the run. Analog computers are capable of simulating mathematical models and consist of at least analog control and programming elements.
This group covers:
- the manufacture of desktop computers;
- the manufacture of laptop computers;
- the manufacture of mainframe computers;
- the manufacture of handheld computers;
- the manufacture of tablet computers;
- the manufacture of computer servers;
- the manufacture of interactive computers, including digital signage, smartboards (interactive whiteboards), and interactive self-service devices (kiosks).
This group also covers:
- the assembly of computers;
- the manufacture of computer terminals, such as automated teller machines (ATMs) and point-of-sale (POS) terminals, that are not mechanically operated;
- the manufacture of computers with special functions for cybersecurity, such as firewalls or network detection and response (NDR).

Kelompok ini mencakup pembuatan kendaraa:
This group covers the manufacture of military combat vehicles, whether or not fitted with weapons, and parts thereof, such as:
- the manufacture of tanks;
- the manufacture of armoured combat vehicles for transporting personnel;
- the manufacture of armoured supply vehicles or armoured recovery vehicles with cranes;
- the manufacture of armoured amphibious military vehicles;
- the manufacture of remotely operated tanks;
- the manufacture of armoured combat-vehicle bodies and parts thereof such as armoured turrets, armoured doors and shields;
- the manufacture of armoured plate identified as part of military combat vehicles;
- the manufacture of other military combat vehicles.
This group also covers the inspection and rebuilding of military combat vehicles at factories.
This group does not cover:
- the manufacture of weapons and ammunition, see subgroup 2520;
- the manufacture of passenger cars and trucks with light armour or with detachable armour, see subgroup 2910;
- the manufacture of military ships, see subgroup 3011;
- the repair and maintenance of military combat vehicles, see subgroup 3315;
- the manufacture of drones for military purposes, see subgroup 3030.

Kelompok ini mencakup pembuatan kimia da:
This group covers the manufacture of basic organic chemicals whose raw materials are derived from petroleum, natural gas, or coal.
This group covers:
- the manufacture of cyclic hydrocarbons, such as benzene, toluene, xylene, ethylbenzene, styrene;
- the manufacture of acyclic hydrocarbons, including via pyrolysis, such as ethylene, propylene, butadiene, methanol, and synthetic ethanol;
- the manufacture of functional compounds obtained from oxidation, alkylation, halogenation, hydration, hydrogenation, such as ethylene dichloride, ethylene oxide, cyclohexane, terephthalic acid, synthetic glycerol, and caprolactam;
- the distillation of coal tar.

Kelompok ini mencakup pembuatan mesin-me:
This group covers the manufacture of machinery and equipment for mining, quarrying, and construction activities, such as:
- the manufacture of elevators and continuous-action goods and material handling equipment for underground use;
- the manufacture of boring, cutting or sinking machinery for extracting minerals or ores or for cutting coal or rock, and tunnelling machinery;
- the manufacture of machinery for processing minerals by way of screening, sorting, separating, washing, crushing, grinding, mixing or kneading earth, stone, ore or other mineral substances, in solid form (including powder or paste);
- the manufacture of concrete and mortar mixing machines;
- the manufacture of earth-moving machinery, such as bulldozers, angle dozers, graders, scrapers, levellers, shovels, and shovel loaders;
- the manufacture of pile-driving and pile-extracting machines, mortar and asphalt spreaders, concrete surface finishing machines, and others;
- the manufacture of machines for mixing mineral substances with bitumen;
- the manufacture of tracklaying excavators;
- the manufacture of bulldozer and angle dozer blades;
- the manufacture of off-road dumping trucks;
- the manufacture of snow ploughs and snow blowers.
This group does not cover:
- the manufacture of lifting and handling equipment, see subgroup 2816;
- the manufacture of other tractors, see subgroup 2821, 2910;
- the manufacture of machine tools for working stone, including machines for breaking or cleaning stone, see subgroup 2822;
- the manufacture of concrete-mixer lorries/wagons, see subgroup 2920.

Kelompok ini mencakup pembuatan peralata:
This group covers the manufacture of electronic audio and video equipment for home entertainment for households and motor vehicles.
This group also covers:
- the manufacture of video recording and reproducing equipment;
- the manufacture of audio reproducing and recording equipment, such as CD and VCD/DVD players;
- the manufacture of radio receivers and combinations thereof;
- the manufacture of stereo equipment;
- the manufacture of optical media players with optical reading systems;
- the manufacture of computer projectors and TV projectors;
- the manufacture of household-type video cameras, such as tape recorders and video recorders;
- the manufacture of jukeboxes.

This group covers the manufacture of other household electronic equipment, such as loudspeakers for conveying information and amplifiers for musical instruments.
This group also covers:
- the manufacture of amplifiers for musical instruments and loudspeakers for conveying information;
- the manufacture of microphones;
- the manufacture of speakers, including loudspeakers;
- the manufacture of headphones, e.g. for radios, stereos, and computers;
- the manufacture of karaoke machines;
- the manufacture of video game consoles;
- the manufacture of personal audio and video equipment (such as VR headsets);
- the manufacture of audio and video equipment for home theatre.
This group does not cover:
- the reproduction of recorded media (computer, audio, video, and similar media), see 1820;
- the manufacture of computer peripherals and computer monitors, see subgroup 2622;
- the manufacture of telephone answering machines, see subgroup 2631;
- the manufacture of pagers, see subgroup 2632;
- the manufacture of remote control equipment (radio and infrared), see subgroup 2639;
- the manufacture of broadcasting studio equipment such as broadcast reproduction equipment, transmitting and receiving antennas, and commercial video cameras, see subgroup 2639;
- the manufacture of broadcasting and studio equipment, see subgroup 2639;
- the manufacture of antennas, see subgroup 2639;
- the manufacture of digital cameras, see subgroup 2670;
- the manufacture of electronic games with fixed software, see subgroup 3240.

... 
- the manufacture of electrical components of the rectification type, electronic equipment, voltage regulators, power-conversion integrated circuits, electronic capacitors, electronic resistors, and similar equipment, see subgroup 2619;
- the manufacture of transformers, motors, generators, switchgear, relays, and controllers for industry, see subgroup 2711, 2712;
... (rest unchanged)

Kelompok ini mencakup pembuatan perlengk:
This group covers the manufacture of computer peripheral equipment, such as storage devices and input or output devices. This group covers:
- the manufacture of magnetic disk drives, flash drives, and other storage devices;
- the manufacture of optical disk drives for computers;
- the manufacture of printers;
- the manufacture of monitors;
- the manufacture of keyboards;
- the manufacture of mice, joysticks, and trackball accessories;
- the manufacture of scanners, including barcode scanners;
- the manufacture of smart card readers;
- the manufacture of computer projectors (video beamers);
- the manufacture of immersive media equipment (e.g. virtual reality, augmented reality, and mixed reality), such as virtual reality helmets and augmented reality glasses.
This group also covers:
- the manufacture of multifunction office equipment capable of performing various functions, such as printing, copying, and faxing.
This group does not cover:
- the reproduction of recorded media (computer, audio, video, and other media), see 1820;
- the manufacture of electronic components and electronic devices used in computers and their peripherals, see 2619;
- the manufacture of interface cards, modules, and their equipment, see subgroup 2619;
- the manufacture of printed circuit boards (PCB) already fitted with passive elements, see subgroup 2619;
- the manufacture of carrier-equipment modems, see subgroup 2639;
- the manufacture of digital communication switches and data communication equipment (e.g. bridges, routers, and gateways), see subgroup 2639;
- the manufacture of television monitors, see subgroup 2641;
- the manufacture of electronic devices such as CD players or DVD players, see subgroup 2642;
- the manufacture of blank magnetic and optical media used with computers or other equipment, see subgroup 2680.

Kelompok ini mencakup pembuatan produk k:
This group covers the manufacture of basic organic chemical products that produce chemicals from agricultural and fishery products, such as:
- the manufacture of biobenzene, biotoluene, and bioxylene through the pyrolysis of acyclic and cyclic alcohol biomass;
- the manufacture of carboxylic acids from animals or plants, such as fatty acids, acetic acid, citric acid, through fermentation or other processes;
- the fermentation of sugarcane, corn, or the like to produce alcohols and esters, such as bioethanol;
- the manufacture of fatty alcohol, furfural, sorbitol;
- the manufacture of wood charcoal, coconut-shell charcoal, coconut-shell charcoal briquettes, charcoal from other biomass;
- the manufacture of products from the distillation of wood and natural resins, such as gum rosin and turpentine;
- the manufacture of chemical compounds separated from essential oils, such as caryophyllene, eugenol, vanillin, geraniol, citronellaldehyde.
This group does not cover:
- the manufacture of liquid biofuel, see subgroup 2029;
- the manufacture of plastic polymers, see subgroup 2013.

Kelompok ini mencakup pembuatan sel sury:
This group covers the manufacture of solar cells, solar panels, and photovoltaic inverters, including photovoltaic cells, modules, and panels.
This group does not cover:
- manufacture of solar-powered lamps, see subgroup 2740;
- manufacture of solar heating systems, see subgroup 2815;
- installation of solar heating systems, see subgroup 4321.

Kelompok ini mencakup pendanaan dan admi:
This group covers the funding and administration of compulsory social security schemes operated by the government. This group covers:
- health, accident, and unemployment social insurance;
- pensions;
- programmes to address loss of income due to childbirth, temporary incapacity, widowhood, and the like.
This group does not cover:
- complementary or supplementary health insurance, see subgroup 6512;
- the provision of retirement income benefits specifically for the employees or members of a sponsor, see subgroup 6530;
- the administration of health and social services, see subgroup 8412;
- the provision of care assistance services, see division 87;
- the provision of welfare and social work services (without accommodation), see subgroups 8810, 8890.

Kelompok ini mencakup penerimaan deposit:
This group covers the acceptance of deposits and/or other forms similar to savings, and the granting of credit or other forms of lending of funds not elsewhere classified. Credit assistance may take various forms, such as mortgage loans and consumer credit cards. These activities are generally carried out by financial institutions other than the central bank, such as financial intermediation services not elsewhere classified, for example postal giro and postal savings operations, specialized deposit-taking institutions authorized to grant credit such as for home purchases, and money-order activities.
This activity does not cover:
- deposit-taking and credit-granting activities by cooperatives on a conventional basis, see group 64191;
- deposit-taking and credit-granting activities by cooperatives based on sharia principles, see group 64192;
- microfinancing activities by non-banking institutions, see group 64193;
- specialized non-deposit-taking institutions that grant credit such as for home purchases (see class 649);
- credit card transaction processing and settlement activities (see 6619).

Kelompok ini mencakup pengawasan dan pen:
This group covers the supervision and management of other units of a company or group of companies, for example acting as a head office; undertaking the strategic or organisational planning and decision-making of the rules of the company or enterprise; exercising operational control and managing the day-to-day operations of related units.
These activities remain the same regardless of the activity carried out by the unit managed (financing, manufacturing, trading, etc.).
This group covers the activities of
- central administrative offices;
- corporate offices (incorporated offices);
- district offices and regional offices;
- branch management offices.
This subclass does not cover
- the activities of holding companies that are not related to head-office activities, see subclass 6421.

Kelompok ini mencakup pengoperasian kere:
This group covers the operation of railways using dedicated tracks for tourism that form part of intra-city transport, such as cable cars in tourist areas.
This group does not cover:
- long-distance (intercity) tourist rail transport for passengers, see group 49111;
- the operation of cable cars, gondolas, and other railways that are not part of intra-city transport, or that are not combined with the operation of amusement and recreation venues, see group 49291;
- the operation of cable cars, gondolas, chairlifts, and other railways as part of the operation of amusement and recreation venues, see subclass 9329.

Kelompok ini mencakup pengoperasian peny:
This group covers the operation of storage for goods requiring refrigeration over a specified preservation period on a fee or contract basis, before such goods are shipped to their final destination.
This group also covers:
- the operation of cold storage in bonded zones;
- the operation of blast-freezing warehouses;
- the operation of facilities for storing physical commodities by freezing or refrigeration.
This group does not cover:
- the operation of cold storage under a warehouse receipt system, see group 52101;
- the operation of cold storage for the storage of petroleum and natural gas, see group 52104;
- the operation of cold storage for the storage of hazardous and toxic goods, see group 52105;
- the operation of cold storage for the storage of ionizing radiation sources, see group 52106;
- the operation of cold storage for the storage of radioactive associated minerals, see group 52107.

Kelompok ini mencakup pengoperasian tran:
This group covers the operation of other land passenger transport, other than intercity and intra-city transport, not elsewhere classified.
This group does not cover:
- the operation of transport on routes from a city to an airport or from a city to a station, see group 49212;
- tourist transport, see group 49292;
- charter, excursion, and other scheduled bus transport, see group 49295;
- shuttle transport, employee transport, residential transport, and intermodal feeder transport, see group 49294.

Kelompok ini mencakup pengorganisasian,:
This group covers the organisation, promotion, and/or management of events, such as
- business and trade fairs;
- corporate events;
- general or specialised exhibitions;
- conferences and conventions;
- seminars, symposia, and workshops;
- agricultural markets and craft fairs;
- rural festivals.
Such activities may be part of a series of meetings, incentive travel, conferences, and exhibitions (MICE) activities. This group may also cover the management and provision of staff to operate the facilities where such events take place, but only if such management and staffing is carried out in connection with the organisation, promotion, and/or management of those events.
This group also covers
- the technical planning, provision, installation, and operation of audiovisual equipment and special effects relating to the staging of conferences, conventions, and trade fairs.
This group does not cover
- the construction of exhibition stands/booths depending on the type of installation carried out, see division 43;
- the staging of cultural events, such as film festivals, music festivals, or dance festivals, see subclass 9039;
- the staging of sporting events, see subclass 9319;
- the staging of private ceremonies or celebrations, including weddings, naming ceremonies, birthday parties, etc., see subclass 9690;
- the technical planning, provision, installation, and operation of audiovisual equipment and special effects relating to the staging of live arts events, subclass 9039;
- the technical planning, provision, installation, and operation of audiovisual equipment and special effects relating to the staging of live sporting events, see subclass 9319;
- the technical planning, provision, installation, and operation of audiovisual equipment and special effects relating to the staging of live entertainment and recreation events, see subclass 9329.

Kelompok ini mencakup penyediaan akomoda:
This group covers the provision of other short-term accommodation not already included in groups 55201 through 55204.
This group covers accommodation such as:
- bungalows;
- cottages without daily housekeeping service;
- mountain lodges;
- hostels;
- bed and breakfast units;
- mountain huts;
- capsule hotels;
- treehouses;
- cabins;
- glamping.
This group does not cover:
- accommodation services in daily or weekly hotels, see subclass 5510;
- intermediation service activities for accommodation, see subclass 5540.

This group covers the provision of accommodation for temporary periods, with or without meals, in private or shared rooms, or dormitories, for students, seasonal workers, and other individuals.
This group covers accommodation in:
- workers' dormitories;
- boarding houses;
- student accommodation provided for less than one year;
- the operation of railway sleeping cars not operated by a railway company;
- communal living (co-living).
This group does not cover:
- the operation of railway sleeping cars as an activity integrated with a railway company, see subclass 4911;
- the operation of cruise ships, see subclasses 5011 and 5021;
- intermediation service activities for accommodation, see subclass 5540;
- all types of accommodation for a period of one year or more, see subclass 6811;
- activities combining accommodation, travel, and food, such as travel agencies and tour operators, see subclasses 7911, 7912.

Kelompok ini mencakup penyediaan berbaga:
This group covers the provision of various personal household service activities such as cooking, washing, cleaning, and ironing, in the household.
The group also covers
- astrology and spiritualist activities;
- social activities such as escort services, dating services and other speed-networking activities, marriage bureau services;
- genealogical or lineage organizations;
- pet care services such as boarding, grooming, sitting, and training of pets; horse whispering activities;
- the operation of animal shelters for stray animals;
- the activities of shoeshiners, porters, valet parking attendants, etc.;
- the operation of coin-operated personal service machine concessions (photo booths, weighing machines, blood-pressure-checking machines, coin-operated lockers, etc.);
- the operation of photo booths and photo-printing machines for printing photos from electronic records, for example from telephones, memory cards, and flash drives;
- the activities of tattoo artists who use biological substances, such as henna, for temporary decoration;
- house-sitting activities;
- the activities of private event organizers (except funerals), such as wedding planners, organizers of birthday parties, bachelor and bachelorette parties, and annual celebrations.
This group does not cover
- veterinary activities, see subclass 7500;
- house-cleaning activities, see subclass 8121;
- yoga lessons, see subclass 8551;
- the provision of alternative therapy services, the activities of healers, hypnotists, and practitioners in the fields of shiatsu, Thai massage, watsu, tuina qigong, see subclass 8699;
- in-home care services for the elderly, including in-home care services, see subclass 8810;
- child day-care services for children under three years of age provided by childminders either in their own homes or in the children's homes, after-school care services, see subclass 8890;
- coin-operated gambling machines, see subclass 9200;
- coin-operated washing machines, see subclass 9610.

Kelompok ini mencakup penyediaan gabunga:
This group covers the provision of combined support services within a client's facilities, such as general interior cleaning, maintenance, waste disposal, doorkeeping, surveillance services, mail delivery, reception, laundry, and related services to support operations within the client's facilities. These service-provision activities are carried out by operational staff who are not involved in or responsible for the client's business or principal activity.
This group does not cover:
- the provision of only a single support service (such as general cleaning services), see the subclass corresponding to the service provided;
- the provision of management and operational staff to run the entire activities of a client's enterprise, such as a hotel, restaurant, mine, or hospital, see the subclass in which those activities are covered;
- the provision of management and operation of a client's computer systems and/or data-processing facilities, see subclass 6220;
- real estate management, for example the management of real estate property or jointly-owned residences, see subclass 6829;
- guarding and security services, see subclass 8011;
- the operation of correctional or prison facilities on a fee or contract basis, see subclass 8423.

Kelompok ini mencakup penyediaan jasa an:
This group covers the provision of meteorological analysis services on the atmosphere and the prediction of weather processes and conditions, comprising:
- weather forecasting activities;
- weather modification services using aircraft, unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs)/small unmanned aircraft systems, weather balloons, and other flying platforms;
- weather modification services using generators and other ground-based weather modification platforms.
This group does not cover:
- research and development in the field of meteorology, see subclass 7210.

Kelompok ini mencakup penyediaan jasa be:
This group covers the provision of residential-based services managed by Social Welfare Institutions (LKS) in providing supervision and counseling, as well as services for persons with mental disabilities, persons with intellectual disabilities, or victims of the abuse of narcotics, psychotropics, and other addictive substances, regardless of age.
This group covers:
- the activities of treatment facilities for victims of illegal drug abuse;
- the activities of recovery homes for persons with mental and intellectual disabilities and victims of illegal drug abuse;
- the activities of group homes;
- the activities of health halfway houses for persons with mental disabilities;
- the activities of assisted living for persons with intellectual disabilities.

This group covers the provision of government-managed residential-based services providing supervision and counseling, as well as care for persons with mental disabilities, persons with intellectual disabilities, or victims of the abuse of narcotics, psychotropics, and other addictive substances, regardless of age.
This group covers:
- the activities of treatment facilities for victims of illegal drug abuse;
- the activities of recovery homes for persons with mental and intellectual disabilities and victims of illegal drug abuse;
- the activities of group homes;
- the activities of halfway houses for persons with mental disabilities;
- the activities of assisted-living accommodation for persons with intellectual disabilities.

Kelompok ini mencakup penyediaan jasa no:
This group covers the provision of non-teaching services that support educational processes or systems:
- educational consultancy;
- vocational and career counseling;
- educational guidance counseling;
- educational evaluation and testing;
- educational testing;
- the administration of student exchange programs;
- curriculum development;
- expert and rehabilitation activities that assess learning abilities.

Kelompok ini mencakup penyediaan jasa so:
This group covers the provision of social, counseling, welfare, refugee, referral, and similar services provided to individuals and families at home or elsewhere, carried out by the government.
This group covers:
- welfare and guidance services for children and adolescents;
- adoption activities and the prevention of child delinquency;
- household financial counseling, marriage and family guidance services, and debt-counseling services;
- psychosocial counseling services;
- community and neighborhood activities;
- activities for disaster victims, refugees, immigrants, and others, including temporary or long-term shelters;
- rehabilitation activities for the unemployed, where the educational component is limited;
- the determination of eligibility in connection with social assistance;
- daycare for children, including for children with disabilities;
- daytime facilities for the homeless and other lower-income social groups;

This group covers the provision of social, counseling, welfare, refugee, referral, and similar services provided to individuals and families at home or elsewhere, carried out by Social Welfare Institutions (LKS).
This group covers:
- welfare and guidance services for children and adolescents;
- adoption activities and the prevention of child delinquency;
- household financial counseling, marriage and family guidance services, and debt-counseling services;
- community and neighborhood activities;
- activities for disaster victims, refugees, immigrants, and others, including temporary or long-term shelters;
- rehabilitation activities for the unemployed, with a limited educational component;
- the determination of eligibility in connection with social assistance;
- daycare for children, including for children with disabilities;
- daytime facilities for the homeless and other lower-income social groups.

Kelompok ini mencakup penyediaan satu at:
This group covers the provision of one or more of the following services: security system services as part of a security service center or alarm receiving center (ARC); remote monitoring and video surveillance system services; and the installation, repair, and maintenance of electronic security systems, only where such activities are provided in connection with subsequent monitoring and remote monitoring services.
This group also covers:
- security consultancy activities;
- the activities of call centers and emergency services or alarm receiving centers (ARC);
- the monitoring and remote monitoring of electronic security systems, such as anti-theft alarms, video surveillance systems, and fire alarms;
- the monitoring and remote monitoring of mechanical or electronic locking devices, safes, and vaults;
- the installation and maintenance of electronic security systems, such as anti-theft alarms, video surveillance systems, and fire alarms, where provided in connection with subsequent monitoring and remote monitoring services;
- the installation, repair, modification, and adaptation of mechanical or electronic locking devices, electronic security systems, safes, and vaults, where provided in connection with subsequent monitoring and remote monitoring services.
This group does not cover:
- the installation of security systems, e.g. anti-theft, surveillance, and fire alarm systems, without monitoring and remote monitoring services, see subclass 4321;
- the retail sale of electronic security alarm systems, mechanical or electronic locking devices, safes, and secure storage rooms, without monitoring, installation, or maintenance services, see subclass 4759;
- public order and safety activities, e.g. policing, see subclass 8423;
- the provision of key duplication services, see subclass 9529;
- cybersecurity consultancy activities, see subclass 6220.

Kelompok ini mencakup penyelenggaraan pe:
This group covers the provision of training in sports activities for groups of individuals, such as in camps or schools. This group also covers both day and overnight sports training camps. Training may be provided in various settings, such as the provider's or client's own training facilities, educational institutions, or by other means including the internet. This training offers a directed educational structure, such as a learner-instructor relationship, designed specifically for education and learning. However, this training does not result in qualifications at education levels from preschool through tertiary.
This group covers sports training (baseball, basketball, cricket, football and others); sports training organised by camps or schools; gymnastics training; horse-riding training; swimming training; rock-climbing training; surfing training; activities carried out by professional sports instructors, teachers, coaches, or assistant coaches; martial arts training, card game training (such as bridge), board game courses, yoga training, electronic sports (esports) training.
This group does not cover
- activities organised by colleges, higher education institutions, and universities, see subclass 8540;
- cultural education, see subclass 8552;
- sports training by sports clubs, see subclass 9312;
- fitness training organised by fitness centres, yoga studios, and similar facilities, see subclass 9311.

This group covers the provision of training in the fields of art, drama, and music carried out by schools, studios, classes, and the like. These activities provide a structured form of learning, including interaction between participants and instructors, designed specifically to support the training process. Such training is primarily intended for hobby, recreation, or self-development, and does not lead to a qualification at any educational level from primary through tertiary.
This group covers
- music training;
- art training;
- dance training;
- training in drama, fine arts, performing arts, and photography.
This group does not cover
- educational activities organized by schools of drama, fine arts, performing arts, and photography that lead to a qualification at the secondary through tertiary educational level, see groups 853, 854;
- foreign-language training, see subclass 8559;
- cultural and intercultural mediation activities aimed at preventing psychosocial distress in adults experiencing difficulties in social and labour-market integration; eliminating social marginalization of children and adolescents; rehabilitating adults and children in prison, on probation, as well as after release from prison; and restoring isolated or withdrawn adults so that they become active again in social life, see subclass 8890;
- cultural development and coordination, see subclass 9039.

Kelompok ini mencakup penyiapan lahan un:
This group covers the preparation of land for subsequent construction activities.
This group covers:
- clearing and grading of construction sites, clearing of brush and undergrowth;
- land clearing/soil stabilization, such as excavation, slope forming, earth-filling, levelling of construction sites, digging of trenches, removal, breaking, or blasting of rock;
- execution of earthworks and/or rocky-soil works, excavation, slope forming, levelling of ground by cut and fill for the construction of roads (major, intermediate, and minor), expressways, railway lines, and airfield pavements (runways, taxiways, and aprons), factories, power plants, transmission lines, substations, and electricity distribution, production facilities, as well as buildings and other civil engineering structures;
- installation, relocation, and protection of utilities, cone-penetration (sondir) and boring tests, drilling, material extraction, and field investigation/sampling for construction, geophysical, geological, or similar purposes;
- site preparation for mining, such as the stripping of overburden as well as the development and preparation of mineral areas and mining sites, except oil and gas mining sites;
- preparation of drainage for construction sites;
- drainage of agricultural or forestry land;
- site preparation for nuclear-energy facilities;
- supporting activities for land preparation such as the installation of construction auxiliary facilities (installation of sheet piles, project signboards, and culverts for cable installation, construction of project offices, base camps, site supervision offices, warehouses, project workshops), re-surveying, construction/diversion of temporary roads, dewatering/drainage, mobilization and demobilization, and other similar works.
This group does not cover:
- the drilling of oil or gas production wells, see subclasses 0610, 0620;
- test drilling and the drilling of test holes for mining operations (other than oil and gas mining), see subclass 0990;
- soil decontamination, see subclass 3900;
- the drilling of water wells, see subclass 4220;
- shaft sinking, see subclass 4390;
- exploration studies of oil fields from geophysical, geological, and seismic aspects, see subclass 7110.

Kelompok ini mencakup perdagangan besar:
This group covers the wholesale of photographic equipment and optical goods, such as eyeglasses, binoculars, and magnifying glasses.
This group does not cover:
- the wholesale of blank audio tapes and video tapes, see subclass 4652;
- the wholesale of radio and TV broadcasting equipment, see subclass 4652;
- the wholesale of office furniture, see subclass 4659.

This group covers the wholesale of fossil fuels and low-carbon or carbon-free fuels, greases, lubricants, and oils.
This group also covers:
- the wholesale of crude petroleum, crude oil, diesel fuel, gasoline, fuel oil, kerosene, and diesel;
- the wholesale of biofuels, recycled-carbon fuels, and synthetic fuels, whether blended or pure;
- the wholesale of charcoal, coal, coke, firewood, wood or biomass pellets, and naphtha;
- the wholesale of liquefied petroleum gas (LPG), liquefied natural gas (LNG), butane and propane gas, as well as related bio or renewable forms, whether blended or pure;
- the wholesale of nuclear fuels.
This group does not cover the wholesale of hydrogen, see group 46751.

This group covers the wholesale trade of industrial machinery and office machinery except computers, and their accessories:
- wholesale trade of industrial machinery, such as wood- and metal-processing machinery; production-processing robots; additive manufacturing machines (three-dimensional printers and others); computer-controlled industrial machinery (textile-industry machinery, sewing machines, knitting machines, and others);
- wholesale trade of office machinery and equipment, except computers and computer peripherals, such as cash registers, calculators, photocopiers not connected to a computer or network, paper shredders, and automated teller machines (ATMs).

This group covers the wholesale trade of agricultural and forestry machinery, equipment and supplies.
This group covers
- wholesale trade of ploughs, fertiliser spreaders, seed planters;
- wholesale trade of harvesting equipment;
- wholesale trade of threshing equipment;
- wholesale trade of milking machines;
- wholesale trade of poultry-keeping machines and beekeeping machines;
- wholesale trade of tractors used in agriculture and forestry;
- wholesale trade of lawn mowers.
This group does not cover
- wholesale trade of fertilisers and agrochemical products, see subclass 4679;
- wholesale trade of animal feed, see subclass 4620.

This group covers the wholesale trade of other products not included in any of the wholesale groups above, such as:
- wholesale trade of textile fibres;
- wholesale trade of precious stones (diamonds, sapphires, and others);
- wholesale trade of e-liquids for electronic cigarettes;
- wholesale trade of wooden packaging (in the form of boxes, crates, drums, and others); wooden cable reels; pallets and other wooden load boards.

Kelompok ini mencakup perdagangan eceran:
